;s:13:\"dr-dhruva-h-m\";s:5:\"photo\";s:49:\"doctors/32270292-df4f-4c4b-aa32-10725e150030.webp\";s:13:\"qualification\";s:15:\"MBBS,MS,DNB,MCh\";s:11:\"designation\";s:20:\"Consultant Urologist\";s:10:\"kmc_number\";s:6:\"117557\";s:8:\"location\";s:4:\"Both\";s:16:\"experience_years\";i:10;s:5:\"about\";s:395:\"Dr. Dhruva H M is a Urologist in Uttarahalli, Bangalore and has an experience of 9 years in this field. Dr. Dhruva H M practices at Nano Hospital in Uttarahalli, Bangalore. He completed MBBS from Kempegowda institution of medical college in 2017,MS - General Surgery from kempegowda institution of medical science in 2021 and MCh - Urology from SHRI B M patel medical college vijayapura in 2025.\";s:13:\"speciality_id\";i:8;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-12 15:23:25\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-12 15:25:17\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:1:{s:10:\"speciality\";O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:4:\"name\";s:8:\"Urology \";s:4:\"slug\";s:7:\"urology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/b8e58dfa-a18a-4a39-ab22-65895a9194f1.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8AFVQM21H9TWPK3ZVNB5Z.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:522:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a leading urology hospital in Bangalore providing expert diagnosis and treatment for all urinary tract disorders in men and women, including kidney stones, prostate enlargement, urinary tract infections, bladder conditions, and male reproductive health problems. Our experienced urologists in Bangalore manage conditions affecting the kidneys, ureters, bladder, urethra, and prostate — using advanced endoscopic and minimally invasive surgical techniques for faster recovery and better outcomes.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:901:\"<p>Urological problems often begin with subtle symptoms — frequent urination, burning sensation, blood in urine, lower abdominal discomfort, or weak urinary flow — but can progress to kidney damage, urinary obstruction, or serious infection if left untreated. As a dedicated urology treatment centre in Bangalore, Nano Hospitals focuses on early detection, precise diagnosis, and timely intervention to protect kidney function and restore normal urinary health.</p><p>Every urology patient at Nano Hospitals receives a personalised treatment plan based on age, medical history, lifestyle, and condition severity — supported by advanced imaging, laser stone treatment, and structured post-treatment follow-up care. Patients across Bangalore trust Nano Hospitals for urology care because of the compassionate, patient-first approach at every stage — from first consultation to full recovery.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:516:\"<p>Urology focuses on diagnosing and managing disorders of the urinary system and male reproductive organs. Early signs such as painful urination, blood in urine, urinary leakage, or flank pain should not be ignored, as they may indicate infection, stones, prostate enlargement, or more serious conditions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early detection, accurate imaging and laboratory evaluation, minimally invasive intervention whenever possible, and long-term monitoring to protect urinary and kidney health</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1114:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical management of urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Medications for prostate enlargement and urinary symptoms</p></li><li><p>Bladder control therapy for incontinence</p></li><li><p>Dietary and lifestyle guidance for kidney stone prevention</p></li><li><p>Hormonal and medication-based management for certain male reproductive disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Cystoscopy for bladder and urethral evaluation</p></li><li><p>Ureteroscopy with laser treatment for kidney and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic prostate procedures (TURP and laser prostate surgery)</p></li><li><p>Image-guided catheter placements and stenting</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive treatment for urinary obstruction</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Kidney stone removal surgeries</p></li><li><p>Prostate surgery for severe enlargement or obstruction</p></li><li><p>Bladder tumor surgery</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive urological surgeries</p></li><li><p>Treatment of congenital urinary tract abnormalitie</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:507:\"<h2>Facilities and Technologies Used</h2><ul><li><p>Advanced Ultrasound for kidney, bladder, and prostate evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan for detailed stone and urinary tract imaging</p></li><li><p>MRI for complex urological assessments</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic urology equipment for minimally invasive procedures</p></li><li><p>Laser technology for stone and prostate treatment</p></li><li><p>Dedicated urology operation theatres</p></li><li><p>Post-operative monitoring and recovery units</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Conditions and Ailments Treated</h2><ul><li><p>Kidney stones and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Enlarged prostate (BPH)</p></li><li><p>Urinary incontinence and bladder control issues</p></li><li><p>Blood in urine (hematuria)</p></li><li><p>Bladder and kidney disorders</p></li><li><p>Male reproductive health issues</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Risks and Challenges</h2><ul><li><p>Recurrent stone formation if preventive care is not followed</p></li><li><p>Kidney damage due to untreated obstruction or infection</p></li><li><p>Urinary retention affecting bladder function</p></li><li><p>Chronic discomfort impacting daily life</p></li><li><p>Need for long-term monitoring in prostate and bladder conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:286:\"<h2>Sub-specialties in Urology</h2><ul><li><p>Endourology and Stone Management</p></li><li><p>Prostate Care and Male Urinary Disorders</p></li><li><p>Uro-Oncology (Urological Tumors)</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive Urology</p></li><li><p>Female Urology and Incontinence Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:87:\"Best Urology Hospital in Bangalore | Kidney Stone & Prostate Treatment | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:243:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted urology hospital in Bangalore offering expert treatment for kidney stones, prostate enlargement, UTIs, bladder disorders, and male reproductive health. Consult experienced urologists — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:25:57\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:17:17\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/50572282-7671-48f3-9be7-031c29c5a936.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:4:\"name\";s:8:\"Urology \";s:4:\"slug\";s:7:\"urology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/b8e58dfa-a18a-4a39-ab22-65895a9194f1.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8AFVQM21H9TWPK3ZVNB5Z.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:522:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a leading urology hospital in Bangalore providing expert diagnosis and treatment for all urinary tract disorders in men and women, including kidney stones, prostate enlargement, urinary tract infections, bladder conditions, and male reproductive health problems. Our experienced urologists in Bangalore manage conditions affecting the kidneys, ureters, bladder, urethra, and prostate — using advanced endoscopic and minimally invasive surgical techniques for faster recovery and better outcomes.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:901:\"<p>Urological problems often begin with subtle symptoms — frequent urination, burning sensation, blood in urine, lower abdominal discomfort, or weak urinary flow — but can progress to kidney damage, urinary obstruction, or serious infection if left untreated. As a dedicated urology treatment centre in Bangalore, Nano Hospitals focuses on early detection, precise diagnosis, and timely intervention to protect kidney function and restore normal urinary health.</p><p>Every urology patient at Nano Hospitals receives a personalised treatment plan based on age, medical history, lifestyle, and condition severity — supported by advanced imaging, laser stone treatment, and structured post-treatment follow-up care. Patients across Bangalore trust Nano Hospitals for urology care because of the compassionate, patient-first approach at every stage — from first consultation to full recovery.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:516:\"<p>Urology focuses on diagnosing and managing disorders of the urinary system and male reproductive organs. Early signs such as painful urination, blood in urine, urinary leakage, or flank pain should not be ignored, as they may indicate infection, stones, prostate enlargement, or more serious conditions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early detection, accurate imaging and laboratory evaluation, minimally invasive intervention whenever possible, and long-term monitoring to protect urinary and kidney health</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1114:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical management of urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Medications for prostate enlargement and urinary symptoms</p></li><li><p>Bladder control therapy for incontinence</p></li><li><p>Dietary and lifestyle guidance for kidney stone prevention</p></li><li><p>Hormonal and medication-based management for certain male reproductive disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Cystoscopy for bladder and urethral evaluation</p></li><li><p>Ureteroscopy with laser treatment for kidney and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic prostate procedures (TURP and laser prostate surgery)</p></li><li><p>Image-guided catheter placements and stenting</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive treatment for urinary obstruction</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Kidney stone removal surgeries</p></li><li><p>Prostate surgery for severe enlargement or obstruction</p></li><li><p>Bladder tumor surgery</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive urological surgeries</p></li><li><p>Treatment of congenital urinary tract abnormalitie</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:507:\"<h2>Facilities and Technologies Used</h2><ul><li><p>Advanced Ultrasound for kidney, bladder, and prostate evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan for detailed stone and urinary tract imaging</p></li><li><p>MRI for complex urological assessments</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic urology equipment for minimally invasive procedures</p></li><li><p>Laser technology for stone and prostate treatment</p></li><li><p>Dedicated urology operation theatres</p></li><li><p>Post-operative monitoring and recovery units</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Conditions and Ailments Treated</h2><ul><li><p>Kidney stones and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Enlarged prostate (BPH)</p></li><li><p>Urinary incontinence and bladder control issues</p></li><li><p>Blood in urine (hematuria)</p></li><li><p>Bladder and kidney disorders</p></li><li><p>Male reproductive health issues</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Risks and Challenges</h2><ul><li><p>Recurrent stone formation if preventive care is not followed</p></li><li><p>Kidney damage due to untreated obstruction or infection</p></li><li><p>Urinary retention affecting bladder function</p></li><li><p>Chronic discomfort impacting daily life</p></li><li><p>Need for long-term monitoring in prostate and bladder conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:286:\"<h2>Sub-specialties in Urology</h2><ul><li><p>Endourology and Stone Management</p></li><li><p>Prostate Care and Male Urinary Disorders</p></li><li><p>Uro-Oncology (Urological Tumors)</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive Urology</p></li><li><p>Female Urology and Incontinence Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:87:\"Best Urology Hospital in Bangalore | Kidney Stone & Prostate Treatment | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:243:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted urology hospital in Bangalore offering expert treatment for kidney stones, prostate enlargement, UTIs, bladder disorders, and male reproductive health. Consult experienced urologists — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:25:57\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:17:17\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/50572282-7671-48f3-9be7-031c29c5a936.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11