:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:12:{i:0;s:2:\"h1\";i:1;s:5:\"title\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:7:\"excerpt\";i:4;s:14:\"featured_image\";i:5;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:6;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:7;s:13:\"meta_keywords\";i:8;s:14:\"content_blocks\";i:9;s:4:\"faqs\";i:10;s:12:\"is_published\";i:11;s:12:\"published_at\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}}}s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;}}',1785304581),('laravel-cache-content:v1:procedure:hip-replacement-surgery','O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:5:\"title\";s:24:\"Hip Replacement Surgery \";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/0d44d9ee-4961-4ee6-b9ec-d8a0de35764d.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:23:\"hip-replacement-surgery\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:742:\"<p>Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from severe hip pain, arthritis, and reduced joint mobility. As a best hospital in Bangalore for orthopedic care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced hip replacement procedures using modern surgical techniques and high-quality implants to restore movement and improve quality of life. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help reduce pain, enhance mobility, and prevent further joint deterioration.</p><p>This article explains hip replacement comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:293:\"<p>The hip is a ball-and-socket joint. In arthritis, the cartilage cushioning the joint wears away, causing bones to rub together. This leads to pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility. Hip replacement replaces the damaged joint with artificial components made of metal, ceramic, or plastic.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:2:\"[]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:2:\"[]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:7:\"<p></p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:509:\"[{\"name\": \"Total Hip Replacement (THR)\", \"description\": \"Both the femoral head (ball) and acetabulum (socket) are replaced.\\n\\nDamaged cartilage and bone are removed.\\n\\nArtificial components made of metal, ceramic, or polyethylene are implanted.\\nRecommended for severe arthritis or advanced joint damage.\"}, {\"name\": \"Partial Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"Only the femoral head is replaced.\\n\\nThe natural socket (acetabulum) is preserved.\\n\\nCommonly performed for hip fractures in elderly patients.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:2:\"[]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:226:\"<p>Hip replacement is highly successful — over <strong>90% of patients experience significant pain relief and improved mobility</strong>. Modern implants last 15–20 years, and many patients return to active lifestyles.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:325:\"<p>Hip replacement surgery transforms lives by relieving pain and restoring independence. With proper patient selection, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation, outcomes are excellent. Patients can look forward to walking comfortably, climbing stairs, and enjoying daily activities without the burden of chronic hip pain.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:64:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:153:\"Looking for the best and top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced hip replacement procedures with expert orthopedic care.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";N;s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-18 17:32:00\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-15 18:32:20\";s:2:\"h1\";s:47:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:5:\"title\";s:24:\"Hip Replacement Surgery \";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/0d44d9ee-4961-4ee6-b9ec-d8a0de35764d.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:23:\"hip-replacement-surgery\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:742:\"<p>Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from severe hip pain, arthritis, and reduced joint mobility. As a best hospital in Bangalore for orthopedic care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced hip replacement procedures using modern surgical techniques and high-quality implants to restore movement and improve quality of life. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help reduce pain, enhance mobility, and prevent further joint deterioration.</p><p>This article explains hip replacement comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:293:\"<p>The hip is a ball-and-socket joint. In arthritis, the cartilage cushioning the joint wears away, causing bones to rub together. This leads to pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility. Hip replacement replaces the damaged joint with artificial components made of metal, ceramic, or plastic.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:2:\"[]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:2:\"[]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:7:\"<p></p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:509:\"[{\"name\": \"Total Hip Replacement (THR)\", \"description\": \"Both the femoral head (ball) and acetabulum (socket) are replaced.\\n\\nDamaged cartilage and bone are removed.\\n\\nArtificial components made of metal, ceramic, or polyethylene are implanted.\\nRecommended for severe arthritis or advanced joint damage.\"}, {\"name\": \"Partial Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"Only the femoral head is replaced.\\n\\nThe natural socket (acetabulum) is preserved.\\n\\nCommonly performed for hip fractures in elderly patients.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:2:\"[]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:226:\"<p>Hip replacement is highly successful — over <strong>90% of patients experience significant pain relief and improved mobility</strong>. Modern implants last 15–20 years, and many patients return to active lifestyles.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:325:\"<p>Hip replacement surgery transforms lives by relieving pain and restoring independence. With proper patient selection, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation, outcomes are excellent. Patients can look forward to walking comfortably, climbing stairs, and enjoying daily activities without the burden of chronic hip pain.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:64:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:153:\"Looking for the best and top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced hip replacement procedures with expert orthopedic care.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";N;s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-18 17:32:00\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-15 18:32:20\";s:2:\"h1\";s:47:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:1:{s:4:\"faqs\";O:39:\"Illuminate\\Database\\Eloquent\\Collection\":2:{s:8:\"\0*\0items\";a:0:{}s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;}}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}',1785307313),('laravel-cache-content:v1:specialities:active','O:39:\"Illuminate\\Database\\Eloquent\\Collection\":2:{s:8:\"\0*\0items\";a:26:{i:0;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:5;s:4:\"name\";s:22:\"Cardiology(heart care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:10:\"heart-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/d4b79b00-5783-4b32-b927-54cde29747bd.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8CGZ01K9DDBXQ95FXYXRV.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:569:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a trusted cardiology and heart care hospital in Bangalore, offering specialised services for the prevention, early detection, and treatment of all heart-related conditions. Heart disease — including coronary artery disease, hypertension, heart failure, and arrhythmia — often develops silently before warning signs like chest pain, breathlessness, palpitations, or fatigue appear. Our experienced cardiologists in Bangalore ensure cardiac risk is identified and treated at the earliest stage, before it becomes a life-threatening emergency.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:937:\"<p>The cardiology department at Nano Hospitals Bangalore is equipped with advanced diagnostics including ECG, 2D Echocardiography, and cardiac risk profiling for patients with diabetes, high blood pressure, obesity, or a family history of heart disease. Each patient receives a personalised, evidence-based heart treatment plan tailored to their age, lifestyle, and condition — with the department working in close coordination with Emergency, ICU, and General Medicine teams for seamless, round-the-clock cardiac care.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, heart care goes beyond symptom relief — the focus is on long-term cardiovascular health and disease prevention. Whether you need a cardiac health check-up in Bangalore, treatment for hypertension, or ongoing management of a diagnosed heart condition, our cardiologists provide clear, personalised guidance at every step — from first consultation to long-term follow-up and recovery.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:345:\"<p>Heart Care focuses on identifying and managing cardiovascular risks early, before complications arise. Timely cardiac evaluation plays a crucial role in preventing life-threatening events.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, cardiology services are integrated with emergency and critical care systems to ensure rapid response and continuity of care.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:888:\"<h3><strong>Cardiac Diagnostic Services</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Electrocardiogram (ECG) for rhythm assessment</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography for heart structure and function</p></li><li><p>Cardiac risk profiling and clinical evaluation</p></li><li><p>Monitoring of heart function in medical and surgical patients</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Medical Management</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Hypertension management</p></li><li><p>Heart failure medical treatment</p></li><li><p>Arrhythmia management</p></li><li><p>Medical treatment for coronary artery disease</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Preventive &amp; Emergency Cardiac Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Cardiac risk assessment and lifestyle counselling</p></li><li><p>Monitoring high-risk patients (diabetes, obesity, family history)</p></li><li><p>Immediate evaluation of chest pain</p></li><li><p>Cardiac monitoring in ICU and wards</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:370:\"<ul><li><p>ECG machines for rapid rhythm assessment</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography systems</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory medicine for cardiac markers</p></li><li><p>ICU and emergency services for continuous monitoring</p></li><li><p>Digital X-Ray, CT, and MRI support when required</p></li><li><p>24×7 pharmacy for uninterrupted medication access</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:349:\"<ul><li><p>Hypertension and coronary artery disease</p></li><li><p>Heart rhythm disorders and heart failure</p></li><li><p>Chest pain, breathlessness, palpitations</p></li><li><p>Dizziness or fainting episodes</p></li><li><p>Cardiac involvement in diabetes and kidney disease</p></li><li><p>Pre-operative cardiac assessment for surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:223:\"<ul><li><p>Early detection over late intervention</p></li><li><p>Evidence-based medical management</p></li><li><p>Patient education and lifestyle modification</p></li><li><p>Continuous monitoring and follow-up</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:174:\"<ul><li><p>Preventive Cardiology</p></li><li><p>Heart Failure Management</p></li><li><p>Medical Cardiology</p></li><li><p>Cardiac Risk Assessment and Monitoring</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:67:\"Best Heart Care & Cardiology Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:258:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted cardiology and heart care hospital in Bangalore offering expert diagnosis and treatment for heart disease, hypertension, arrhythmia, heart failure, and chest pain. Consult experienced cardiologists — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:14:30\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:16:18\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/a7cdc4e0-1622-45f5-8253-216e12293df9.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:5;s:4:\"name\";s:22:\"Cardiology(heart care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:10:\"heart-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/d4b79b00-5783-4b32-b927-54cde29747bd.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8CGZ01K9DDBXQ95FXYXRV.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:569:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a trusted cardiology and heart care hospital in Bangalore, offering specialised services for the prevention, early detection, and treatment of all heart-related conditions. Heart disease — including coronary artery disease, hypertension, heart failure, and arrhythmia — often develops silently before warning signs like chest pain, breathlessness, palpitations, or fatigue appear. Our experienced cardiologists in Bangalore ensure cardiac risk is identified and treated at the earliest stage, before it becomes a life-threatening emergency.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:937:\"<p>The cardiology department at Nano Hospitals Bangalore is equipped with advanced diagnostics including ECG, 2D Echocardiography, and cardiac risk profiling for patient