Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:131:\"Get comprehensive diagnostic lab services in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Timely and precise testing for better treatment planning.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:18:41\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:18:15\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/c7c14599-24ae-4195-a683-a5a2b466188b.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:4;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:21;s:4:\"name\";s:25:\"Emergency & Critical Care\";s:4:\"slug\";s:23:\"emergency-critical-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/24638eed-2bd6-4892-b285-7a8481dd71cb.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/988881f7-dded-4dac-b6b4-2149ec631368.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:339:\"<p>Emergency &amp; Critical Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> provides immediate, life-saving medical attention for patients with severe illness, injury, or life-threatening conditions. This department operates круглthe clock, ensuring rapid assessment, stabilization, and advanced medical support when every second matters.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:672:\"<p>Emergencies may include chest pain, breathing difficulty, severe trauma, stroke symptoms, seizures, poisoning, or sudden loss of consciousness. Critical care services support patients whose vital organs require continuous monitoring and advanced life support. At Nano Hospitals, care is focused on rapid response, precise diagnosis, and intensive monitoring to stabilise patients and prevent complications.</p><p>Treatment is delivered by a multidisciplinary team of emergency physicians, critical care specialists, nurses, and paramedical staff trained in advanced life support. Care plans are tailored in real time according to the patient’s evolving condition.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:421:\"<p>Emergency medicine deals with urgent medical and surgical conditions requiring immediate evaluation. Critical care focuses on patients with organ failure or unstable vital signs who need continuous monitoring and advanced interventions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises rapid triage systems, evidence-based emergency protocols, and seamless transition from emergency care to intensive care or specialty departments.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:896:\"<h3>Emergency Medical Care</h3><ul><li><p>Cardiac emergency management (heart attack, arrhythmias)</p></li><li><p>Stroke stabilization and rapid response</p></li><li><p>Trauma and accident care</p></li><li><p>Poisoning and overdose treatment</p></li><li><p>Acute respiratory distress management</p></li></ul><h3>Critical Care Interventions</h3><ul><li><p>Mechanical ventilation for breathing support</p></li><li><p>Advanced cardiac life support (ACLS)</p></li><li><p>Invasive and non-invasive monitoring</p></li><li><p>Sepsis and multi-organ failure management</p></li><li><p>Dialysis support in critical kidney failure</p></li></ul><h3>Life-Saving Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Intubation and airway management</p></li><li><p>Central line and arterial line placement</p></li><li><p>Emergency surgeries in coordination with surgical teams</p></li><li><p>Defibrillation and resuscitation</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:403:\"<ul><li><p>24/7 fully equipped Emergency Department</p></li><li><p>Advanced cardiac monitors and ventilators</p></li><li><p>Point-of-care laboratory testing</p></li><li><p>Portable ultrasound and bedside imaging</p></li><li><p>Dedicated Intensive Care Units (ICUs)</p></li><li><p>High-dependency units (HDU) for step-down care</p></li><li><p>Infection-controlled critical care environments</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:389:\"<ul><li><p>Heart attacks and cardiac arrest</p></li><li><p>Stroke and sudden neurological emergencies</p></li><li><p>Severe infections and sepsis</p></li><li><p>Major trauma and road traffic injuries</p></li><li><p>Acute respiratory failure</p></li><li><p>Poisoning and drug overdose</p></li><li><p>Severe allergic reactions (anaphylaxis)</p></li><li><p>Uncontrolled bleeding</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:307:\"<ul><li><p>Rapid deterioration without immediate treatment</p></li><li><p>Multi-organ failure in severe illness</p></li><li><p>Need for prolonged intensive monitoring</p></li><li><p>High emotional stress for patients and families</p></li><li><p>Risk of complications in critically ill patients</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:226:\"<ul><li><p>Trauma and Emergency Surgery Support</p></li><li><p>Cardiac Critical Care</p></li><li><p>Neurocritical Care</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Critical Care</p></li><li><p>Respiratory and Pulmonary Critical Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:53:\"24/7 Emergency Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:134:\"Nano Hospitals provides 24-hour emergency care in Bangalore with ICU support, trauma care, and quick response for critical conditions.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:07:30\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-07 14:52:41\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/52f60a9f-1d7e-4ca2-b1ca-982d89d2fdad.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:21;s:4:\"name\";s:25:\"Emergency & Critical Care\";s:4:\"slug\";s:23:\"emergency-critical-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/24638eed-2bd6-4892-b285-7a8481dd71cb.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/988881f7-dded-4dac-b6b4-2149ec631368.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:339:\"<p>Emergency &amp; Critical Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> provides immediate, life-saving medical attention for patients with severe illness, injury, or life-threatening conditions. This department operates круглthe clock, ensuring rapid assessment, stabilization, and advanced medical support when every second matters.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:672:\"<p>Emergencies may include chest pain, breathing difficulty, severe trauma, stroke symptoms, seizures, poisoning, or sudden loss of consciousness. Critical care services support patients whose vital organs require continuous monitoring and advanced life support. At Nano Hospitals, care is focused on rapid response, precise diagnosis, and intensive monitoring to stabilise patients and prevent complications.</p><p>Treatment is delivered by a multidisciplinary team of emergency physicians, critical care specialists, nurses, and paramedical staff trained in advanced life support. Care plans are tailored in real time according to the patient’s evolving condition.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:421:\"<p>Emergency medicine deals with urgent medical and surgical conditions requiring immediate evaluation. Critical care focuses on patients with organ failure or unstable vital signs who need continuous monitoring and advanced interventions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises rapid triage systems, evidence-based emergency protocols, and seamless transition from emergency care to intensive care or specialty departments.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:896:\"<h3>Emergency Medical Care</h3><ul><li><p>Cardiac emergency management (heart attack, arrhythmias)</p></li><li><p>Stroke stabilization and rapid response</p></li><li><p>Trauma and accident care</p></li><li><p>Poisoning and overdose treatment</p></li><li><p>Acute respiratory distress management</p></li></ul><h3>Critical Care Interventions</h3><ul><li><p>Mechanical ventilation for breathing support</p></li><li><p>Advanced cardiac life support (ACLS)</p></li><li><p>Invasive and non-invasive monitoring</p></li><li><p>Sepsis and multi-organ failure management</p></li><li><p>Dialysis support in critical kidney failure</p></li></ul><h3>Life-Saving Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Intubation and airway management</p></li><li><p>Central line and arterial line placement</p></li><li><p>Emergency surgeries in coordination with surgical teams</p></li><li><p>Defibrillation and resuscitation</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:403:\"<ul><li><p>24/7 fully equipped Emergency Department</p></li><li><p>Advanced cardiac monitors and ventilators</p></li><li><p>Point-of-care laboratory testing</p></li><li><p>Portable ultrasound and bedside imaging</p></li><li><p>Dedicated Intensive Care Units (ICUs)</p></li><li><p>High-dependency units (HDU) for step-down care</p></li><li><p>Infection-controlled critical care environments</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:389:\"<ul><li><p>Heart attacks and cardiac arrest</p></li><li><p>Stroke and sudden neurological emergencies</p></li><li><p>Severe infections and sepsis</p></li><li><p>Major trauma and road traffic injuries</p></li><li><p>Acute respiratory failure</p></li><li><p>Poisoning and drug overdose</p></li><li><p>Severe allergic reactions (anaphylaxis)</p></li><li><p>Uncontrolled bleeding</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:307:\"<ul><li><p>Rapid deterioration without immediate treatment</p></li><li><p>Multi-organ failure in severe illness</p></li><li><p>Need for prolonged intensive monitoring</p></li><li><p>High emotional stress for patients and families</p></li><li><p>Risk of complications in critically ill patients</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:226:\"<ul><li><p>Trauma and Emergency Surgery Support</p></li><li><p>Cardiac Critical Care</p></li><li><p>Neurocritical Care</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Critical Care</p></li><li><p>Respiratory and Pulmonary Critical Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:53:\"24/7 Emergency Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:134:\"Nano Hospitals provides 24-hour emergency care in Bangalore with ICU support, trauma care, and quick response for critical conditions.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:07:30\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-07 14:52:41\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/52f60a9f-1d7e-4ca2-b1ca-982d89d2fdad.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:5;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:15;s:4:\"name\";s:24:\"ENT (Ear, Nose & Throat)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:19:\"ent-ear-nose-throat\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/81e37695-8ad3-421b-820b-a3803c1c26a6.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/584ecd7e-f9da-4310-b634-97d42b2226a1.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:216:\"<p>ENT Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of disorders affecting the ear, nose, throat, sinuses, voice box, and related head and neck structures.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:691:\"<p>ENT problems often begin with common symptoms such as ear pain, hearing difficulty, nasal blockage, sinus headaches, sore throat, or voice changes. While many issues are mild, persistent or recurrent symptoms can indicate infections, structural problems, allergies, or more serious conditions. At Nano Hospitals, care is directed toward relieving symptoms, restoring normal function, and preventing complications.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, endoscopic assessment, hearing tests, imaging, and when needed, medical or surgical intervention. Care plans are tailored according to age, symptom severity, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:401:\"<p>Otolaryngology (ENT) deals with conditions of hearing, balance, breathing, speech, and swallowing. Early symptoms such as persistent nasal congestion, frequent throat infections, dizziness, or hearing loss should not be ignored.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis using endoscopy, audiology testing, and imaging, followed by personalised treatment and rehabilitation when required.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:943:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical treatment for ear, sinus, and throat infections</p></li><li><p>Allergy management and nasal spray therapy</p></li><li><p>Hearing aid fitting and hearing rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Voice therapy for vocal strain or hoarseness</p></li><li><p>Management of vertigo and balance disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Nasal endoscopy for sinus and nasal evaluation</p></li><li><p>Ear microsuction and minor ear procedures</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic sinus procedures</p></li><li><p>Injection therapy for vocal cord disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Tonsillectomy and adenoidectomy</p></li><li><p>Functional Endoscopic Sinus Surgery (FESS)</p></li><li><p>Ear surgeries including eardrum repair</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and salivary gland surgeries</p></li><li><p>Head and neck tumor surgeries (in coordination with oncology)</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:332:\"<ul><li><p>Nasal endoscopy and laryngoscopy systems</p></li><li><p>Audiometry and hearing assessment labs</p></li><li><p>CT Scan for sinus and temporal bone imaging</p></li><li><p>Microscopic ear surgery equipment</p></li><li><p>Voice analysis and speech therapy support</p></li><li><p>Dedicated ENT operation theatres</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:394:\"<ul><li><p>Sinusitis and nasal polyps</p></li><li><p>Allergic rhinitis</p></li><li><p>Hearing loss and ear infections</p></li><li><p>Tinnitus (ringing in ears)</p></li><li><p>Tonsillitis and throat infections</p></li><li><p>Voice disorders</p></li><li><p>Vertigo and balance disorders</p></li><li><p>Deviated nasal septum (DNS)</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and salivary gland conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:293:\"<ul><li><p>Chronic sinus infections affecting breathing and sleep</p></li><li><p>Progressive hearing loss if untreated</p></li><li><p>Recurrent throat infections in children</p></li><li><p>Voice strain impacting communication</p></li><li><p>Balance disorders increasing fall risk</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:219:\"<ul><li><p>Otology (Ear and Hearing Care)</p></li><li><p>Rhinology (Nose and Sinus Care)</p></li><li><p>Laryngology (Voice and Throat Care)</p></li><li><p>Head and Neck Surgery</p></li><li><p>Pediatric ENT</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:74:\"ENT Specialist in Bangalore | Ear Nose Throat Treatment – Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:160:\"Consult experienced ENT specialists in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals for sinus issues, ear infections, hearing problems, and throat conditions with advanced care.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:51:52\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:15:20\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/8b867e2e-4698-4bcf-a6c3-e53687f62a85.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:15;s:4:\"name\";s:24:\"ENT (Ear, Nose & Throat)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:19:\"ent-ear-nose-throat\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/81e37695-8ad3-421b-820b-a3803c1c26a6.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/584ecd7e-f9da-4310-b634-97d42b2226a1.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:216:\"<p>ENT Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of disorders affecting the ear, nose, throat, sinuses, voice box, and related head and neck structures.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:691:\"<p>ENT problems often begin with common symptoms such as ear pain, hearing difficulty, nasal blockage, sinus headaches, sore throat, or voice changes. While many issues are mild, persistent or recurrent symptoms can indicate infections, structural problems, allergies, or more serious conditions. At Nano Hospitals, care is directed toward relieving symptoms, restoring normal function, and preventing complications.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, endoscopic assessment, hearing tests, imaging, and when needed, medical or surgical intervention. Care plans are tailored according to age, symptom severity, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:401:\"<p>Otolaryngology (ENT) deals with conditions of hearing, balance, breathing, speech, and swallowing. Early symptoms such as persistent nasal congestion, frequent throat infections, dizziness, or hearing loss should not be ignored.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis using endoscopy, audiology testing, and imaging, followed by personalised treatment and rehabilitation when required.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:943:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical treatment for ear, sinus, and throat infections</p></li><li><p>Allergy management and nasal spray therapy</p></li><li><p>Hearing aid fitting and hearing rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Voice therapy for vocal strain or hoarseness</p></li><li><p>Management of vertigo and balance disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Nasal endoscopy for sinus and nasal evaluation</p></li><li><p>Ear microsuction and minor ear procedures</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic sinus procedures</p></li><li><p>Injection therapy for vocal cord disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Tonsillectomy and adenoidectomy</p></li><li><p>Functional Endoscopic Sinus Surgery (FESS)</p></li><li><p>Ear surgeries including eardrum repair</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and salivary gland surgeries</p></li><li><p>Head and neck tumor surgeries (in coordination with oncology)</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:332:\"<ul><li><p>Nasal endoscopy and laryngoscopy systems</p></li><li><p>Audiometry and hearing assessment labs</p></li><li><p>CT Scan for sinus and temporal bone imaging</p></li><li><p>Microscopic ear surgery equipment</p></li><li><p>Voice analysis and speech therapy support</p></li><li><p>Dedicated ENT operation theatres</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:394:\"<ul><li><p>Sinusitis and nasal polyps</p></li><li><p>Allergic rhinitis</p></li><li><p>Hearing loss and ear infections</p></li><li><p>Tinnitus (ringing in ears)</p></li><li><p>Tonsillitis and throat infections</p></li><li><p>Voice disorders</p></li><li><p>Vertigo and balance disorders</p></li><li><p>Deviated nasal septum (DNS)</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and salivary gland conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:293:\"<ul><li><p>Chronic sinus infections affecting breathing and sleep</p></li><li><p>Progressive hearing loss if untreated</p></li><li><p>Recurrent throat infections in children</p></li><li><p>Voice strain impacting communication</p></li><li><p>Balance disorders increasing fall risk</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:219:\"<ul><li><p>Otology (Ear and Hearing Care)</p></li><li><p>Rhinology (Nose and Sinus Care)</p></li><li><p>Laryngology (Voice and Throat Care)</p></li><li><p>Head and Neck Surgery</p></li><li><p>Pediatric ENT</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:74:\"ENT Specialist in Bangalore | Ear Nose Throat Treatment – Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:160:\"Consult experienced ENT specialists in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals for sinus issues, ear infections, hearing problems, and throat conditions with advanced care.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:51:52\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:15:20\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/8b867e2e-4698-4bcf-a6c3-e53687f62a85.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:6;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:9;s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"Gastroenterology\";s:4:\"slug\";s:16:\"gastroenterology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/27b1930a-0ce1-4e3f-a9c1-68aebd59524b.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/e9eaf58f-eec1-467c-9950-4c43f16d8102.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:555:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a trusted gastroenterology and digestive care hospital in Bangalore, offering expert diagnosis and treatment for all conditions affecting the oesophagus, stomach, intestines, liver, gallbladder, pancreas, and rectum. Our experienced gastroenterologist in Bangalore — with DM Gastroenterology qualification — provides evidence-based treatment for acidity, GERD, peptic ulcers, IBS, IBD, gallstones, liver disease, pancreatitis, and gastrointestinal bleeding using advanced endoscopy, imaging, and minimally invasive procedures.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:972:\"<p>Digestive problems often start as minor discomforts — persistent acidity, bloating, irregular bowel habits, or abdominal pain — but can progress to serious conditions like chronic inflammation, liver damage, ulcers, nutritional deficiencies, or GI bleeding if left untreated. As a dedicated gastroenterology treatment hospital in Bangalore, Nano Hospitals focuses on early endoscopic diagnosis, identifying root causes, and personalised treatment plans to restore digestive health and prevent recurrence.</p><p>Care at Nano Hospitals follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, high-definition endoscopy and colonoscopy, advanced liver and abdominal imaging, dietary guidance, and surgical intervention when needed. Each gastroenterology treatment plan in Bangalore is tailored to the patient&#039;s age, lifestyle, medical history, and disease severity — with structured follow-up to ensure lasting digestive health and quality of life.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:454:\"<p>Gastroenterology deals with diseases of the gastrointestinal (GI) tract and associated organs such as the liver and pancreas. Early symptoms like persistent heartburn, abdominal pain, constipation, diarrhea, or unexplained weight loss should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis through endoscopy and imaging, personalised treatment plans, and long-term dietary and lifestyle support to maintain digestive health.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1059:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical management of acidity, gastritis, and reflux</p></li><li><p>Treatment of infections such as H. pylori</p></li><li><p>Dietary planning for IBS and digestive disorders</p></li><li><p>Medication-based management of liver and pancreatic conditions</p></li><li><p>Nutritional therapy for malabsorption disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Upper GI endoscopy for stomach and esophagus evaluation</p></li><li><p>Colonoscopy for large intestine examination</p></li><li><p>ERCP for bile duct and pancreatic duct disorders</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic removal of polyps and small growths</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic control of GI bleeding</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Gallbladder removal (cholecystectomy)</p></li><li><p>Surgery for hernias affecting the digestive tract</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction surgery</p></li><li><p>Liver and pancreatic surgical procedures (when required)</p></li><li><p>Tumor removal surgeries in the digestive system</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:450:\"<ul><li><p>High-definition endoscopy and colonoscopy systems</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound for abdominal organ evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan and MRI for liver, pancreas, and intestinal imaging</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory testing for digestive disorders</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic ultrasound (EUS) for deeper tissue assessment</p></li><li><p>Dedicated GI procedure suites</p></li><li><p>Post-procedure recovery and monitoring units</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:414:\"<ul><li><p>Acid reflux (GERD) and gastritis</p></li><li><p>Peptic ulcers</p></li><li><p>Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS)</p></li><li><p>Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD)</p></li><li><p>Gallstones and bile duct disorders</p></li><li><p>Liver diseases including fatty liver and hepatitis</p></li><li><p>Pancreatitis</p></li><li><p>Constipation and chronic diarrhea</p></li><li><p>Gastrointestinal bleeding</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:351:\"<ul><li><p>Chronic inflammation leading to long-term damage</p></li><li><p>Nutritional deficiencies due to poor absorption</p></li><li><p>Risk of bleeding or obstruction in untreated conditions</p></li><li><p>Liver damage if metabolic or viral diseases are not managed</p></li><li><p>Recurrence of symptoms without lifestyle modification</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:214:\"<ul><li><p>Gastroenterology</p></li><li><p>Hepatology (Liver Care)</p></li><li><p>Pancreatic Disorders Management</p></li><li><p>Advanced Endoscopy</p></li><li><p>GI Oncology (Digestive System Tumors)</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:106:\"Best Gastroenterology Hospital in Bangalore | Digestive Care, Endoscopy & Liver Treatment | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:273:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted gastroenterology hospital in Bangalore offering expert treatment for acidity, GERD, IBS, gallstones, liver disease, pancreatitis, and digestive disorders. Experienced gastroenterologists with DM Gastroenterology — book your appointment today.\n\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:28:42\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:42:49\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/696ceeb8-be1b-4ef3-adae-fee0989cdcda.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:9;s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"Gastroenterology\";s:4:\"slug\";s:16:\"gastroenterology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/27b1930a-0ce1-4e3f-a9c1-68aebd59524b.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/e9eaf58f-eec1-467c-9950-4c43f16d8102.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:555:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a trusted gastroenterology and digestive care hospital in Bangalore, offering expert diagnosis and treatment for all conditions affecting the oesophagus, stomach, intestines, liver, gallbladder, pancreas, and rectum. Our experienced gastroenterologist in Bangalore — with DM Gastroenterology qualification — provides evidence-based treatment for acidity, GERD, peptic ulcers, IBS, IBD, gallstones, liver disease, pancreatitis, and gastrointestinal bleeding using advanced endoscopy, imaging, and minimally invasive procedures.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:972:\"<p>Digestive problems often start as minor discomforts — persistent acidity, bloating, irregular bowel habits, or abdominal pain — but can progress to serious conditions like chronic inflammation, liver damage, ulcers, nutritional deficiencies, or GI bleeding if left untreated. As a dedicated gastroenterology treatment hospital in Bangalore, Nano Hospitals focuses on early endoscopic diagnosis, identifying root causes, and personalised treatment plans to restore digestive health and prevent recurrence.</p><p>Care at Nano Hospitals follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, high-definition endoscopy and colonoscopy, advanced liver and abdominal imaging, dietary guidance, and surgical intervention when needed. Each gastroenterology treatment plan in Bangalore is tailored to the patient&#039;s age, lifestyle, medical history, and disease severity — with structured follow-up to ensure lasting digestive health and quality of life.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:454:\"<p>Gastroenterology deals with diseases of the gastrointestinal (GI) tract and associated organs such as the liver and pancreas. Early symptoms like persistent heartburn, abdominal pain, constipation, diarrhea, or unexplained weight loss should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis through endoscopy and imaging, personalised treatment plans, and long-term dietary and lifestyle support to maintain digestive health.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1059:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical management of acidity, gastritis, and reflux</p></li><li><p>Treatment of infections such as H. pylori</p></li><li><p>Dietary planning for IBS and digestive disorders</p></li><li><p>Medication-based management of liver and pancreatic conditions</p></li><li><p>Nutritional therapy for malabsorption disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Upper GI endoscopy for stomach and esophagus evaluation</p></li><li><p>Colonoscopy for large intestine examination</p></li><li><p>ERCP for bile duct and pancreatic duct disorders</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic removal of polyps and small growths</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic control of GI bleeding</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Gallbladder removal (cholecystectomy)</p></li><li><p>Surgery for hernias affecting the digestive tract</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction surgery</p></li><li><p>Liver and pancreatic surgical procedures (when required)</p></li><li><p>Tumor removal surgeries in the digestive system</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:450:\"<ul><li><p>High-definition endoscopy and colonoscopy systems</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound for abdominal organ evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan and MRI for liver, pancreas, and intestinal imaging</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory testing for digestive disorders</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic ultrasound (EUS) for deeper tissue assessment</p></li><li><p>Dedicated GI procedure suites</p></li><li><p>Post-procedure recovery and monitoring units</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:414:\"<ul><li><p>Acid reflux (GERD) and gastritis</p></li><li><p>Peptic ulcers</p></li><li><p>Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS)</p></li><li><p>Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD)</p></li><li><p>Gallstones and bile duct disorders</p></li><li><p>Liver diseases including fatty liver and hepatitis</p></li><li><p>Pancreatitis</p></li><li><p>Constipation and chronic diarrhea</p></li><li><p>Gastrointestinal bleeding</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:351:\"<ul><li><p>Chronic inflammation leading to long-term damage</p></li><li><p>Nutritional deficiencies due to poor absorption</p></li><li><p>Risk of bleeding or obstruction in untreated conditions</p></li><li><p>Liver damage if metabolic or viral diseases are not managed</p></li><li><p>Recurrence of symptoms without lifestyle modification</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:214:\"<ul><li><p>Gastroenterology</p></li><li><p>Hepatology (Liver Care)</p></li><li><p>Pancreatic Disorders Management</p></li><li><p>Advanced Endoscopy</p></li><li><p>GI Oncology (Digestive System Tumors)</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:106:\"Best Gastroenterology Hospital in Bangalore | Digestive Care, Endoscopy & Liver Treatment | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:273:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted gastroenterology hospital in Bangalore offering expert treatment for acidity, GERD, IBS, gallstones, liver disease, pancreatitis, and digestive disorders. Experienced gastroenterologists with DM Gastroenterology — book your appointment today.\n\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:28:42\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:42:49\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/696ceeb8-be1b-4ef3-adae-fee0989cdcda.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:7;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:4;s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"General Medicine\";s:4:\"slug\";s:16:\"general-medicine\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/c722a471-d790-4f97-b241-93335a9a9b2f.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/4391236c-b190-4044-8e18-6fcf4d9e7cbb.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:375:\"<p>General Medicine &amp; Allied Specialties at Nano Hospitals forms the core foundation of adult patient care, serving as the first and most crucial point of contact for individuals experiencing acute illness, chronic disease, or unexplained symptoms. The department focuses on holistic diagnosis, medical management, disease prevention, and long-term health monitoring.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:419:\"<p>Many medical conditions begin subtly—fatigue, fever, breathlessness, weight changes, or body pain may signal deeper issues. General Medicine specialists are trained to assess the body as a whole, identify root causes, and coordinate care across specialties when required.</p><p>Care is continuous, evidence-based, and personalised—supporting patients through illness, recovery, and long-term disease control.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:317:\"<p>General Medicine focuses on comprehensive adult healthcare, from diagnosis of acute illnesses to long-term management of chronic and complex conditions.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, the department plays a pivotal role in early detection, coordinated treatment, and timely referral to super-specialties when needed.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:913:\"<h3><strong>Diagnostic &amp; Evaluation Services</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Detailed medical consultation and physical examination</p></li><li><p>Systematic evaluation of unexplained symptoms</p></li><li><p>Risk assessment for lifestyle and metabolic diseases</p></li><li><p>Coordination of diagnostic investigations</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Medical Management</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Treatment of acute infections and illnesses</p></li><li><p>Long-term management of chronic diseases</p></li><li><p>Medication optimisation and monitoring</p></li><li><p>Supportive care during hospitalisation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Preventive &amp; Inpatient Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Preventive health check-ups and adult vaccinations</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle modification and nutritional counselling</p></li><li><p>Management of hospitalised patients</p></li><li><p>ICU coordination and post-discharge follow-up</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:344:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced laboratory medicine for accurate diagnostics</p></li><li><p>ECG, Digital X-Ray, CT Scan, and MRI</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography when cardiac assessment is required</p></li><li><p>24×7 pharmacy support</p></li><li><p>ICU and emergency services</p></li><li><p>Electronic monitoring and documentation systems</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:450:\"<ul><li><p>Fever of unknown origin and acute infections</p></li><li><p>Respiratory and gastrointestinal illnesses</p></li><li><p>Diabetes, hypertension, and thyroid disorders</p></li><li><p>Chronic kidney and liver disease (medical management)</p></li><li><p>Obesity, dyslipidaemia, and metabolic syndrome</p></li><li><p>Geriatric conditions and multiple co-morbidities</p></li><li><p>Undiagnosed fatigue, weight loss, pain, or weakness</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:288:\"<ul><li><p>Thorough clinical evaluation, not assumptions</p></li><li><p>Early diagnosis to prevent complications</p></li><li><p>Rational, evidence-based treatment</p></li><li><p>Clear communication and patient education</p></li><li><p>Long-term disease control and follow-up</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:209:\"<ul><li><p>Internal Medicine</p></li><li><p>Preventive Medicine</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Medicine</p></li><li><p>Infectious Disease Management</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle and Metabolic Disorder Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:60:\"Best General Medicine Hospital in Bangalore | Nano hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:170:\"Nano Hospitals offers expert general medicine care in Bangalore with experienced physicians for diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of a wide range of health conditions.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:11:51\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:15:56\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/4b17feda-73bd-4d51-a61e-89312fe7b056.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:4;s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"General Medicine\";s:4:\"slug\";s:16:\"general-medicine\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/c722a471-d790-4f97-b241-93335a9a9b2f.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/4391236c-b190-4044-8e18-6fcf4d9e7cbb.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:375:\"<p>General Medicine &amp; Allied Specialties at Nano Hospitals forms the core foundation of adult patient care, serving as the first and most crucial point of contact for individuals experiencing acute illness, chronic disease, or unexplained symptoms. The department focuses on holistic diagnosis, medical management, disease prevention, and long-term health monitoring.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:419:\"<p>Many medical conditions begin subtly—fatigue, fever, breathlessness, weight changes, or body pain may signal deeper issues. General Medicine specialists are trained to assess the body as a whole, identify root causes, and coordinate care across specialties when required.</p><p>Care is continuous, evidence-based, and personalised—supporting patients through illness, recovery, and long-term disease control.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:317:\"<p>General Medicine focuses on comprehensive adult healthcare, from diagnosis of acute illnesses to long-term management of chronic and complex conditions.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, the department plays a pivotal role in early detection, coordinated treatment, and timely referral to super-specialties when needed.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:913:\"<h3><strong>Diagnostic &amp; Evaluation Services</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Detailed medical consultation and physical examination</p></li><li><p>Systematic evaluation of unexplained symptoms</p></li><li><p>Risk assessment for lifestyle and metabolic diseases</p></li><li><p>Coordination of diagnostic investigations</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Medical Management</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Treatment of acute infections and illnesses</p></li><li><p>Long-term management of chronic diseases</p></li><li><p>Medication optimisation and monitoring</p></li><li><p>Supportive care during hospitalisation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Preventive &amp; Inpatient Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Preventive health check-ups and adult vaccinations</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle modification and nutritional counselling</p></li><li><p>Management of hospitalised patients</p></li><li><p>ICU coordination and post-discharge follow-up</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:344:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced laboratory medicine for accurate diagnostics</p></li><li><p>ECG, Digital X-Ray, CT Scan, and MRI</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography when cardiac assessment is required</p></li><li><p>24×7 pharmacy support</p></li><li><p>ICU and emergency services</p></li><li><p>Electronic monitoring and documentation systems</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:450:\"<ul><li><p>Fever of unknown origin and acute infections</p></li><li><p>Respiratory and gastrointestinal illnesses</p></li><li><p>Diabetes, hypertension, and thyroid disorders</p></li><li><p>Chronic kidney and liver disease (medical management)</p></li><li><p>Obesity, dyslipidaemia, and metabolic syndrome</p></li><li><p>Geriatric conditions and multiple co-morbidities</p></li><li><p>Undiagnosed fatigue, weight loss, pain, or weakness</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:288:\"<ul><li><p>Thorough clinical evaluation, not assumptions</p></li><li><p>Early diagnosis to prevent complications</p></li><li><p>Rational, evidence-based treatment</p></li><li><p>Clear communication and patient education</p></li><li><p>Long-term disease control and follow-up</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:209:\"<ul><li><p>Internal Medicine</p></li><li><p>Preventive Medicine</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Medicine</p></li><li><p>Infectious Disease Management</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle and Metabolic Disorder Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:60:\"Best General Medicine Hospital in Bangalore | Nano hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:170:\"Nano Hospitals offers expert general medicine care in Bangalore with experienced physicians for diagnosis, treatment, and prevention of a wide range of health conditions.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:11:51\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:15:56\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/4b17feda-73bd-4d51-a61e-89312fe7b056.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:8;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:20;s:4:\"name\";s:15:\"General Surgery\";s:4:\"slug\";s:15:\"general-surgery\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/b2ff2995-3f03-4edb-b01d-745873f23215.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/743532e5-1351-4c45-b9b9-0d681d1876c8.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:306:\"<p>General Surgery at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the surgical management of a wide range of conditions affecting the abdomen, digestive tract, soft tissues, skin, and certain endocrine organs. It is one of the core surgical specialties, addressing both emergency and planned procedures.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:717:\"<p>Surgical conditions may present with symptoms such as persistent abdominal pain, swelling, lumps, hernias, infections, or digestive complications. Some conditions require urgent intervention, while others can be treated electively using minimally invasive techniques. At Nano Hospitals, care aims to provide safe surgery, faster recovery, minimal scarring, and reduced hospital stay whenever possible.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, imaging, laboratory tests, anesthesia support, advanced laparoscopic techniques, and structured post-operative care. Each surgical plan is personalised based on the patient’s condition, age, overall health, and risk factors.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:446:\"<p>General Surgery deals with diseases that often require operative treatment, particularly those involving the abdomen and soft tissues. Early symptoms like severe abdominal pain, vomiting, swelling in the groin, or unexplained lumps should be medically evaluated without delay.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises timely diagnosis, minimally invasive approaches, infection control, and enhanced recovery protocols for improved patient outcomes.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:844:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Initial management of infections and abscesses</p></li><li><p>Medical management of early-stage surgical conditions</p></li><li><p>Wound care and dressing</p></li><li><p>Pre-surgical evaluation and stabilization</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Laparoscopic appendectomy</p></li><li><p>Laparoscopic gallbladder removal</p></li><li><p>Laparoscopic hernia repair</p></li><li><p>Diagnostic laparoscopy</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive abscess drainage</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Appendectomy for appendicitis</p></li><li><p>Hernia repair surgery</p></li><li><p>Gallbladder removal for gallstones</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction surgery</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and breast lump surgeries</p></li><li><p>Emergency abdominal surgeries</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:317:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced laparoscopic surgery systems</p></li><li><p>High-definition imaging equipment</p></li><li><p>Modular operation theatres</p></li><li><p>Intensive Care Unit (ICU) support</p></li><li><p>Post-operative monitoring units</p></li><li><p>Sterile surgical environments with infection control</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:370:\"<ul><li><p>Appendicitis</p></li><li><p>Hernias (inguinal, umbilical, incisional)</p></li><li><p>Gallstones and gallbladder disease</p></li><li><p>Piles (hemorrhoids) and anal fissures</p></li><li><p>Breast lumps and infections</p></li><li><p>Thyroid nodules and goiter</p></li><li><p>Abdominal infections and abscesses</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:336:\"<ul><li><p>Risk of complications in emergency surgeries</p></li><li><p>Infection risk if wounds are not properly managed</p></li><li><p>Delayed treatment leading to severe complications</p></li><li><p>Need for post-operative lifestyle adjustments</p></li><li><p>Possibility of recurrence in certain conditions like hernias</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:215:\"<ul><li><p>Laparoscopic (Minimally Invasive) Surgery</p></li><li><p>Gastrointestinal Surgery</p></li><li><p>Breast Surgery</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and Endocrine Surgery</p></li><li><p>Colorectal Surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:59:\"Comprehensive General Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:134:\"Trusted general surgery services at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore. Expert surgeons for a wide range of conditions and surgical treatments.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:04:07\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-07 14:05:37\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/38da333d-f9cb-4879-af67-1e028b207439.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:20;s:4:\"name\";s:15:\"General Surgery\";s:4:\"slug\";s:15:\"general-surgery\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/b2ff2995-3f03-4edb-b01d-745873f23215.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:60:\"specialities/icons/743532e5-1351-4c45-b9b9-0d681d1876c8.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:306:\"<p>General Surgery at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the surgical management of a wide range of conditions affecting the abdomen, digestive tract, soft tissues, skin, and certain endocrine organs. It is one of the core surgical specialties, addressing both emergency and planned procedures.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:717:\"<p>Surgical conditions may present with symptoms such as persistent abdominal pain, swelling, lumps, hernias, infections, or digestive complications. Some conditions require urgent intervention, while others can be treated electively using minimally invasive techniques. At Nano Hospitals, care aims to provide safe surgery, faster recovery, minimal scarring, and reduced hospital stay whenever possible.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, imaging, laboratory tests, anesthesia support, advanced laparoscopic techniques, and structured post-operative care. Each surgical plan is personalised based on the patient’s condition, age, overall health, and risk factors.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:446:\"<p>General Surgery deals with diseases that often require operative treatment, particularly those involving the abdomen and soft tissues. Early symptoms like severe abdominal pain, vomiting, swelling in the groin, or unexplained lumps should be medically evaluated without delay.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises timely diagnosis, minimally invasive approaches, infection control, and enhanced recovery protocols for improved patient outcomes.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:844:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Initial management of infections and abscesses</p></li><li><p>Medical management of early-stage surgical conditions</p></li><li><p>Wound care and dressing</p></li><li><p>Pre-surgical evaluation and stabilization</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Laparoscopic appendectomy</p></li><li><p>Laparoscopic gallbladder removal</p></li><li><p>Laparoscopic hernia repair</p></li><li><p>Diagnostic laparoscopy</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive abscess drainage</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Appendectomy for appendicitis</p></li><li><p>Hernia repair surgery</p></li><li><p>Gallbladder removal for gallstones</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction surgery</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and breast lump surgeries</p></li><li><p>Emergency abdominal surgeries</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:317:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced laparoscopic surgery systems</p></li><li><p>High-definition imaging equipment</p></li><li><p>Modular operation theatres</p></li><li><p>Intensive Care Unit (ICU) support</p></li><li><p>Post-operative monitoring units</p></li><li><p>Sterile surgical environments with infection control</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:370:\"<ul><li><p>Appendicitis</p></li><li><p>Hernias (inguinal, umbilical, incisional)</p></li><li><p>Gallstones and gallbladder disease</p></li><li><p>Piles (hemorrhoids) and anal fissures</p></li><li><p>Breast lumps and infections</p></li><li><p>Thyroid nodules and goiter</p></li><li><p>Abdominal infections and abscesses</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:336:\"<ul><li><p>Risk of complications in emergency surgeries</p></li><li><p>Infection risk if wounds are not properly managed</p></li><li><p>Delayed treatment leading to severe complications</p></li><li><p>Need for post-operative lifestyle adjustments</p></li><li><p>Possibility of recurrence in certain conditions like hernias</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:215:\"<ul><li><p>Laparoscopic (Minimally Invasive) Surgery</p></li><li><p>Gastrointestinal Surgery</p></li><li><p>Breast Surgery</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and Endocrine Surgery</p></li><li><p>Colorectal Surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:59:\"Comprehensive General Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:134:\"Trusted general surgery services at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore. Expert surgeons for a wide range of conditions and surgical treatments.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:04:07\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-07 14:05:37\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/38da333d-f9cb-4879-af67-1e028b207439.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:9;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:23;s:4:\"name\";s:23:\"Geriatrics (Elder Care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:10:\"geriatrics\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/0d72e63e-fd1d-427c-a360-747430272bc4.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8RK6FVB8NJHQ6KGJH998F.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:292:\"<p>Elder Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the comprehensive healthcare needs of older adults. This specialty addresses age-related medical conditions, mobility challenges, memory concerns, and overall well-being to help seniors maintain independence and quality of life.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:719:\"<p>As people age, they may experience multiple health issues such as joint pain, balance problems, memory decline, vision or hearing loss, and chronic illnesses like diabetes or heart disease. These conditions often require coordinated care rather than treatment of a single problem. At Nano Hospitals, elder care is designed to provide holistic, respectful, and continuous support tailored to the unique needs of senior patients.</p><p>Care follows a patient-centred and family-inclusive approach, combining medical management, rehabilitation, nutritional guidance, mental health support, and preventive care. Treatment plans are personalised according to functional ability, lifestyle, and long-term health goals.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:389:\"<p>Geriatric care focuses on preventing, diagnosing, and managing health conditions common in older adults. Early recognition of mobility decline, memory changes, or increased fall risk can significantly improve long-term outcomes.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises preventive screenings, chronic disease management, fall prevention, and rehabilitation to support safe and active ageing.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:843:\"<h3>Medical Care</h3><ul><li><p>Management of chronic diseases (diabetes, hypertension, arthritis)</p></li><li><p>Medication review to prevent side effects and interactions</p></li><li><p>Memory and cognitive health evaluation</p></li><li><p>Vaccination and preventive health screening</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive Therapies</h3><ul><li><p>Physiotherapy for mobility and balance</p></li><li><p>Nutritional counselling for age-related needs</p></li><li><p>Pain management programs</p></li><li><p>Mental health support for depression, anxiety, and loneliness</p></li></ul><h3>Functional and Home Support</h3><ul><li><p>Fall risk assessment and prevention strategies</p></li><li><p>Home care guidance and caregiver education</p></li><li><p>Post-hospitalisation recovery programs</p></li><li><p>Palliative and comfort care when needed</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:355:\"<ul><li><p>Senior-friendly consultation areas</p></li><li><p>Multidisciplinary geriatric assessment services</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation and physiotherapy units</p></li><li><p>Cognitive screening and mental health support</p></li><li><p>Nutrition and lifestyle counselling services</p></li><li><p>Coordination with home healthcare services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:381:\"<ul><li><p>Arthritis and joint degeneration</p></li><li><p>Osteoporosis and fracture risk</p></li><li><p>Memory disorders and dementia</p></li><li><p>Balance disorders and frequent falls</p></li><li><p>Hearing and vision-related difficulties</p></li><li><p>Chronic heart, lung, and metabolic diseases</p></li><li><p>Urinary incontinence</p></li><li><p>Sleep disorders</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:288:\"<ul><li><p>Increased risk of falls and fractures</p></li><li><p>Multiple medications causing side effects</p></li><li><p>Memory decline affecting daily independence</p></li><li><p>Social isolation impacting mental health</p></li><li><p>Slow recovery after illness or surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:220:\"<ul><li><p>Geriatric Medicine</p></li><li><p>Memory and Cognitive Health Care</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Palliative and Supportive Care</p></li><li><p>Preventive Geriatric Health</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:63:\"Comprehensive Elder & Senior Care in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:130:\"Get specialized geriatric care in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Support for senior health, memory concerns, and independent living.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:13:23\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:11:14\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/fe45f2bc-389d-4ec0-afce-faac4e823222.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:23;s:4:\"name\";s:23:\"Geriatrics (Elder Care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:10:\"geriatrics\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/0d72e63e-fd1d-427c-a360-747430272bc4.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8RK6FVB8NJHQ6KGJH998F.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:292:\"<p>Elder Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the comprehensive healthcare needs of older adults. This specialty addresses age-related medical conditions, mobility challenges, memory concerns, and overall well-being to help seniors maintain independence and quality of life.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:719:\"<p>As people age, they may experience multiple health issues such as joint pain, balance problems, memory decline, vision or hearing loss, and chronic illnesses like diabetes or heart disease. These conditions often require coordinated care rather than treatment of a single problem. At Nano Hospitals, elder care is designed to provide holistic, respectful, and continuous support tailored to the unique needs of senior patients.</p><p>Care follows a patient-centred and family-inclusive approach, combining medical management, rehabilitation, nutritional guidance, mental health support, and preventive care. Treatment plans are personalised according to functional ability, lifestyle, and long-term health goals.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:389:\"<p>Geriatric care focuses on preventing, diagnosing, and managing health conditions common in older adults. Early recognition of mobility decline, memory changes, or increased fall risk can significantly improve long-term outcomes.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises preventive screenings, chronic disease management, fall prevention, and rehabilitation to support safe and active ageing.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:843:\"<h3>Medical Care</h3><ul><li><p>Management of chronic diseases (diabetes, hypertension, arthritis)</p></li><li><p>Medication review to prevent side effects and interactions</p></li><li><p>Memory and cognitive health evaluation</p></li><li><p>Vaccination and preventive health screening</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive Therapies</h3><ul><li><p>Physiotherapy for mobility and balance</p></li><li><p>Nutritional counselling for age-related needs</p></li><li><p>Pain management programs</p></li><li><p>Mental health support for depression, anxiety, and loneliness</p></li></ul><h3>Functional and Home Support</h3><ul><li><p>Fall risk assessment and prevention strategies</p></li><li><p>Home care guidance and caregiver education</p></li><li><p>Post-hospitalisation recovery programs</p></li><li><p>Palliative and comfort care when needed</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:355:\"<ul><li><p>Senior-friendly consultation areas</p></li><li><p>Multidisciplinary geriatric assessment services</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation and physiotherapy units</p></li><li><p>Cognitive screening and mental health support</p></li><li><p>Nutrition and lifestyle counselling services</p></li><li><p>Coordination with home healthcare services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:381:\"<ul><li><p>Arthritis and joint degeneration</p></li><li><p>Osteoporosis and fracture risk</p></li><li><p>Memory disorders and dementia</p></li><li><p>Balance disorders and frequent falls</p></li><li><p>Hearing and vision-related difficulties</p></li><li><p>Chronic heart, lung, and metabolic diseases</p></li><li><p>Urinary incontinence</p></li><li><p>Sleep disorders</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:288:\"<ul><li><p>Increased risk of falls and fractures</p></li><li><p>Multiple medications causing side effects</p></li><li><p>Memory decline affecting daily independence</p></li><li><p>Social isolation impacting mental health</p></li><li><p>Slow recovery after illness or surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:220:\"<ul><li><p>Geriatric Medicine</p></li><li><p>Memory and Cognitive Health Care</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Palliative and Supportive Care</p></li><li><p>Preventive Geriatric Health</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:63:\"Comprehensive Elder & Senior Care in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:130:\"Get specialized geriatric care in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Support for senior health, memory concerns, and independent living.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:13:23\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:11:14\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/fe45f2bc-389d-4ec0-afce-faac4e823222.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:10;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:3;s:4:\"name\";s:24:\"Gynaecology (Women care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:21:\"women-care-obstetrics\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/9e11e61f-65dc-4fcc-a31a-b6da65c0a508.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ87T8219AQDKPMNBFTX08S.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:314:\"<p>Women Care at Nano Hospitals is dedicated to supporting women through every stage of life—adolescence, reproductive years, pregnancy, childbirth, and menopause. Women’s health needs are complex and dynamic, influenced by hormonal changes, lifestyle, family planning choices, and age-related transitions.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:516:\"<p>From preventive screenings and menstrual health to safe motherhood and advanced gynaecological care, the department emphasises early diagnosis, informed decision-making, and respectful care. During pregnancy and childbirth, special focus is placed on maternal safety and newborn wellbeing, supported by integrated neonatal services and emergency preparedness.</p><p>Care is delivered in partnership with women and their families—ensuring clarity, dignity, and emotional support alongside medical excellence.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:345:\"<p>Women Care focuses on preventive health, reproductive wellbeing, safe motherhood, and gynaecological care across all life stages. Early diagnosis and continuity of care help women make informed health decisions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals combines clinical expertise with respectful, compassionate care to support women’s long-term wellbeing.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:866:\"<h3><strong>Preventive &amp; Outpatient Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Adolescent gynaecology counselling</p></li><li><p>Menstrual health evaluation and management</p></li><li><p>Family planning and contraception guidance</p></li><li><p>Routine gynaecological check-ups and screenings</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Antenatal &amp; Pregnancy Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Preconception counselling</p></li><li><p>Antenatal check-ups and fetal monitoring</p></li><li><p>Management of pregnancy-related conditions</p></li><li><p>High-risk pregnancy monitoring and care</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Labour, Delivery &amp; Gynaecological Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Normal and assisted vaginal deliveries</p></li><li><p>Emergency obstetric interventions</p></li><li><p>Immediate newborn assessment and care</p></li><li><p>Medical and surgical gynaecological treatments</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:332:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced labour room with continuous monitoring</p></li><li><p>Neonatal resuscitation setup within delivery areas</p></li><li><p>NICU for immediate newborn support</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound and imaging services</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory diagnostics</p></li><li><p>Emergency operation theatre access</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:333:\"<ul><li><p>Irregular or painful periods, PCOS, and hormonal imbalances</p></li><li><p>High-risk pregnancies and gestational complications</p></li><li><p>Anaemia during pregnancy</p></li><li><p>Uterine fibroids, ovarian cysts, and pelvic infections</p></li><li><p>Adolescent and menopause-related gynaecological concerns</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:227:\"<ul><li><p>Respectful, woman-centred care</p></li><li><p>Clear communication and shared decision-making</p></li><li><p>Safety-first clinical protocols</p></li><li><p>Emotional support during sensitive life moments</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:183:\"<ul><li><p>Obstetrics and Maternity Care</p></li><li><p>High-Risk Pregnancy Management</p></li><li><p>Preventive Gynaecology</p></li><li><p>Adolescent and Menopause Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:56:\"Best Gynaecology  Hospital in Bangalore | 