nitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT)</p></li><li><p>Stress management and relaxation therapy</p></li><li><p>Family and relationship counseling</p></li><li><p>Behavioral therapy for children and adolescents</p></li></ul><h3>Medication-Based Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Antidepressant and anti-anxiety medications</p></li><li><p>Mood stabilisers for bipolar disorder</p></li><li><p>Medication management for psychotic disorders</p></li><li><p>Sleep disorder treatment</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive and Advanced Care</h3><ul><li><p>De-addiction and substance use rehabilitation programs</p></li><li><p>Crisis intervention and emergency mental health care</p></li><li><p>Mindfulness and coping skill training</p></li><li><p>Occupational and social rehabilitation support</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:339:\"<ul><li><p>Private and confidential consultation rooms</p></li><li><p>Psychological testing and assessment tools</p></li><li><p>Therapy and counseling suites</p></li><li><p>Day-care mental health programs</p></li><li><p>Inpatient mental health support (when required)</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation and follow-up care services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:430:\"<ul><li><p>Depression and mood disorders</p></li><li><p>Anxiety disorders and panic attacks</p></li><li><p>Stress-related disorders</p></li><li><p>Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (OCD)</p></li><li><p>Bipolar disorder</p></li><li><p>Schizophrenia and psychotic disorders</p></li><li><p>Sleep disorders</p></li><li><p>Substance use and addiction</p></li><li><p>Emotional and behavioral issues in children and adolescents</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:298:\"<ul><li><p>Impact on work, studies, and relationships</p></li><li><p>Physical health problems linked to chronic stress</p></li><li><p>Social withdrawal and isolation</p></li><li><p>Risk of self-harm if severe symptoms are untreated</p></li><li><p>Stigma preventing timely help-seeking</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:206:\"<ul><li><p>Adult Psychiatry</p></li><li><p>Child and Adolescent Psychiatry</p></li><li><p>Clinical Psychology</p></li><li><p>De-addiction Psychiatry</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Mental Health Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:71:\"Best Mental Health Hospital in Bangalore | Psychiatry at Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:143:\"Get comprehensive psychiatry support in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Expert care for anxiety, depression, and overall psychological well-being.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:54:19\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-12 15:33:10\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/60a96ce2-5665-4524-9924-43b042a8ca6c.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:21;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:7;s:4:\"name\";s:23:\"Pulmonology (Lung Care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:9:\"lung-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/2eb47bd3-8740-4bf3-afb9-441228a04ded.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ89VSJPF5RRSXWXGPP1CB1.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:240:\"<p>Lung Care at Nano Hospitals focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of respiratory and lung-related conditions. Breathing problems may range from mild, recurrent symptoms to sudden, life-threatening emergencies.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:419:\"<p>Conditions such as asthma, chronic bronchitis, respiratory infections, or lung complications related to other medical illnesses can significantly affect daily life if not addressed early.</p><p>The department emphasises early intervention, accurate diagnosis, patient education, and continuity of care, supported by emergency and critical care services to prevent disease progression and reduce hospitalisations.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:318:\"<p>Lung Care focuses on early identification and structured management of respiratory conditions to improve breathing comfort and prevent complications.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, pulmonology services are closely integrated with emergency and ICU teams to ensure timely escalation and continuous respiratory support.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:941:\"<h3><strong>Diagnostic &amp; Evaluation Services</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Detailed respiratory history and clinical examination</p></li><li><p>Assessment of breathlessness, cough, and chest symptoms</p></li><li><p>Chest imaging coordination (X-ray, CT scan when required)</p></li><li><p>Laboratory investigations for infections and inflammation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Medical Respiratory Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Management of asthma and COPD</p></li><li><p>Treatment of respiratory infections</p></li><li><p>Oxygen therapy for breathing difficulty</p></li><li><p>Medical management of airway and lung inflammation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Emergency &amp; Long-Term Lung Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Stabilisation of acute respiratory distress</p></li><li><p>Ventilatory and oxygen support when required</p></li><li><p>Respiratory monitoring in ICU and wards</p></li><li><p>Chronic disease monitoring and patient education</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:397:\"<ul><li><p>Digital X-Ray for rapid chest evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan support for detailed lung imaging</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory medicine for respiratory diagnostics</p></li><li><p>ICU and emergency services for respiratory monitoring</p></li><li><p>Oxygen therapy and ventilatory support systems</p></li><li><p>24×7 pharmacy for uninterrupted respiratory medications</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:296:\"<ul><li><p>Asthma, COPD, and chronic bronchitis</p></li><li><p>Pneumonia, tuberculosis, and viral respiratory infections</p></li><li><p>Acute breathlessness and respiratory failure</p></li><li><p>Severe chest infections</p></li><li><p>Persistent cough, wheezing, and chest tightness</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:304:\"<ul><li><p>Early identification of respiratory symptoms</p></li><li><p>Accurate diagnosis of underlying causes</p></li><li><p>Preventive strategies to reduce flare-ups</p></li><li><p>Patient education for long-term control</p></li><li><p>Seamless integration with emergency and ICU services</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:184:\"<ul><li><p>Asthma and allergy care</p></li><li><p>Chronic lung disease management</p></li><li><p>Respiratory infection management</p></li><li><p>Critical respiratory care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:69:\"Best Lung Care Hospital in Bangalore | Advanced Respiratory Treatment\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:159:\"Nano Hospitals offers advanced lung care services in Bangalore for asthma, breathing disorders, and critical respiratory conditions with expert pulmonologists.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:19:03\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 12:49:52\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/b7bc5299-eb9a-4ef8-ba7c-5990e97a552f.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:7;s:4:\"name\";s:23:\"Pulmonology (Lung Care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:9:\"lung-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/2eb47bd3-8740-4bf3-afb9-441228a04ded.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ89VSJPF5RRSXWXGPP1CB1.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:240:\"<p>Lung Care at Nano Hospitals focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of respiratory and lung-related conditions. Breathing problems may range from mild, recurrent symptoms to sudden, life-threatening emergencies.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:419:\"<p>Conditions such as asthma, chronic bronchitis, respiratory infections, or lung complications related to other medical illnesses can significantly affect daily life if not addressed early.</p><p>The department emphasises early intervention, accurate diagnosis, patient education, and continuity of care, supported by emergency and critical care services to prevent disease progression and reduce hospitalisations.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:318:\"<p>Lung Care focuses on early identification and structured management of respiratory conditions to improve breathing comfort and prevent complications.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, pulmonology services are closely integrated with emergency and ICU teams to ensure timely escalation and continuous respiratory support.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:941:\"<h3><strong>Diagnostic &amp; Evaluation Services</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Detailed respiratory history and clinical examination</p></li><li><p>Assessment of breathlessness, cough, and chest symptoms</p></li><li><p>Chest imaging coordination (X-ray, CT scan when required)</p></li><li><p>Laboratory investigations for infections and inflammation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Medical Respiratory Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Management of asthma and COPD</p></li><li><p>Treatment of respiratory infections</p></li><li><p>Oxygen therapy for breathing difficulty</p></li><li><p>Medical management of airway and lung inflammation</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Emergency &amp; Long-Term Lung Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Stabilisation of acute respiratory distress</p></li><li><p>Ventilatory and oxygen support when required</p></li><li><p>Respiratory monitoring in ICU and wards</p></li><li><p>Chronic disease monitoring and patient education</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:397:\"<ul><li><p>Digital X-Ray for rapid chest evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan support for detailed lung imaging</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory medicine for respiratory diagnostics</p></li><li><p>ICU and emergency services for respiratory monitoring</p></li><li><p>Oxygen therapy and ventilatory support systems</p></li><li><p>24×7 pharmacy for uninterrupted respiratory medications</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:296:\"<ul><li><p>Asthma, COPD, and chronic bronchitis</p></li><li><p>Pneumonia, tuberculosis, and viral respiratory infections</p></li><li><p>Acute breathlessness and respiratory failure</p></li><li><p>Severe chest infections</p></li><li><p>Persistent cough, wheezing, and chest tightness</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:304:\"<ul><li><p>Early identification of respiratory symptoms</p></li><li><p>Accurate diagnosis of underlying causes</p></li><li><p>Preventive strategies to reduce flare-ups</p></li><li><p>Patient education for long-term control</p></li><li><p>Seamless integration with emergency and ICU services</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:184:\"<ul><li><p>Asthma and allergy care</p></li><li><p>Chronic lung disease management</p></li><li><p>Respiratory infection management</p></li><li><p>Critical respiratory care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:69:\"Best Lung Care Hospital in Bangalore | Advanced Respiratory Treatment\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:159:\"Nano Hospitals offers advanced lung care services in Bangalore for asthma, breathing disorders, and critical respiratory conditions with expert pulmonologists.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:19:03\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 12:49:52\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/b7bc5299-eb9a-4ef8-ba7c-5990e97a552f.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:22;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:24;s:4:\"name\";s:19:\"Radiology & Imaging\";s:4:\"slug\";s:17:\"radiology-imaging\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/3a8a2a3b-3aba-40bd-863e-2ba1d54e4d07.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8TZX2TB0DJZCJR59HVY23.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:345:\"<p>Radiology &amp; Imaging at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> provides advanced diagnostic and interventional imaging services that help detect, monitor, and guide treatment for a wide range of medical conditions. Imaging plays a critical role in early diagnosis, treatment planning, and follow-up care across nearly all medical specialties.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:578:\"<p>Many diseases may not show clear external symptoms in early stages. Imaging tests allow doctors to see inside the body safely and accurately, helping identify infections, fractures, tumors, organ disorders, and vascular conditions. At Nano Hospitals, radiology services focus on delivering precise imaging with minimal discomfort and radiation exposure.</p><p>Care is delivered by experienced radiologists and technologists using modern imaging technology and evidence-based protocols. Each imaging study is tailored to the patient’s symptoms, age, and medical history.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:349:\"<p>Radiology uses medical imaging techniques to diagnose and sometimes treat diseases. Imaging can detect problems early, often before symptoms become severe, allowing timely medical intervention.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises accurate image interpretation, fast reporting, and integration with clinical teams for effective patient management.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:775:\"<h3>Basic Imaging</h3><ul><li><p>Digital X-rays for bones, chest, and joints</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound for abdomen, pelvis, thyroid, and pregnancy scans</p></li><li><p>Doppler studies for blood flow evaluation</p></li></ul><h3>Advanced Imaging</h3><ul><li><p>CT Scan for detailed cross-sectional images of organs and bones</p></li><li><p>MRI for brain, spine, joints, and soft tissue evaluation</p></li><li><p>Mammography for breast screening</p></li><li><p>Bone density scan (DEXA) for osteoporosis assessment</p></li></ul><h3>Interventional Radiology</h3><ul><li><p>Image-guided biopsies</p></li><li><p>Drainage of fluid collections or abscesses</p></li><li><p>Vascular procedures such as angiography</p></li><li><p>Catheter-based minimally invasive treatment</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:377:\"<ul><li><p>High-resolution Digital X-ray systems</p></li><li><p>Multi-slice CT scanner</p></li><li><p>Advanced MRI scanner</p></li><li><p>3D/4D Ultrasound machines</p></li><li><p>Mammography units with low radiation dose</p></li><li><p>Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) for digital reporting</p></li><li><p>Dedicated interventional radiology suite</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:391:\"<ul><li><p>Bone fractures and joint disorders</p></li><li><p>Brain and spine conditions</p></li><li><p>Lung infections and chest diseases</p></li><li><p>Abdominal organ disorders</p></li><li><p>Tumors and abnormal growths</p></li><li><p>Kidney stones and urinary tract issues</p></li><li><p>Vascular blockages and clots</p></li><li><p>Pregnancy and fetal development monitoring</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:328:\"<ul><li><p>Minimising radiation exposure through safety protocols</p></li><li><p>Ensuring patient comfort during longer scans (e.g., MRI)</p></li><li><p>Need for contrast agents in some imaging studies</p></li><li><p>Claustrophobia concerns during MRI scans</p></li><li><p>Special precautions for pregnant patients</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:222:\"<ul><li><p>Diagnostic Radiology</p></li><li><p>Interventional Radiology</p></li><li><p>Neuroradiology</p></li><li><p>Musculoskeletal Imaging</p></li><li><p>Women’s Imaging</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Radiology</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:63:\"Advanced Radiology & Imaging Care in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:140:\"Expert radiology services at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore. Advanced imaging for diagnosis, monitoring, and guided treatment across specialties.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:15:59\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:20:40\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/c123a29f-f3b2-48d3-a6b6-65ae974e4725.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:24;s:4:\"name\";s:19:\"Radiology & Imaging\";s:4:\"slug\";s:17:\"radiology-imaging\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/3a8a2a3b-3aba-40bd-863e-2ba1d54e4d07.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8TZX2TB0DJZCJR59HVY23.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:345:\"<p>Radiology &amp; Imaging at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> provides advanced diagnostic and interventional imaging services that help detect, monitor, and guide treatment for a wide range of medical conditions. Imaging plays a critical role in early diagnosis, treatment planning, and follow-up care across nearly all medical specialties.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:578:\"<p>Many diseases may not show clear external symptoms in early stages. Imaging tests allow doctors to see inside the body safely and accurately, helping identify infections, fractures, tumors, organ disorders, and vascular conditions. At Nano Hospitals, radiology services focus on delivering precise imaging with minimal discomfort and radiation exposure.</p><p>Care is delivered by experienced radiologists and technologists using modern imaging technology and evidence-based protocols. Each imaging study is tailored to the patient’s symptoms, age, and medical history.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:349:\"<p>Radiology uses medical imaging techniques to diagnose and sometimes treat diseases. Imaging can detect problems early, often before symptoms become severe, allowing timely medical intervention.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises accurate image interpretation, fast reporting, and integration with clinical teams for effective patient management.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:775:\"<h3>Basic Imaging</h3><ul><li><p>Digital X-rays for bones, chest, and joints</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound for abdomen, pelvis, thyroid, and pregnancy scans</p></li><li><p>Doppler studies for blood flow evaluation</p></li></ul><h3>Advanced Imaging</h3><ul><li><p>CT Scan for detailed cross-sectional images of organs and bones</p></li><li><p>MRI for brain, spine, joints, and soft tissue evaluation</p></li><li><p>Mammography for breast screening</p></li><li><p>Bone density scan (DEXA) for osteoporosis assessment</p></li></ul><h3>Interventional Radiology</h3><ul><li><p>Image-guided biopsies</p></li><li><p>Drainage of fluid collections or abscesses</p></li><li><p>Vascular procedures such as angiography</p></li><li><p>Catheter-based minimally invasive treatment</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:377:\"<ul><li><p>High-resolution Digital X-ray systems</p></li><li><p>Multi-slice CT scanner</p></li><li><p>Advanced MRI scanner</p></li><li><p>3D/4D Ultrasound machines</p></li><li><p>Mammography units with low radiation dose</p></li><li><p>Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) for digital reporting</p></li><li><p>Dedicated interventional radiology suite</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:391:\"<ul><li><p>Bone fractures and joint disorders</p></li><li><p>Brain and spine conditions</p></li><li><p>Lung infections and chest diseases</p></li><li><p>Abdominal organ disorders</p></li><li><p>Tumors and abnormal growths</p></li><li><p>Kidney stones and urinary tract issues</p></li><li><p>Vascular blockages and clots</p></li><li><p>Pregnancy and fetal development monitoring</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:328:\"<ul><li><p>Minimising radiation exposure through safety protocols</p></li><li><p>Ensuring patient comfort during longer scans (e.g., MRI)</p></li><li><p>Need for contrast agents in some imaging studies</p></li><li><p>Claustrophobia concerns during MRI scans</p></li><li><p>Special precautions for pregnant patients</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:222:\"<ul><li><p>Diagnostic Radiology</p></li><li><p>Interventional Radiology</p></li><li><p>Neuroradiology</p></li><li><p>Musculoskeletal Imaging</p></li><li><p>Women’s Imaging</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Radiology</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:63:\"Advanced Radiology & Imaging Care in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:140:\"Expert radiology services at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore. Advanced imaging for diagnosis, monitoring, and guided treatment across specialties.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 18:15:59\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:20:40\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/c123a29f-f3b2-48d3-a6b6-65ae974e4725.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:23;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:17;s:4:\"name\";s:12:\"Rheumatology\";s:4:\"slug\";s:12:\"rheumatology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/5caa94a9-dc01-41b9-9150-232f38ff5266.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8YH5EY1KCNNYK5PF1XCQF.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:226:\"<p>Rheumatology at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of autoimmune and inflammatory diseases that primarily affect joints, muscles, bones, and connective tissues.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:757:\"<p>Rheumatologic conditions often begin gradually with symptoms such as joint pain, morning stiffness, swelling, fatigue, or muscle weakness. These disorders can be chronic and progressive, sometimes affecting internal organs like the lungs, heart, kidneys, or skin. At Nano Hospitals, care is aimed not only at controlling pain and inflammation but also at preventing joint damage, preserving mobility, and maintaining quality of life.</p><p>Care is delivered through a patient-centred, multidisciplinary approach combining clinical evaluation, laboratory testing, imaging, immunological assessment, medication therapy, and rehabilitation support. Each treatment plan is personalised based on disease type, severity, age, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:456:\"<p>Rheumatology deals with autoimmune, inflammatory, and degenerative conditions of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissues. Early signs such as persistent joint stiffness (especially in the morning), symmetrical joint pain, or unexplained fatigue should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis, disease-modifying treatment, and long-term monitoring to prevent irreversible joint damage and organ complications.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:940:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (DMARDs)</p></li><li><p>Biologic and targeted therapies for autoimmune diseases</p></li><li><p>Anti-inflammatory and pain management medications</p></li><li><p>Physiotherapy and joint mobility exercises</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle and dietary guidance for inflammation control</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Joint aspiration (removal of excess joint fluid)</p></li><li><p>Steroid injections for inflamed joints</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound-guided joint procedures</p></li><li><p>Minor procedures for soft tissue inflammation</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive and Advanced Care</h3><ul><li><p>Management of systemic autoimmune disorders</p></li><li><p>Bone protection therapy in inflammatory arthritis</p></li><li><p>Occupational therapy for joint function support</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation programs for long-term mobility</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:366:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced autoimmune and inflammatory blood testing</p></li><li><p>Musculoskeletal ultrasound</p></li><li><p>Digital X-ray, CT Scan, and MRI for joint evaluation</p></li><li><p>Bone density scan (DEXA) for osteoporosis risk</p></li><li><p>Infusion therapy units for biologic treatments</p></li><li><p>Physiotherapy and rehabilitation services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:336:\"<ul><li><p>Rheumatoid arthritis</p></li><li><p>Osteoarthritis</p></li><li><p>Ankylosing spondylitis</p></li><li><p>Psoriatic arthritis</p></li><li><p>Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)</p></li><li><p>Gout and crystal arthritis</p></li><li><p>Vasculitis</p></li><li><p>Fibromyalgia</p></li><li><p>Connective tissue diseases</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:339:\"<ul><li><p>Progressive joint damage without early treatment</p></li><li><p>Disability due to chronic pain and stiffness</p></li><li><p>Organ involvement in systemic autoimmune diseases</p></li><li><p>Need for lifelong monitoring and medication adjustment</p></li><li><p>Risk of osteoporosis in chronic inflammatory conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:243:\"<ul><li><p>Inflammatory Arthritis Management</p></li><li><p>Autoimmune Connective Tissue Disorders</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Rheumatology</p></li><li><p>Osteoporosis and Bone Health</p></li><li><p>Vasculitis and Systemic Disorders</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:65:\"Best Rheumatology Hospital in Bangalore | Joint & Autoimmune Care\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:145:\"Get specialized rheumatology treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Expert care for joint pain, autoimmune diseases, and chronic inflammation.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:56:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:28:31\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/06b63db8-2a15-41d5-a9c5-30a6e75d5fef.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:17;s:4:\"name\";s:12:\"Rheumatology\";s:4:\"slug\";s:12:\"rheumatology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/5caa94a9-dc01-41b9-9150-232f38ff5266.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8YH5EY1KCNNYK5PF1XCQF.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:226:\"<p>Rheumatology at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of autoimmune and inflammatory diseases that primarily affect joints, muscles, bones, and connective tissues.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:757:\"<p>Rheumatologic conditions often begin gradually with symptoms such as joint pain, morning stiffness, swelling, fatigue, or muscle weakness. These disorders can be chronic and progressive, sometimes affecting internal organs like the lungs, heart, kidneys, or skin. At Nano Hospitals, care is aimed not only at controlling pain and inflammation but also at preventing joint damage, preserving mobility, and maintaining quality of life.</p><p>Care is delivered through a patient-centred, multidisciplinary approach combining clinical evaluation, laboratory testing, imaging, immunological assessment, medication therapy, and rehabilitation support. Each treatment plan is personalised based on disease type, severity, age, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:456:\"<p>Rheumatology deals with autoimmune, inflammatory, and degenerative conditions of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissues. Early signs such as persistent joint stiffness (especially in the morning), symmetrical joint pain, or unexplained fatigue should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis, disease-modifying treatment, and long-term monitoring to prevent irreversible joint damage and organ complications.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:940:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (DMARDs)</p></li><li><p>Biologic and targeted therapies for autoimmune diseases</p></li><li><p>Anti-inflammatory and pain management medications</p></li><li><p>Physiotherapy and joint mobility exercises</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle and dietary guidance for inflammation control</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Joint aspiration (removal of excess joint fluid)</p></li><li><p>Steroid injections for inflamed joints</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound-guided joint procedures</p></li><li><p>Minor procedures for soft tissue inflammation</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive and Advanced Care</h3><ul><li><p>Management of systemic autoimmune disorders</p></li><li><p>Bone protection therapy in inflammatory arthritis</p></li><li><p>Occupational therapy for joint function support</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation programs for long-term mobility</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:366:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced autoimmune and inflammatory blood testing</p></li><li><p>Musculoskeletal ultrasound</p></li><li><p>Digital X-ray, CT Scan, and MRI for joint evaluation</p></li><li><p>Bone density scan (DEXA) for osteoporosis risk</p></li><li><p>Infusion therapy units for biologic treatments</p></li><li><p>Physiotherapy and rehabilitation services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:336:\"<ul><li><p>Rheumatoid arthritis</p></li><li><p>Osteoarthritis</p></li><li><p>Ankylosing spondylitis</p></li><li><p>Psoriatic arthritis</p></li><li><p>Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)</p></li><li><p>Gout and crystal arthritis</p></li><li><p>Vasculitis</p></li><li><p>Fibromyalgia</p></li><li><p>Connective tissue diseases</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:339:\"<ul><li><p>Progressive joint damage without early treatment</p></li><li><p>Disability due to chronic pain and stiffness</p></li><li><p>Organ involvement in systemic autoimmune diseases</p></li><li><p>Need for lifelong monitoring and medication adjustment</p></li><li><p>Risk of osteoporosis in chronic inflammatory conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:243:\"<ul><li><p>Inflammatory Arthritis Management</p></li><li><p>Autoimmune Connective Tissue Disorders</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Rheumatology</p></li><li><p>Osteoporosis and Bone Health</p></li><li><p>Vasculitis and Systemic Disorders</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:65:\"Best Rheumatology Hospital in Bangalore | Joint & Autoimmune Care\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:145:\"Get specialized rheumatology treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Expert care for joint pain, autoimmune diseases, and chronic inflammation.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:56:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:28:31\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/06b63db8-2a15-41d5-a9c5-30a6e75d5fef.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:24;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:4:\"name\";s:8:\"Urology \";s:4:\"slug\";s:7:\"urology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/b8e58dfa-a18a-4a39-ab22-65895a9194f1.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8AFVQM21H9TWPK3ZVNB5Z.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:522:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a leading urology hospital in Bangalore providing expert diagnosis and treatment for all urinary tract disorders in men and women, including kidney stones, prostate enlargement, urinary tract infections, bladder conditions, and male reproductive health problems. Our experienced urologists in Bangalore manage conditions affecting the kidneys, ureters, bladder, urethra, and prostate — using advanced endoscopic and minimally invasive surgical techniques for faster recovery and better outcomes.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:901:\"<p>Urological problems often begin with subtle symptoms — frequent urination, burning sensation, blood in urine, lower abdominal discomfort, or weak urinary flow — but can progress to kidney damage, urinary obstruction, or serious infection if left untreated. As a dedicated urology treatment centre in Bangalore, Nano Hospitals focuses on early detection, precise diagnosis, and timely intervention to protect kidney function and restore normal urinary health.</p><p>Every urology patient at Nano Hospitals receives a personalised treatment plan based on age, medical history, lifestyle, and condition severity — supported by advanced imaging, laser stone treatment, and structured post-treatment follow-up care. Patients across Bangalore trust Nano Hospitals for urology care because of the compassionate, patient-first approach at every stage — from first consultation to full recovery.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:516:\"<p>Urology focuses on diagnosing and managing disorders of the urinary system and male reproductive organs. Early signs such as painful urination, blood in urine, urinary leakage, or flank pain should not be ignored, as they may indicate infection, stones, prostate enlargement, or more serious conditions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early detection, accurate imaging and laboratory evaluation, minimally invasive intervention whenever possible, and long-term monitoring to protect urinary and kidney health</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1114:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical management of urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Medications for prostate enlargement and urinary symptoms</p></li><li><p>Bladder control therapy for incontinence</p></li><li><p>Dietary and lifestyle guidance for kidney stone prevention</p></li><li><p>Hormonal and medication-based management for certain male reproductive disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Cystoscopy for bladder and urethral evaluation</p></li><li><p>Ureteroscopy with laser treatment for kidney and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic prostate procedures (TURP and laser prostate surgery)</p></li><li><p>Image-guided catheter placements and stenting</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive treatment for urinary obstruction</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Kidney stone removal surgeries</p></li><li><p>Prostate surgery for severe enlargement or obstruction</p></li><li><p>Bladder tumor surgery</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive urological surgeries</p></li><li><p>Treatment of congenital urinary tract abnormalitie</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:507:\"<h2>Facilities and Technologies Used</h2><ul><li><p>Advanced Ultrasound for kidney, bladder, and prostate evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan for detailed stone and urinary tract imaging</p></li><li><p>MRI for complex urological assessments</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic urology equipment for minimally invasive procedures</p></li><li><p>Laser technology for stone and prostate treatment</p></li><li><p>Dedicated urology operation theatres</p></li><li><p>Post-operative monitoring and recovery units</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Conditions and Ailments Treated</h2><ul><li><p>Kidney stones and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Enlarged prostate (BPH)</p></li><li><p>Urinary incontinence and bladder control issues</p></li><li><p>Blood in urine (hematuria)</p></li><li><p>Bladder and kidney disorders</p></li><li><p>Male reproductive health issues</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Risks and Challenges</h2><ul><li><p>Recurrent stone formation if preventive care is not followed</p></li><li><p>Kidney damage due to untreated obstruction or infection</p></li><li><p>Urinary retention affecting bladder function</p></li><li><p>Chronic discomfort impacting daily life</p></li><li><p>Need for long-term monitoring in prostate and bladder conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:286:\"<h2>Sub-specialties in Urology</h2><ul><li><p>Endourology and Stone Management</p></li><li><p>Prostate Care and Male Urinary Disorders</p></li><li><p>Uro-Oncology (Urological Tumors)</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive Urology</p></li><li><p>Female Urology and Incontinence Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:87:\"Best Urology Hospital in Bangalore | Kidney Stone & Prostate Treatment | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:243:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted urology hospital in Bangalore offering expert treatment for kidney stones, prostate enlargement, UTIs, bladder disorders, and male reproductive health. Consult experienced urologists — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:25:57\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:17:17\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/50572282-7671-48f3-9be7-031c29c5a936.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:4:\"name\";s:8:\"Urology \";s:4:\"slug\";s:7:\"urology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/b8e58dfa-a18a-4a39-ab22-65895a9194f1.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8AFVQM21H9TWPK3ZVNB5Z.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:522:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a leading urology hospital in Bangalore providing expert diagnosis and treatment for all urinary tract disorders in men and women, including kidney stones, prostate enlargement, urinary tract infections, bladder conditions, and male reproductive health problems. Our experienced urologists in Bangalore manage conditions affecting the kidneys, ureters, bladder, urethra, and prostate — using advanced endoscopic and minimally invasive surgical techniques for faster recovery and better outcomes.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:901:\"<p>Urological problems often begin with subtle symptoms — frequent urination, burning sensation, blood in urine, lower abdominal discomfort, or weak urinary flow — but can progress to kidney damage, urinary obstruction, or serious infection if left untreated. As a dedicated urology treatment centre in Bangalore, Nano Hospitals focuses on early detection, precise diagnosis, and timely intervention to protect kidney function and restore normal urinary health.</p><p>Every urology patient at Nano Hospitals receives a personalised treatment plan based on age, medical history, lifestyle, and condition severity — supported by advanced imaging, laser stone treatment, and structured post-treatment follow-up care. Patients across Bangalore trust Nano Hospitals for urology care because of the compassionate, patient-first approach at every stage — from first consultation to full recovery.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:516:\"<p>Urology focuses on diagnosing and managing disorders of the urinary system and male reproductive organs. Early signs such as painful urination, blood in urine, urinary leakage, or flank pain should not be ignored, as they may indicate infection, stones, prostate enlargement, or more serious conditions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early detection, accurate imaging and laboratory evaluation, minimally invasive intervention whenever possible, and long-term monitoring to protect urinary and kidney health</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1114:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical management of urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Medications for prostate enlargement and urinary symptoms</p></li><li><p>Bladder control therapy for incontinence</p></li><li><p>Dietary and lifestyle guidance for kidney stone prevention</p></li><li><p>Hormonal and medication-based management for certain male reproductive disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Cystoscopy for bladder and urethral evaluation</p></li><li><p>Ureteroscopy with laser treatment for kidney and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic prostate procedures (TURP and laser prostate surgery)</p></li><li><p>Image-guided catheter placements and stenting</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive treatment for urinary obstruction</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Kidney stone removal surgeries</p></li><li><p>Prostate surgery for severe enlargement or obstruction</p></li><li><p>Bladder tumor surgery</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive urological surgeries</p></li><li><p>Treatment of congenital urinary tract abnormalitie</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:507:\"<h2>Facilities and Technologies Used</h2><ul><li><p>Advanced Ultrasound for kidney, bladder, and prostate evaluation</p></li><li><p>CT Scan for detailed stone and urinary tract imaging</p></li><li><p>MRI for complex urological assessments</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic urology equipment for minimally invasive procedures</p></li><li><p>Laser technology for stone and prostate treatment</p></li><li><p>Dedicated urology operation theatres</p></li><li><p>Post-operative monitoring and recovery units</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Conditions and Ailments Treated</h2><ul><li><p>Kidney stones and ureteric stones</p></li><li><p>Urinary tract infections (UTIs)</p></li><li><p>Enlarged prostate (BPH)</p></li><li><p>Urinary incontinence and bladder control issues</p></li><li><p>Blood in urine (hematuria)</p></li><li><p>Bladder and kidney disorders</p></li><li><p>Male reproductive health issues</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:380:\"<h2>Risks and Challenges</h2><ul><li><p>Recurrent stone formation if preventive care is not followed</p></li><li><p>Kidney damage due to untreated obstruction or infection</p></li><li><p>Urinary retention affecting bladder function</p></li><li><p>Chronic discomfort impacting daily life</p></li><li><p>Need for long-term monitoring in prostate and bladder conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:286:\"<h2>Sub-specialties in Urology</h2><ul><li><p>Endourology and Stone Management</p></li><li><p>Prostate Care and Male Urinary Disorders</p></li><li><p>Uro-Oncology (Urological Tumors)</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive Urology</p></li><li><p>Female Urology and Incontinence Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:87:\"Best Urology Hospital in Bangalore | Kidney Stone & Prostate Treatment | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:243:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted urology hospital in Bangalore offering expert treatment for kidney stones, prostate enlargement, UTIs, bladder disorders, and male reproductive health. Consult experienced urologists — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:25:57\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:17:17\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/50572282-7671-48f3-9be7-031c29c5a936.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:25;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:12;s:4:\"name\";s:16:\"Vascular Surgery\";s:4:\"slug\";s:16:\"vascular-surgery\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/d2edb3ef-e297-4343-ace4-1bf8ab7ee0cb.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8F6F501HFEH5PB27Q2ZY3.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:512:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a leading vascular surgery hospital in Bangalore, providing advanced diagnosis and treatment for all conditions affecting arteries, veins, and blood circulation. Our experienced vascular surgeons in Bangalore treat a wide range of disorders — from varicose veins and blocked arteries to diabetic foot, deep vein thrombosis (DVT), peripheral artery disease (PAD), and non-healing vascular ulcers — using the latest minimally invasive endovascular techniques for safe, faster recovery.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:1030:\"<p>Vascular disorders often begin with easily ignored symptoms — leg pain while walking, swollen feet, visible bulging veins, numbness, cold limbs, or slow-healing wounds. Without timely vascular treatment in Bangalore, these conditions can progress to dangerous complications including blood clots, gangrene, stroke, or limb loss. At Nano Hospitals, early detection through Doppler ultrasound and CT angiography ensures that circulation problems are identified and treated before they become life-threatening.</p><p>Every vascular patient at Nano Hospitals receives a personalised treatment plan based on disease severity, risk factors like diabetes and hypertension, and overall health. From medical management and compression therapy to endovascular stenting, laser varicose vein treatment, bypass surgery, and limb salvage procedures, Nano Hospitals offers complete vascular care under one roof — with expert surgeons, advanced imaging, and dedicated post-treatment follow-up across BG Road and Uttarahalli, Bangalore.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:409:\"<p>Vascular Surgery involves managing diseases of the circulatory system outside the heart and brain. Early symptoms such as leg cramps during walking, persistent swelling, skin discoloration, or cold extremities should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early vascular screening, Doppler studies, and preventive care to reduce the risk of stroke, limb loss, and other severe outcomes.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:967:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medications to improve blood flow and prevent clots</p></li><li><p>Compression therapy for venous disorders</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle modification and smoking cessation support</p></li><li><p>Wound care for vascular ulcers</p></li><li><p>Diabetes and blood pressure management to protect vessels</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Angiography for vessel imaging</p></li><li><p>Angioplasty and stent placement to open blocked arteries</p></li><li><p>Endovenous laser treatment (EVLT) for varicose veins</p></li><li><p>Catheter-based clot removal procedures</p></li><li><p>Image-guided vascular interventions</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Bypass surgery for blocked arteries</p></li><li><p>Varicose vein surgery</p></li><li><p>Carotid artery surgery to reduce stroke risk</p></li><li><p>Aneurysm repair surgeries</p></li><li><p>Limb-saving vascular reconstructions</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:405:\"<ul><li><p>Vascular Doppler Ultrasound</p></li><li><p>CT Angiography and MR Angiography</p></li><li><p>Digital Subtraction Angiography (DSA) suite</p></li><li><p>Endovascular catheterisation labs</p></li><li><p>Hybrid operation theatres for complex vascular procedures</p></li><li><p>Dedicated vascular ICU and recovery units</p></li><li><p>Advanced wound care and limb preservation services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:372:\"<ul><li><p>Peripheral Artery Disease (PAD)</p></li><li><p>Varicose veins and chronic venous insufficiency</p></li><li><p>Deep Vein Thrombosis (DVT)</p></li><li><p>Diabetic foot with poor circulation</p></li><li><p>Carotid artery disease</p></li><li><p>Aortic aneurysms</p></li><li><p>Non-healing vascular ulcers</p></li><li><p>Blood vessel blockages in limbs</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:300:\"<ul><li><p>Risk of stroke from untreated carotid disease</p></li><li><p>Limb loss due to severe arterial blockage</p></li><li><p>Recurrent clots in high-risk patients</p></li><li><p>Chronic pain and mobility limitations</p></li><li><p>Long-term care needed for diabetic vascular disease</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:238:\"<ul><li><p>Endovascular Surgery</p></li><li><p>Peripheral Arterial Disease Management</p></li><li><p>Venous Disorders and Varicose Vein Care</p></li><li><p>Diabetic Limb Salvage</p></li><li><p>Aortic and Major Vessel Surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:104:\"Best Vascular Surgery Hospital in Bangalore | Varicose Veins & Blocked Artery Treatment | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:272:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted vascular surgery hospital in Bangalore offering expert treatment for varicose veins, blocked arteries, diabetic foot, DVT, peripheral artery disease, and non-healing ulcers. Consult experienced vascular surgeons — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:43:28\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:18:10\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/bc161b15-e5eb-478c-8622-64722d0c1e94.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"