nts used to control excessive thyroid hormone production in conditions such as hyperthyroidism and Graves’ disease.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";N;s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-09 05:51:59\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 15:31:26\";s:2:\"h1\";s:42:\"Best Anti-Thyroid Medications In Bangalore\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:1:{s:4:\"faqs\";O:39:\"Illuminate\\Database\\Eloquent\\Collection\":2:{s:8:\"\0*\0items\";a:0:{}s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;}}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}',1785308079),('laravel-cache-content:v17:procedure:anti-tuberculosis-therapy-att','O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:756;s:5:\"title\";s:31:\"Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT)\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/f87e56de-8bfe-4482-a6d3-605cae5f6170.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:29:\"anti-tuberculosis-therapy-att\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:537:\"<p>Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT) is a specialized medical treatment procedure used to eliminate Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection and manage tuberculosis (TB) affecting the lungs or other organs of the body. ATT involves the use of a combination of anti-tubercular medications over a prolonged duration to control infection, prevent disease spread, reduce complications, and improve long-term recovery outcomes. Proper treatment adherence is essential to prevent drug resistance and ensure complete eradication of the infection.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:654:\"<p>Anti-tuberculosis therapy typically includes multiple medications administered together in different phases of treatment to effectively destroy TB bacteria and reduce the risk of resistance. ATT is commonly used for pulmonary tuberculosis, extrapulmonary tuberculosis, latent TB infection, and drug-resistant TB under close medical supervision. Treatment duration may vary depending on the severity of infection, drug sensitivity, patient health status, and response to therapy. Regular monitoring through laboratory tests, imaging, and clinical evaluation is important to assess treatment effectiveness and detect medication-related side effects.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:272:\"[{\"value\":\"Persistent cough lasting several weeks\"},{\"value\":\"Fever, night sweats, or chills\"},{\"value\":\"Weight loss, fatigue, or weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Chest pain or breathing difficulty\"},{\"value\":\"Coughing up blood or recurrent respiratory infections in advanced cases\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:1120:\"[{\"value\":\"Medication-related liver toxicity or gastrointestinal side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Drug-resistant tuberculosis due to incomplete treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Vision, nerve, or hearing complications from certain medications\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent infection or spread of disease to other organs\"},{\"value\":\"Increased risk of severe lung damage if treatment is delayed or interrupted\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Anti-tuberculosis therapy focuses on eliminating TB infection, preventing transmission, controlling symptoms, and reducing long-term respiratory complications. Treatment may include first-line anti-tubercular medications, multidrug-resistant TB therapy, nutritional support, respiratory care, infection control measures, and regular laboratory monitoring. Patients may also require hospitalization, oxygen therapy, pulmonary rehabilitation, counseling, vaccination support, and management of associated conditions such as HIV\\/AIDS or chronic lung disease. Strict medication adherence and regular medical follow-up are essential for successful treatment completion and prevention of recurrence.\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:700:\"<p>Anti-tuberculosis therapy focuses on eliminating TB infection, preventing transmission, controlling symptoms, and reducing long-term respiratory complications. Treatment may include first-line anti-tubercular medications, multidrug-resistant TB therapy, nutritional support, respiratory care, infection control measures, and regular laboratory monitoring. Patients may also require hospitalization, oxygen therapy, pulmonary rehabilitation, counseling, vaccination support, and management of associated conditions such as HIV/AIDS or chronic lung disease. Strict medication adherence and regular medical follow-up are essential for successful treatment completion and prevention of recurrence.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:373:\"[{\"value\":\"Regular monitoring of treatment response and respiratory symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Periodic liver function and laboratory evaluation during therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring for medication side effects or complications\"},{\"value\":\"Nutritional support and respiratory rehabilitation when required\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term pulmonology and infectious disease follow-up care\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:1120:\"[{\"value\":\"Medication-related liver toxicity or gastrointestinal side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Drug-resistant tuberculosis due to incomplete treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Vision, nerve, or hearing complications from certain medications\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent infection or spread of disease to other organs\"},{\"value\":\"Increased risk of severe lung damage if treatment is delayed or interrupted\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Anti-tuberculosis therapy focuses on eliminating TB infection, preventing transmission, controlling symptoms, and reducing long-term respiratory complications. Treatment may include first-line anti-tubercular medications, multidrug-resistant TB therapy, nutritional support, respiratory care, infection control measures, and regular laboratory monitoring. Patients may also require hospitalization, oxygen therapy, pulmonary rehabilitation, counseling, vaccination support, and management of associated conditions such as HIV\\/AIDS or chronic lung disease. Strict medication adherence and regular medical follow-up are essential for successful treatment completion and prevention of recurrence.\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:462:\"<p>The long-term outlook following anti-tuberculosis therapy is generally positive with early diagnosis and proper treatment adherence. Completion of the full ATT course, regular medical monitoring, healthy nutrition, infection prevention measures, smoking cessation, pulmonary rehabilitation, and continuous follow-up significantly help improve recovery, prevent recurrence, reduce complications, preserve lung function, and enhance overall quality of life.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:7:\"<p></p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:31:\"Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT)\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:210:\"Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT) is a specialized medical treatment procedure used to eliminate Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection and manage tuberculosis (TB) affecting the lungs or other organs of the body. \";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";N;s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-10 07:28:05\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-13 13:23:55\";s:2:\"h1\";s:43:\"Best Anti Tuberculosis Therapy in Bangalore\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:756;s:5:\"title\";s:31:\"Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT)\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/f87e56de-8bfe-4482-a6d3-605cae5f6170.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:29:\"anti-tuberculosis-therapy-att\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:537:\"<p>Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT) is a specialized medical treatment procedure used to eliminate Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection and manage tuberculosis (TB) affecting the lungs or other organs of the body. ATT involves the use of a combination of anti-tubercular medications over a prolonged duration to control infection, prevent disease spread, reduce complications, and improve long-term recovery outcomes. Proper treatment adherence is essential to prevent drug resistance and ensure complete eradication of the infection.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:654:\"<p>Anti-tuberculosis therapy typically includes multiple medications administered together in different phases of treatment to effectively destroy TB bacteria and reduce the risk of resistance. ATT is commonly used for pulmonary tuberculosis, extrapulmonary tuberculosis, latent TB infection, and drug-resistant TB under close medical supervision. Treatment duration may vary depending on the severity of infection, drug sensitivity, patient health status, and response to therapy. Regular monitoring through laboratory tests, imaging, and clinical evaluation is important to assess treatment effectiveness and detect medication-related side effects.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:272:\"[{\"value\":\"Persistent cough lasting several weeks\"},{\"value\":\"Fever, night sweats, or chills\"},{\"value\":\"Weight loss, fatigue, or weakness\"},{\"value\":\"Chest pain or breathing difficulty\"},{\"value\":\"Coughing up blood or recurrent respiratory infections in advanced cases\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:1120:\"[{\"value\":\"Medication-related liver toxicity or gastrointestinal side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Drug-resistant tuberculosis due to incomplete treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Vision, nerve, or hearing complications from certain medications\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent infection or spread of disease to other organs\"},{\"value\":\"Increased risk of severe lung damage if treatment is delayed or interrupted\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Anti-tuberculosis therapy focuses on eliminating TB infection, preventing transmission, controlling symptoms, and reducing long-term respiratory complications. Treatment may include first-line anti-tubercular medications, multidrug-resistant TB therapy, nutritional support, respiratory care, infection control measures, and regular laboratory monitoring. Patients may also require hospitalization, oxygen therapy, pulmonary rehabilitation, counseling, vaccination support, and management of associated conditions such as HIV\\/AIDS or chronic lung disease. Strict medication adherence and regular medical follow-up are essential for successful treatment completion and prevention of recurrence.\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:700:\"<p>Anti-tuberculosis therapy focuses on eliminating TB infection, preventing transmission, controlling symptoms, and reducing long-term respiratory complications. Treatment may include first-line anti-tubercular medications, multidrug-resistant TB therapy, nutritional support, respiratory care, infection control measures, and regular laboratory monitoring. Patients may also require hospitalization, oxygen therapy, pulmonary rehabilitation, counseling, vaccination support, and management of associated conditions such as HIV/AIDS or chronic lung disease. Strict medication adherence and regular medical follow-up are essential for successful treatment completion and prevention of recurrence.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:373:\"[{\"value\":\"Regular monitoring of treatment response and respiratory symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Periodic liver function and laboratory evaluation during therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Monitoring for medication side effects or complications\"},{\"value\":\"Nutritional support and respiratory rehabilitation when required\"},{\"value\":\"Long-term pulmonology and infectious disease follow-up care\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:1120:\"[{\"value\":\"Medication-related liver toxicity or gastrointestinal side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Drug-resistant tuberculosis due to incomplete treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Vision, nerve, or hearing complications from certain medications\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent infection or spread of disease to other organs\"},{\"value\":\"Increased risk of severe lung damage if treatment is delayed or interrupted\"},{\"value\":\"Treatment Options\"},{\"value\":\"Anti-tuberculosis therapy focuses on eliminating TB infection, preventing transmission, controlling symptoms, and reducing long-term respiratory complications. Treatment may include first-line anti-tubercular medications, multidrug-resistant TB therapy, nutritional support, respiratory care, infection control measures, and regular laboratory monitoring. Patients may also require hospitalization, oxygen therapy, pulmonary rehabilitation, counseling, vaccination support, and management of associated conditions such as HIV\\/AIDS or chronic lung disease. Strict medication adherence and regular medical follow-up are essential for successful treatment completion and prevention of recurrence.\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:462:\"<p>The long-term outlook following anti-tuberculosis therapy is generally positive with early diagnosis and proper treatment adherence. Completion of the full ATT course, regular medical monitoring, healthy nutrition, infection prevention measures, smoking cessation, pulmonary rehabilitation, and continuous follow-up significantly help improve recovery, prevent recurrence, reduce complications, preserve lung function, and enhance overall quality of life.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:7:\"<p></p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:31:\"Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT)\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:210:\"Anti-Tuberculosis Therapy (ATT) is a specialized medical treatment procedure used to eliminate Mycobacterium tuberculosis infection and manage tuberculosis (TB) affecting the lungs or other organs of the body. \";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";N;s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-10 07:28:05\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-13 13:23:55\";s:2:\"h1\";s:43:\"Best Anti Tuberculosis Therapy in Bangalore\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:1:{s:4:\"faqs\";O:39:\"Illuminate\\Database\\Eloquent\\Collection\":2:{s:8:\"\0*\0items\";a:0:{}s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;}}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}',1785308074),('laravel-cache-content:v17:procedure:antibiotic-therapy','O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:204;s:5:\"title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/8af12096-3c95-4bf1-8a9d-afc174649736.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:74:\"procedures/banners/relatedimages/989c2a28-2c1c-4a55-a387-00a199d8c2b4.webp\";s:4:\"slug\";s:18:\"antibiotic-therapy\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:159:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is a medical treatment used to manage bacterial infections in children using medications that kill or inhibit the growth of bacteria.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:111:\"<p>Antibiotics play an important role in treating serious bacterial illnesses and preventing complications.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:180:\"[{\"value\":\"High fever\"},{\"value\":\"Bacterial throat infection\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent cough with infection\"},{\"value\":\"Painful urination\"},{\"value\":\"Skin swelling or pus formation\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:187:\"[{\"value\":\"Culture sensitivity testing\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Urine testing\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical infection assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory infection evaluation\"}]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:141:\"<p>Doctors select antibiotics based on clinical findings, laboratory reports, culture sensitivity tests, and suspected infection sources.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:237:\"[{\"value\":\"Complete the full antibiotic course\"},{\"value\":\"Follow dosage instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration and nutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up evaluations if needed\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:119:\"<p>Proper antibiotic therapy effectively treats bacterial infections and prevents severe complications in children.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:100:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is essential for managing bacterial infections and reducing complications.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:75:\"Learn about antibiotic therapy and pediatric bacterial infection treatment.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:72:\"antibiotic therapy, pediatric antibiotics, bacterial infection treatment\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 15:59:51\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 16:13:29\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:204;s:5:\"title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/8af12096-3c95-4bf1-8a9d-afc174649736.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:74:\"procedures/banners/relatedimages/989c2a28-2c1c-4a55-a387-00a199d8c2b4.webp\";s:4:\"slug\";s:18:\"antibiotic-therapy\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:159:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is a medical treatment used to manage bacterial infections in children using medications that kill or inhibit the growth of bacteria.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:111:\"<p>Antibiotics play an important role in treating serious bacterial illnesses and preventing complications.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:180:\"[{\"value\":\"High fever\"},{\"value\":\"Bacterial throat infection\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent cough with infection\"},{\"value\":\"Painful urination\"},{\"value\":\"Skin swelling or pus formation\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:187:\"[{\"value\":\"Culture sensitivity testing\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Urine testing\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical infection assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory infection evaluation\"}]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:141:\"<p>Doctors select antibiotics based on clinical findings, laboratory reports, culture sensitivity tests, and suspected infection sources.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:237:\"[{\"value\":\"Complete the full antibiotic course\"},{\"value\":\"Follow dosage instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration and nutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up evaluations if needed\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:119:\"<p>Proper antibiotic therapy effectively treats bacterial infections and prevents severe complications in children.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:100:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is essential for managing bacterial infections and reducing complications.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:75:\"Learn about antibiotic therapy and pediatric bacterial infection treatment.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:72:\"antibiotic therapy, pediatric antibiotics, bacterial infection treatment\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 15:59:51\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 16:13:29\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:1:{s:4:\"faqs\";O:39:\"Illuminate\\Database\\Eloquent\\Collection\":2:{s:8:\"\0*\0items\";a:0:{}s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;}}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}',1785308086),('laravel-cache-content:v17:procedure:hip-replacement-surgery','O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:5:\"title\";s:24:\"Hip Replacement Surgery \";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/0d44d9ee-4961-4ee6-b9ec-d8a0de35764d.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:23:\"hip-replacement-surgery\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:742:\"<p>Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from severe hip pain, arthritis, and reduced joint mobility. As a best hospital in Bangalore for orthopedic care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced hip replacement procedures using modern surgical techniques and high-quality implants to restore movement and improve quality of life. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help reduce pain, enhance mobility, and prevent further joint deterioration.</p><p>This article explains hip replacement comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:293:\"<p>The hip is a ball-and-socket joint. In arthritis, the cartilage cushioning the joint wears away, causing bones to rub together. This leads to pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility. Hip replacement replaces the damaged joint with artificial components made of metal, ceramic, or plastic.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:387:\"[{\"value\":\"Persistent hip pain that limits walking, climbing stairs, or daily activities\"},{\"value\":\"Stiffness in the hip joint, especially after sitting or resting\"},{\"value\":\"Pain that continues even while resting or at night\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced range of motion and difficulty bending to put on shoes or socks\"},{\"value\":\"Limping or an uneven walking pattern due to joint discomfort\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:335:\"[{\"value\":\"Osteoarthritis causing cartilage wear in the hip joint\"},{\"value\":\"Rheumatoid arthritis or other inflammatory joint disease\"},{\"value\":\"Avascular necrosis (loss of blood supply to the femoral head)\"},{\"value\":\"Hip fracture or previous traumatic injury\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital hip dysplasia or long-standing joint deformity\"}]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:2:\"[]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:546:\"<p>Hip replacement surgery is considered when pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility no longer improve with medicines, physiotherapy, activity modification, or walking aids. The damaged ball-and-socket surfaces of the hip are replaced with artificial components to restore smoother movement and reduce pain.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, orthopedic specialists evaluate joint damage with clinical examination and imaging, then recommend total or partial hip replacement based on the severity of arthritis, fracture pattern, age, and overall health.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:509:\"[{\"name\": \"Total Hip Replacement (THR)\", \"description\": \"Both the femoral head (ball) and acetabulum (socket) are replaced.\\n\\nDamaged cartilage and bone are removed.\\n\\nArtificial components made of metal, ceramic, or polyethylene are implanted.\\nRecommended for severe arthritis or advanced joint damage.\"}, {\"name\": \"Partial Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"Only the femoral head is replaced.\\n\\nThe natural socket (acetabulum) is preserved.\\n\\nCommonly performed for hip fractures in elderly patients.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:629:\"[{\"stage\":\"Hospital stay (usually 2\\u20134 days)\",\"details\":\"Pain control, wound care, and first steps with a walker or support under physiotherapy supervision.\"},{\"stage\":\"First 2\\u20136 weeks\",\"details\":\"Home recovery with walking aids, hip precautions, and progressive physiotherapy to rebuild strength and confidence.\"},{\"stage\":\"6\\u201312 weeks\",\"details\":\"Most patients regain greater independence for daily activities; driving and light work may resume based on surgeon advice.\"},{\"stage\":\"3\\u20136 months\",\"details\":\"Continued improvement in mobility and endurance, with many patients returning to an active lifestyle.\"}]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:364:\"[{\"value\":\"Early walking with support under physiotherapy guidance\"},{\"value\":\"Pain control and swelling management as advised by the care team\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care and follow-up visits to monitor healing\"},{\"value\":\"Hip precautions and safe movement techniques during early recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual return to daily activities with strengthening exercises\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:287:\"[{\"value\":\"Infection around the surgical site or prosthesis\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots in the legs or lungs\"},{\"value\":\"Hip dislocation or implant loosening over time\"},{\"value\":\"Leg length difference or temporary nerve irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding, swelling, or delayed wound healing\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:226:\"<p>Hip replacement is highly successful — over <strong>90% of patients experience significant pain relief and improved mobility</strong>. Modern implants last 15–20 years, and many patients return to active lifestyles.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:325:\"<p>Hip replacement surgery transforms lives by relieving pain and restoring independence. With proper patient selection, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation, outcomes are excellent. Patients can look forward to walking comfortably, climbing stairs, and enjoying daily activities without the burden of chronic hip pain.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:64:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:153:\"Looking for the best and top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced hip replacement procedures with expert orthopedic care.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";N;s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-18 17:32:00\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-07-29 05:43:02\";s:2:\"h1\";s:47:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:8;s:5:\"title\";s:24:\"Hip Replacement Surgery \";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/0d44d9ee-4961-4ee6-b9ec-d8a0de35764d.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:23:\"hip-replacement-surgery\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:742:\"<p>Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals is recognized among the best and top treatment options for patients suffering from severe hip pain, arthritis, and reduced joint mobility. As a best hospital in Bangalore for orthopedic care, Nano Hospitals provides advanced hip replacement procedures using modern surgical techniques and high-quality implants to restore movement and improve quality of life. Early diagnosis and timely treatment can help reduce pain, enhance mobility, and prevent further joint deterioration.</p><p>This article explains hip replacement comprehensively — what the condition is, symptoms, causes, risks, prevention, diagnosis, surgical procedure, recovery, complications, and long-term outlook.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:293:\"<p>The hip is a ball-and-socket joint. In arthritis, the cartilage cushioning the joint wears away, causing bones to rub together. This leads to pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility. Hip replacement replaces the damaged joint with artificial components made of metal, ceramic, or plastic.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:387:\"[{\"value\":\"Persistent hip pain that limits walking, climbing stairs, or daily activities\"},{\"value\":\"Stiffness in the hip joint, especially after sitting or resting\"},{\"value\":\"Pain that continues even while resting or at night\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced range of motion and difficulty bending to put on shoes or socks\"},{\"value\":\"Limping or an uneven walking pattern due to joint discomfort\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:335:\"[{\"value\":\"Osteoarthritis causing cartilage wear in the hip joint\"},{\"value\":\"Rheumatoid arthritis or other inflammatory joint disease\"},{\"value\":\"Avascular necrosis (loss of blood supply to the femoral head)\"},{\"value\":\"Hip fracture or previous traumatic injury\"},{\"value\":\"Congenital hip dysplasia or long-standing joint deformity\"}]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:2:\"[]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:546:\"<p>Hip replacement surgery is considered when pain, stiffness, and reduced mobility no longer improve with medicines, physiotherapy, activity modification, or walking aids. The damaged ball-and-socket surfaces of the hip are replaced with artificial components to restore smoother movement and reduce pain.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, orthopedic specialists evaluate joint damage with clinical examination and imaging, then recommend total or partial hip replacement based on the severity of arthritis, fracture pattern, age, and overall health.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:509:\"[{\"name\": \"Total Hip Replacement (THR)\", \"description\": \"Both the femoral head (ball) and acetabulum (socket) are replaced.\\n\\nDamaged cartilage and bone are removed.\\n\\nArtificial components made of metal, ceramic, or polyethylene are implanted.\\nRecommended for severe arthritis or advanced joint damage.\"}, {\"name\": \"Partial Hip Replacement\", \"description\": \"Only the femoral head is replaced.\\n\\nThe natural socket (acetabulum) is preserved.\\n\\nCommonly performed for hip fractures in elderly patients.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:629:\"[{\"stage\":\"Hospital stay (usually 2\\u20134 days)\",\"details\":\"Pain control, wound care, and first steps with a walker or support under physiotherapy supervision.\"},{\"stage\":\"First 2\\u20136 weeks\",\"details\":\"Home recovery with walking aids, hip precautions, and progressive physiotherapy to rebuild strength and confidence.\"},{\"stage\":\"6\\u201312 weeks\",\"details\":\"Most patients regain greater independence for daily activities; driving and light work may resume based on surgeon advice.\"},{\"stage\":\"3\\u20136 months\",\"details\":\"Continued improvement in mobility and endurance, with many patients returning to an active lifestyle.\"}]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:364:\"[{\"value\":\"Early walking with support under physiotherapy guidance\"},{\"value\":\"Pain control and swelling management as advised by the care team\"},{\"value\":\"Wound care and follow-up visits to monitor healing\"},{\"value\":\"Hip precautions and safe movement techniques during early recovery\"},{\"value\":\"Gradual return to daily activities with strengthening exercises\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:287:\"[{\"value\":\"Infection around the surgical site or prosthesis\"},{\"value\":\"Blood clots in the legs or lungs\"},{\"value\":\"Hip dislocation or implant loosening over time\"},{\"value\":\"Leg length difference or temporary nerve irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Bleeding, swelling, or delayed wound healing\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:226:\"<p>Hip replacement is highly successful — over <strong>90% of patients experience significant pain relief and improved mobility</strong>. Modern implants last 15–20 years, and many patients return to active lifestyles.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:325:\"<p>Hip replacement surgery transforms lives by relieving pain and restoring independence. With proper patient selection, surgical expertise, and rehabilitation, outcomes are excellent. Patients can look forward to walking comfortably, climbing stairs, and enjoying daily activities without the burden of chronic hip pain.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:64:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:153:\"Looking for the best and top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore? Nano Hospitals offers advanced hip replacement procedures with expert orthopedic care.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";N;s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-18 17:32:00\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-07-29 05:43:02\";s:2:\"h1\";s:47:\"Best & Top Hip Replacement Surgery in Bangalore\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\