e\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:329;s:5:\"title\";s:54:\"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm Repair (Open / Endovascular)\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/807c5f3e-bd4d-4ba5-aeae-64c42e87e85e.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:50:\"abdominal-aortic-aneurysm-repair-open-endovascular\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:262:\"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA) repair is a major vascular procedure performed to treat dangerous enlargement of the abdominal aorta and prevent life-threatening rupture. Repair may be performed through open surgery or minimally invasive endovascular techniques.\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:462:\"An abdominal aortic aneurysm develops when the aortic wall weakens and enlarges over time. Treatment options include: Open surgical aneurysm repair Endovascular aneurysm repair (EVAR) The procedure involves: Replacing or reinforcing the weakened aorta Restoring safe blood flow Preventing rupture and internal bleeding EVAR generally offers: Smaller incisions Faster recovery Reduced hospital stay Large or symptomatic aneurysms usually require urgent treatment.\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:206:\"[{\"value\":\"Pulsating abdominal swelling\"},{\"value\":\"Abdominal or back pain\"},{\"value\":\"Sudden severe pain in rupture cases\"},{\"value\":\"Dizziness or collapse\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced blood circulation symptoms\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:178:\"[{\"value\":\"Major bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Graft complications or leakage\"},{\"value\":\"Infection or blood clots\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney complications\"},{\"value\":\"Rare aneurysm recurrence\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:242:\"[{\"value\":\"Maintain strict blood pressure control\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid smoking completely\"},{\"value\":\"Attend regular imaging follow-up visits\"},{\"value\":\"Take medications as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Report abdominal pain or weakness immediately\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:178:\"[{\"value\":\"Major bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Graft complications or leakage\"},{\"value\":\"Infection or blood clots\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney complications\"},{\"value\":\"Rare aneurysm recurrence\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:109:\"Early aneurysm repair significantly reduces rupture risk and improves long-term survival and vascular health.\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:54:\"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm Repair (Open / Endovascular)\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:262:\"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA) repair is a major vascular procedure performed to treat dangerous enlargement of the abdominal aorta and prevent life-threatening rupture. Repair may be performed through open surgery or minimally invasive endovascular techniques.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 07:03:51\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-09 05:52:03\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:329;s:5:\"title\";s:54:\"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm Repair (Open / Endovascular)\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/807c5f3e-bd4d-4ba5-aeae-64c42e87e85e.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:50:\"abdominal-aortic-aneurysm-repair-open-endovascular\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:262:\"Abdominal Aortic Aneurysm (AAA) repair is a major vascular procedure performed to treat dangerous enlargement of the abdominal aorta and prevent life-threatening rupture. Repair may be performed through open surgery or minimally invasive endovascular techniques.\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:462:\