lood pressure, improve heart function, and protect the kidneys and blood vessels. These medications are commonly used in hypertension, heart failure, and post-heart attack care. They help reduce strain on the heart and improve long-term cardiovascular outcomes.\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:314:\"Common medications include: Enalapril Ramipril Losartan Telmisartan Sacubitril/Valsartan (ARNI) The therapy helps: Relax blood vessels Reduce blood pressure Improve heart pumping efficiency Protect kidney function Reduce heart failure progression These medications are essential in modern heart failure management.\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:195:\"[{\"value\":\"High blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs or breathlessness\"},{\"value\":\"Weak heart pumping function\"},{\"value\":\"Diabetic kidney involvement\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:204:\"[{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent dry cough with ACE inhibitors\"},{\"value\":\"Elevated potassium levels\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic swelling reactions\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:251:\"[{\"value\":\"Monitor blood pressure regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend kidney function and electrolyte testing\"},{\"value\":\"Take medications consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid excessive salt intake\"},{\"value\":\"Report swelling or breathing difficulty immediately\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:204:\"[{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent dry cough with ACE inhibitors\"},{\"value\":\"Elevated potassium levels\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic swelling reactions\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:136:\"These medications improve heart function, reduce hospitalizations, protect kidney health, and improve long-term cardiovascular survival.\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:28:\"ACE Inhibitors / ARBs / ARNI\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:344:\"ACE inhibitors, ARBs, and ARNI medications are cardiovascular drugs used to lower blood pressure, improve heart function, and protect the kidneys and blood vessels. These medications are commonly used in hypertension, heart failure, and post-heart attack care. They help reduce strain on the heart and improve long-term cardiovascular outcomes.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 07:03:47\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 12:37:27\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:247;s:5:\"title\";s:28:\"ACE Inhibitors / ARBs / ARNI\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/8020abbd-fff9-4ece-b7db-8733e4fc8b93.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:24:\"ace-inhibitors-arbs-arni\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:344:\"ACE inhibitors, ARBs, and ARNI medications are cardiovascular drugs used to lower blood pressure, improve heart function, and protect the kidneys and blood vessels. These medications are commonly used in hypertension, heart failure, and post-heart attack care. They help reduce strain on the heart and improve long-term cardiovascular outcomes.\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:314:\"Common medications include: Enalapril Ramipril Losartan Telmisartan Sacubitril/Valsartan (ARNI) The therapy helps: Relax blood vessels Reduce blood pressure Improve heart pumping efficiency Protect kidney function Reduce heart failure progression These medications are essential in modern heart failure management.\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:195:\"[{\"value\":\"High blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Heart failure symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling of legs or breathlessness\"},{\"value\":\"Weak heart pumping function\"},{\"value\":\"Diabetic kidney involvement\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:204:\"[{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent dry cough with ACE inhibitors\"},{\"value\":\"Elevated potassium levels\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic swelling reactions\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:251:\"[{\"value\":\"Monitor blood pressure regularly\"},{\"value\":\"Attend kidney function and electrolyte testing\"},{\"value\":\"Take medications consistently\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid excessive salt intake\"},{\"value\":\"Report swelling or breathing difficulty immediately\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:204:\"[{\"value\":\"Low blood pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent dry cough with ACE inhibitors\"},{\"value\":\"Elevated potassium levels\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney function changes\"},{\"value\":\"Rare allergic swelling reactions\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:136:\"These medications improve heart function, reduce hospitalizations, protect kidney health, and improve long-term cardiovascular survival.\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:28:\"ACE Inhibitors / ARBs / ARNI\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:344:\"ACE inhibitors, ARBs, and ARNI medications are cardiovascular drugs used to lower blood pressure, improve heart function, and protect the kidneys and blood vessels. These medications are commonly used in hypertension, heart failure, and post-heart attack care. They help reduce strain on the heart and improve long-term cardiovascular outcomes.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 07:03:47\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 12:37:27\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:3;O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:58;s:5:\"title\";s:22:\"Achilles Tendon Repair\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/c87010c4-485d-4fef-8ff2-38eb8b97fb2e.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:22:\"achilles-tendon-repair\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:186:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair is a surgical procedure used to treat a torn or ruptured Achilles tendon, which connects the calf muscles to the heel bone and helps in walking and running.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:315:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair is a surgical procedure performed to repair a torn or ruptured Achilles tendon. The Achilles tendon is the largest tendon in the body and plays an essential role in walking, running, and jumping. Surgery restores tendon continuity and strength so the ankle can function normally again.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:123:\"[\"Sudden pain in the back of the ankle\", \"Difficulty walking\", \"Swelling near the heel\", \"Weakness while pushing the foot\"]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:90:\"[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden increase in physical activity\", \"Direct trauma to the tendon\"]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:135:\"[\"High-impact sports activities\", \"Sudden strain on calf muscles\", \"Previous Achilles tendon injuries\", \"Poor warm-up before exercise\"]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:181:\"[\"Warm up properly before physical activity\", \"Gradually increase intensity of exercise\", \"Perform calf strengthening and stretching exercises\", \"Use proper footwear during sports\"]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:153:\"[\"Physical examination of the ankle\", \"Ultrasound imaging of the tendon\", \"MRI scan to assess tendon rupture\", \"Functional assessment of ankle movement\"]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:270:\"<p>During Achilles tendon repair surgery, the torn ends of the tendon are stitched together using strong sutures. In some cases, tendon grafts may be used if the rupture is severe. The goal of the surgery is to restore tendon strength, stability, and ankle function.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:299:\"[{\"name\": \"1. Open Achilles Tendon Repair\", \"description\": \"A traditional surgical approach using an incision to repair the torn tendon.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Minimally Invasive Achilles Repair\", \"description\": \"A modern technique using small incisions and specialized instruments to repair the tendon.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:239:\"[\"Wear protective braces or casts as advised\", \"Follow physiotherapy and rehabilitation exercises\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain and inflammation\", \"Attend regular follow-up visits\"]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:81:\"[\"Infection\", \"Tendon stiffness\", \"Re-rupture of the tendon\", \"Nerve irritation\"]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:332:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair helps restore strength and flexibility in the ankle. With proper rehabilitation, most patients regain normal walking and athletic ability. Physiotherapy exercises improve muscle strength and balance. Avoiding excessive strain during recovery is important. Long-term results are usually very successful.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:228:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair surgery is an effective treatment for ruptured tendons and helps restore ankle stability and movement. With proper rehabilitation and care, patients can return to normal daily activities and sports.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:57:\"Achilles Tendon Repair Surgery & Recovery | Nano Hospital\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:160:\"Expert Achilles tendon rupture treatment at Nano Hospital. Learn about our advanced surgery options, diagnosis, recovery timelines, and expert care to get you b\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:155:\"achilles tendon repair surgery, achilles tendon rupture treatment, ankle tendon repair, achilles surgery, Nano Hospital orthopedics, torn achilles recovery\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-03-17 13:39:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-13 16:55:20\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:58;s:5:\"title\";s:22:\"Achilles Tendon Repair\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/c87010c4-485d-4fef-8ff2-38eb8b97fb2e.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:22:\"achilles-tendon-repair\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:186:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair is a surgical procedure used to treat a torn or ruptured Achilles tendon, which connects the calf muscles to the heel bone and helps in walking and running.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:315:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair is a surgical procedure performed to repair a torn or ruptured Achilles tendon. The Achilles tendon is the largest tendon in the body and plays an essential role in walking, running, and jumping. Surgery restores tendon continuity and strength so the ankle can function normally again.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:123:\"[\"Sudden pain in the back of the ankle\", \"Difficulty walking\", \"Swelling near the heel\", \"Weakness while pushing the foot\"]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:90:\"[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden increase in physical activity\", \"Direct trauma to the tendon\"]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:135:\"[\"High-impact sports activities\", \"Sudden strain on calf muscles\", \"Previous Achilles tendon injuries\", \"Poor warm-up before exercise\"]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:181:\"[\"Warm up properly before physical activity\", \"Gradually increase intensity of exercise\", \"Perform calf strengthening and stretching exercises\", \"Use proper footwear during sports\"]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:153:\"[\"Physical examination of the ankle\", \"Ultrasound imaging of the tendon\", \"MRI scan to assess tendon rupture\", \"Functional assessment of ankle movement\"]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:270:\"<p>During Achilles tendon repair surgery, the torn ends of the tendon are stitched together using strong sutures. In some cases, tendon grafts may be used if the rupture is severe. The goal of the surgery is to restore tendon strength, stability, and ankle function.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:299:\"[{\"name\": \"1. Open Achilles Tendon Repair\", \"description\": \"A traditional surgical approach using an incision to repair the torn tendon.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Minimally Invasive Achilles Repair\", \"description\": \"A modern technique using small incisions and specialized instruments to repair the tendon.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:239:\"[\"Wear protective braces or casts as advised\", \"Follow physiotherapy and rehabilitation exercises\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Take prescribed medications for pain and inflammation\", \"Attend regular follow-up visits\"]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:81:\"[\"Infection\", \"Tendon stiffness\", \"Re-rupture of the tendon\", \"Nerve irritation\"]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:332:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair helps restore strength and flexibility in the ankle. With proper rehabilitation, most patients regain normal walking and athletic ability. Physiotherapy exercises improve muscle strength and balance. Avoiding excessive strain during recovery is important. Long-term results are usually very successful.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:228:\"<p>Achilles tendon repair surgery is an effective treatment for ruptured tendons and helps restore ankle stability and movement. With proper rehabilitation and care, patients can return to normal daily activities and sports.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:57:\"Achilles Tendon Repair Surgery & Recovery | Nano Hospital\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:160:\"Expert Achilles tendon rupture treatment at Nano Hospital. Learn about our advanced surgery options, diagnosis, recovery timelines, and expert care to get you b\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:155:\"achilles tendon repair surgery, achilles tendon rupture treatment, ankle tendon repair, achilles surgery, Nano Hospital orthopedics, torn achilles recovery\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-03-17 13:39:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-13 16:55:20\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:4;O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:44;s:5:\"title\";s:18:\"ACL Reconstruction\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/e1d2a12b-f74e-4a75-aa79-8af8e493e42b.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:18:\"acl-reconstruction\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:169:\"<p>ACL reconstruction is a surgical procedure used to repair a torn anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) in the knee, which is commonly injured during sports activities.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:355:\"<p>ACL reconstruction is an orthopedic surgery performed to replace a damaged or torn anterior cruciate ligament in the knee. The ACL plays a critical role in stabilizing the knee joint during movement. When this ligament is torn due to injury or sports activity, surgical reconstruction using a tendon graft helps restore knee stability and function.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:97:\"[\"Sudden knee pain\", \"Knee instability\", \"Swelling around the knee\", \"Difficulty bearing weight\"]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:79:\"[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden twisting of the knee\", \"Direct impact to the knee\"]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:145:\"[\"High-impact sports such as football or basketball\", \"Sudden changes in direction while running\", \"Weak knee muscles\", \"Previous knee injuries\"]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:169:\"[\"Strength training for leg and knee muscles\", \"Proper warm-up before sports activities\", \"Use of correct sports techniques\", \"Avoid excessive stress on the knee joint\"]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:158:\"[\"Physical knee stability examination\", \"MRI scan to evaluate ligament damage\", \"X-ray imaging to rule out bone injury\", \"Arthroscopic diagnostic evaluation\"]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:351:\"<p>ACL reconstruction surgery involves replacing the torn ligament with a graft taken from another tendon in the patient’s body or from a donor. The graft acts as a new ligament and is secured inside the knee joint to restore stability and normal movement. Arthroscopic techniques are commonly used to perform the surgery with minimal incisions.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:499:\"[{\"name\": \"1. Autograft ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"The torn ligament is replaced using a tendon taken from the patient’s own body, usually from the hamstring or patellar tendon.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Allograft ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"A donor tendon graft is used to replace the damaged ACL ligament.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Arthroscopic ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive surgical approach using a small camera and specialized instruments to reconstruct the ACL.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:208:\"[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Use knee braces if recommended by the surgeon\", \"Apply ice to reduce swelling\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Attend regular follow-up visits\"]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:82:\"[\"Infection\", \"Knee stiffness\", \"Re-injury of the ligament\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:381:\"<p>ACL reconstruction helps restore stability and function of the knee joint. Most patients can return to sports and physical activities after proper rehabilitation. Strength training and physiotherapy are important for long-term recovery. Maintaining muscle strength around the knee helps protect the joint. With proper care, patients can achieve excellent long-term outcomes.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:237:\"<p>ACL reconstruction is a highly effective treatment for torn anterior cruciate ligaments. With modern surgical techniques and structured rehabilitation programs, patients can regain knee stability and return to an active lifestyle.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:43:\"ACL Reconstruction Surgery | Nano Hospitals\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:125:\"Learn about ACL Reconstruction surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:104:\"ACL reconstruction, anterior cruciate ligament surgery, ACL repair surgery, knee ligament reconstruction\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-03-17 13:12:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-03-17 15:44:35\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:44;s:5:\"title\";s:18:\"ACL Reconstruction\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/e1d2a12b-f74e-4a75-aa79-8af8e493e42b.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:18:\"acl-reconstruction\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:169:\"<p>ACL reconstruction is a surgical procedure used to repair a torn anterior cruciate ligament (ACL) in the knee, which is commonly injured during sports activities.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:355:\"<p>ACL reconstruction is an orthopedic surgery performed to replace a damaged or torn anterior cruciate ligament in the knee. The ACL plays a critical role in stabilizing the knee joint during movement. When this ligament is torn due to injury or sports activity, surgical reconstruction using a tendon graft helps restore knee stability and function.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:97:\"[\"Sudden knee pain\", \"Knee instability\", \"Swelling around the knee\", \"Difficulty bearing weight\"]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:79:\"[\"Sports injuries\", \"Sudden twisting of the knee\", \"Direct impact to the knee\"]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:145:\"[\"High-impact sports such as football or basketball\", \"Sudden changes in direction while running\", \"Weak knee muscles\", \"Previous knee injuries\"]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:169:\"[\"Strength training for leg and knee muscles\", \"Proper warm-up before sports activities\", \"Use of correct sports techniques\", \"Avoid excessive stress on the knee joint\"]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:158:\"[\"Physical knee stability examination\", \"MRI scan to evaluate ligament damage\", \"X-ray imaging to rule out bone injury\", \"Arthroscopic diagnostic evaluation\"]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:351:\"<p>ACL reconstruction surgery involves replacing the torn ligament with a graft taken from another tendon in the patient’s body or from a donor. The graft acts as a new ligament and is secured inside the knee joint to restore stability and normal movement. Arthroscopic techniques are commonly used to perform the surgery with minimal incisions.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:499:\"[{\"name\": \"1. Autograft ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"The torn ligament is replaced using a tendon taken from the patient’s own body, usually from the hamstring or patellar tendon.\"}, {\"name\": \"2. Allograft ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"A donor tendon graft is used to replace the damaged ACL ligament.\"}, {\"name\": \"3. Arthroscopic ACL Reconstruction\", \"description\": \"A minimally invasive surgical approach using a small camera and specialized instruments to reconstruct the ACL.\"}]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:208:\"[\"Follow physiotherapy exercises regularly\", \"Use knee braces if recommended by the surgeon\", \"Apply ice to reduce swelling\", \"Avoid high-impact activities during recovery\", \"Attend regular follow-up visits\"]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:82:\"[\"Infection\", \"Knee stiffness\", \"Re-injury of the ligament\", \"Blood clots (rare)\"]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:381:\"<p>ACL reconstruction helps restore stability and function of the knee joint. Most patients can return to sports and physical activities after proper rehabilitation. Strength training and physiotherapy are important for long-term recovery. Maintaining muscle strength around the knee helps protect the joint. With proper care, patients can achieve excellent long-term outcomes.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:237:\"<p>ACL reconstruction is a highly effective treatment for torn anterior cruciate ligaments. With modern surgical techniques and structured rehabilitation programs, patients can regain knee stability and return to an active lifestyle.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:43:\"ACL Reconstruction Surgery | Nano Hospitals\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:125:\"Learn about ACL Reconstruction surgery including symptoms, causes, diagnosis, treatment options, recovery timeline and risks.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:104:\"ACL reconstruction, anterior cruciate ligament surgery, ACL repair surgery, knee ligament reconstruction\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-03-17 13:12:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-03-17 15:44:35\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:5;O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:126;s:5:\"title\";s:46:\"Activity Modification and Ergonomic Correction\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/a57551a4-2889-4395-adbd-32d98e50094c.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:74:\"procedures/banners/relatedimages/b75a2cfe-86d3-4391-aa61-c6040c360182.webp\";s:4:\"slug\";s:46:\"activity-modification-and-ergonomic-correction\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:138:\"<p>Activity modification and ergonomic correction involve adjusting daily activities and posture to reduce stress on bones and joints.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:129:\"<p>This treatment focuses on preventing further injury and reducing pain through posture correction and movement improvement.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:221:\"[{\"value\":\"Pain during repetitive movements\"},{\"value\":\"Neck and back discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Joint strain during work activities\"},{\"value\":\"Muscle fatigue from poor posture\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced productivity due to pain\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:281:\"[{\"value\":\"Difficulty adapting to lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort during posture correction\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete symptom relief if habits continue\"},{\"value\":\"Slow improvement in chronic conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of recurrence without long-term compliance\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:75:\"<p>Ergonomic correction improves posture and reduces orthopedic strain.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:264:\"[{\"value\":\"Maintain proper sitting and standing posture\"},{\"value\":\"Use ergonomic furniture and supports\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid repetitive strain activities\"},{\"value\":\"Take regular stretching breaks during work\"},{\"value\":\"Follow physiotherapy guidance consistently\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:281:\"[{\"value\":\"Difficulty adapting to lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort during posture correction\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete symptom relief if habits continue\"},{\"value\":\"Slow improvement in chronic conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of recurrence without long-term compliance\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:81:\"<p>Ergonomic correction can significantly reduce pain and prevent recurrence.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:66:\"<p>Activity modification improves long-term orthopedic health.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:46:\"Activity Modification and Ergonomic Correction\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:59:\"Learn about ergonomic correction and activity modification.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:41:\"ergonomic correction, posture improvement\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-12 11:38:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-12 16:24:16\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:126;s:5:\"title\";s:46:\"Activity Modification and Ergonomic Correction\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/a57551a4-2889-4395-adbd-32d98e50094c.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:74:\"procedures/banners/relatedimages/b75a2cfe-86d3-4391-aa61-c6040c360182.webp\";s:4:\"slug\";s:46:\"activity-modification-and-ergonomic-correction\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:138:\"<p>Activity modification and ergonomic correction involve adjusting daily activities and posture to reduce stress on bones and joints.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:129:\"<p>This treatment focuses on preventing further injury and reducing pain through posture correction and movement improvement.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:221:\"[{\"value\":\"Pain during repetitive movements\"},{\"value\":\"Neck and back discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Joint strain during work activities\"},{\"value\":\"Muscle fatigue from poor posture\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced productivity due to pain\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:281:\"[{\"value\":\"Difficulty adapting to lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort during posture correction\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete symptom relief if habits continue\"},{\"value\":\"Slow improvement in chronic conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of recurrence without long-term compliance\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:75:\"<p>Ergonomic correction improves posture and reduces orthopedic strain.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:264:\"[{\"value\":\"Maintain proper sitting and standing posture\"},{\"value\":\"Use ergonomic furniture and supports\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid repetitive strain activities\"},{\"value\":\"Take regular stretching breaks during work\"},{\"value\":\"Follow physiotherapy guidance consistently\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:281:\"[{\"value\":\"Difficulty adapting to lifestyle changes\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary discomfort during posture correction\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete symptom relief if habits continue\"},{\"value\":\"Slow improvement in chronic conditions\"},{\"value\":\"Risk of recurrence without long-term compliance\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:81:\"<p>Ergonomic correction can significantly reduce pain and prevent recurrence.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:66:\"<p>Activity modification improves long-term orthopedic health.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:46:\"Activity Modification and Ergonomic Correction\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:59:\"Learn about ergonomic correction and activity modification.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:41:\"ergonomic correction, posture improvement\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-12 11:38:48\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-12 16:24:16\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";