;s:326:\"Antacids quickly neutralize stomach acid, while mucosal protectants coat the stomach lining and promote healing. These therapies are commonly used for: Gastritis Acid reflux Peptic ulcer disease Indigestion Gastric irritation from medications They are often used along with lifestyle modification and acid-suppressing therapy.\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:178:\"[{\"value\":\"Burning sensation in chest or stomach\"},{\"value\":\"Acid indigestion\"},{\"value\":\"Nausea after meals\"},{\"value\":\"Gastric discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Mild ulcer-related pain\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:221:\"[{\"value\":\"Constipation or diarrhea\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance with overuse\"},{\"value\":\"Drug interaction with other medications\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary symptom masking\"},{\"value\":\"Rare kidney-related complications\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:230:\"[{\"value\":\"Avoid overeating and spicy foods\"},{\"value\":\"Use medications only as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain adequate hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid smoking and alcohol intake\"},{\"value\":\"Seek medical review if symptoms persist\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:221:\"[{\"value\":\"Constipation or diarrhea\"},{\"value\":\"Electrolyte imbalance with overuse\"},{\"value\":\"Drug interaction with other medications\"},{\"value\":\"Temporary symptom masking\"},{\"value\":\"Rare kidney-related complications\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:135:\"These medications effectively relieve gastric discomfort, support ulcer healing, and improve digestive comfort when used appropriately.\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:30:\"Antacids / Mucosal Protectants\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:213:\"Antacids and mucosal protectants are medications used to neutralize stomach acid and protect the digestiv