-be94b579a9f2.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:40:\"antibiotic-and-anti-inflammatory-therapy\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:358:\"Antibiotic and anti-inflammatory therapy is a medical treatment used in ENT disorders to control infections, reduce swelling, relieve pain, and promote healing. The therapy is commonly used for ear infections, sinusitis, tonsillitis, throat infections, and inflammatory ENT conditions. Proper treatment helps prevent progression of disease and complications.\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:463:\"The treatment plan depends on the type of infection and severity of inflammation. Antibiotics target bacterial infections, while anti-inflammatory medications reduce tissue swelling, pain, redness, and irritation. Therapy may include: Oral medications Injectable antibiotics Nasal sprays Ear drops Gargles or topical medications ENT specialists carefully select medications based on patient age, allergy history, infection type, and associated medical conditions.\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:169:\"[{\"value\":\"Fever and infection symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Ear or throat pain\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling and redness\"},{\"value\":\"Nasal congestion\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty swallowing\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:207:\"[{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Stomach irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete infection control if treatment is interrupted\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:248:\"[{\"value\":\"Take medications exactly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Complete the entire antibiotic course\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain adequate hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid self-medication without medical advice\"},{\"value\":\"Report allergic symptoms immediately\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:207:\"[{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Stomach irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete infection control if treatment is interrupted\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:158:\"Appropriate antibiotic and anti-inflammatory therapy effectively controls ENT infections and reduces recurrence or long-term complications when used properly.\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:40:\"Antibiotic and Anti-Inflammatory Therapy\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:358:\"Antibiotic and anti-inflammatory therapy is a medical treatment used in ENT disorders to control infections, reduce swelling, relieve pain, and promote healing. The therapy is commonly used for ear infections, sinusitis, tonsillitis, throat infections, and inflammatory ENT conditions. Proper treatment helps prevent progression of disease and complications.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 07:03:49\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 12:37:28\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:271;s:5:\"title\";s:40:\"Antibiotic and Anti-Inflammatory Therapy\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/f11cb042-60c8-4761-83c2-be94b579a9f2.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";N;s:4:\"slug\";s:40:\"antibiotic-and-anti-inflammatory-therapy\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:358:\"Antibiotic and anti-inflammatory therapy is a medical treatment used in ENT disorders to control infections, reduce swelling, relieve pain, and promote healing. The therapy is commonly used for ear infections, sinusitis, tonsillitis, throat infections, and inflammatory ENT conditions. Proper treatment helps prevent progression of disease and complications.\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:463:\"The treatment plan depends on the type of infection and severity of inflammation. Antibiotics target bacterial infections, while anti-inflammatory medications reduce tissue swelling, pain, redness, and irritation. Therapy may include: Oral medications Injectable antibiotics Nasal sprays Ear drops Gargles or topical medications ENT specialists carefully select medications based on patient age, allergy history, infection type, and associated medical conditions.\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:169:\"[{\"value\":\"Fever and infection symptoms\"},{\"value\":\"Ear or throat pain\"},{\"value\":\"Swelling and redness\"},{\"value\":\"Nasal congestion\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty swallowing\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:207:\"[{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Stomach irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete infection control if treatment is interrupted\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:2:\"[]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:0:\"\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:248:\"[{\"value\":\"Take medications exactly as prescribed\"},{\"value\":\"Complete the entire antibiotic course\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain adequate hydration\"},{\"value\":\"Avoid self-medication without medical advice\"},{\"value\":\"Report allergic symptoms immediately\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:207:\"[{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Stomach irritation\"},{\"value\":\"Medication side effects\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete infection control if treatment is interrupted\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:158:\"Appropriate antibiotic and anti-inflammatory therapy effectively controls ENT infections and reduces recurrence or long-term complications when used properly.\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:40:\"Antibiotic and Anti-Inflammatory Therapy\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:358:\"Antibiotic and anti-inflammatory therapy is a medical treatment used in ENT disorders to control infections, reduce swelling, relieve pain, and promote healing. The therapy is commonly used for ear infections, sinusitis, tonsillitis, throat infections, and inflammatory ENT conditions. Proper treatment helps prevent progression of disease and complications.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:0:\"\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 07:03:49\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-18 12:37:28\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:9;O:20:\"App\\Models\\Procedure\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:10:\"procedures\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:204;s:5:\"title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/8af12096-3c95-4bf1-8a9d-afc174649736.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:74:\"procedures/banners/relatedimages/989c2a28-2c1c-4a55-a387-00a199d8c2b4.webp\";s:4:\"slug\";s:18:\"antibiotic-therapy\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:159:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is a medical treatment used to manage bacterial infections in children using medications that kill or inhibit the growth of bacteria.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:111:\"<p>Antibiotics play an important role in treating serious bacterial illnesses and preventing complications.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:180:\"[{\"value\":\"High fever\"},{\"value\":\"Bacterial throat infection\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent cough with infection\"},{\"value\":\"Painful urination\"},{\"value\":\"Skin swelling or pus formation\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:187:\"[{\"value\":\"Culture sensitivity testing\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Urine testing\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical infection assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory infection evaluation\"}]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:141:\"<p>Doctors select antibiotics based on clinical findings, laboratory reports, culture sensitivity tests, and suspected infection sources.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:237:\"[{\"value\":\"Complete the full antibiotic course\"},{\"value\":\"Follow dosage instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration and nutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up evaluations if needed\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:119:\"<p>Proper antibiotic therapy effectively treats bacterial infections and prevents severe complications in children.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:100:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is essential for managing bacterial infections and reducing complications.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:75:\"Learn about antibiotic therapy and pediatric bacterial infection treatment.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:72:\"antibiotic therapy, pediatric antibiotics, bacterial infection treatment\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 15:59:51\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 16:13:29\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:26:{s:2:\"id\";i:204;s:5:\"title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:60:\"procedures/banners/8af12096-3c95-4bf1-8a9d-afc174649736.webp\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:74:\"procedures/banners/relatedimages/989c2a28-2c1c-4a55-a387-00a199d8c2b4.webp\";s:4:\"slug\";s:18:\"antibiotic-therapy\";s:12:\"introduction\";s:159:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is a medical treatment used to manage bacterial infections in children using medications that kill or inhibit the growth of bacteria.</p>\";s:7:\"what_is\";s:111:\"<p>Antibiotics play an important role in treating serious bacterial illnesses and preventing complications.</p>\";s:8:\"symptoms\";s:180:\"[{\"value\":\"High fever\"},{\"value\":\"Bacterial throat infection\"},{\"value\":\"Persistent cough with infection\"},{\"value\":\"Painful urination\"},{\"value\":\"Skin swelling or pus formation\"}]\";s:6:\"causes\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:2:\"[]\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:187:\"[{\"value\":\"Culture sensitivity testing\"},{\"value\":\"Blood investigations\"},{\"value\":\"Urine testing\"},{\"value\":\"Clinical infection assessment\"},{\"value\":\"Respiratory infection evaluation\"}]\";s:18:\"treatment_overview\";s:141:\"<p>Doctors select antibiotics based on clinical findings, laboratory reports, culture sensitivity tests, and suspected infection sources.</p>\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:2:\"[]\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:2:\"[]\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:237:\"[{\"value\":\"Complete the full antibiotic course\"},{\"value\":\"Follow dosage instructions carefully\"},{\"value\":\"Monitor for allergic reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Maintain hydration and nutrition\"},{\"value\":\"Attend follow-up evaluations if needed\"}]\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:193:\"[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic resistance\"},{\"value\":\"Allergic drug reactions\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or stomach upset\"},{\"value\":\"Incorrect antibiotic use\"},{\"value\":\"Incomplete treatment complications\"}]\";s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";s:119:\"<p>Proper antibiotic therapy effectively treats bacterial infections and prevents severe complications in children.</p>\";s:10:\"conclusion\";s:100:\"<p>Antibiotic therapy is essential for managing bacterial infections and reducing complications.</p>\";s:9:\"seo_title\";s:18:\"Antibiotic Therapy\";s:15:\"seo_description\";s:75:\"Learn about antibiotic therapy and pediatric bacterial infection treatment.\";s:12:\"seo_keywords\";s:72:\"antibiotic therapy, pediatric antibiotics, bacterial infection treatment\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 15:59:51\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-05-15 16:13:29\";s:2:\"h1\";N;}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:10:{s:8:\"symptoms\";s:5:\"array\";s:6:\"causes\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"condition_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:11:\"preventions\";s:5:\"array\";s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_types\";s:5:\"array\";s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";s:5:\"array\";s:12:\"post_op_care\";s:5:\"array\";s:13:\"surgery_risks\";s:5:\"array\";s:9:\"is_active\";s:7:\"boolean\";}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:23:{i:0;s:5:\"title\";i:1;s:2:\"h1\";i:2;s:4:\"slug\";i:3;s:12:\"introduction\";i:4;s:7:\"what_is\";i:5;s:8:\"symptoms\";i:6;s:6:\"causes\";i:7;s:15:\"condition_risks\";i:8;s:11:\"preventions\";i:9;s:15:\"diagnosis_tests\";i:10;s:18:\"treatment_overview\";i:11;s:13:\"surgery_types\";i:12;s:17:\"recovery_timeline\";i:13;s:12:\"post_op_care\";i:14;s:13:\"surgery_risks\";i:15;s:17:\"long_term_outlook\";i:16;s:10:\"conclusion\";i:17;s:9:\"seo_title\";i:18;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:19;s:13:\"related_image\";i:20;s:15:\"seo_description\";i:21;s:12:\"seo_keywords\";i:22;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}}s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;}s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:10;s:14:\"\0*\0currentPage\";i:3;s:7:\"\0*\0path\";s:32:\"http://127.0.0.1:8000/procedures\";s:8:\"\0*\0query\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fragment\";N;s:11:\"\0*\0pageName\";s:4:\"page\";s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:10:\"onEachSide\";i:3;s:10:\"\0*\0options\";a:2:{s:4:\"path\";s:32:\"http://127.0.0.1:8000/procedures\";s:8:\"pageName\";s:4:\"page\";}s:8:\"\0*\0total\";i:798;s:11:\"\0*\0lastPage\";i:80;}',1785306272);
INSERT INTO `cache` VALUES ('laravel-cache-content:v17:specialities:active','O:39:\"Illuminate\\Database\\Eloquent\\Collection\":2:{s:8:\"\0*\0items\";a:26:{i:0;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:5;s:4:\"name\";s:22:\"Cardiology(heart care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:10:\"heart-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/d4b79b00-5783-4b32-b927-54cde29747bd.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8CGZ01K9DDBXQ95FXYXRV.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:569:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a trusted cardiology and heart care hospital in Bangalore, offering specialised services for the prevention, early detection, and treatment of all heart-related conditions. Heart disease — including coronary artery disease, hypertension, heart failure, and arrhythmia — often develops silently before warning signs like chest pain, breathlessness, palpitations, or fatigue appear. Our experienced cardiologists in Bangalore ensure cardiac risk is identified and treated at the earliest stage, before it becomes a life-threatening emergency.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:937:\"<p>The cardiology department at Nano Hospitals Bangalore is equipped with advanced diagnostics including ECG, 2D Echocardiography, and cardiac risk profiling for patients with diabetes, high blood pressure, obesity, or a family history of heart disease. Each patient receives a personalised, evidence-based heart treatment plan tailored to their age, lifestyle, and condition — with the department working in close coordination with Emergency, ICU, and General Medicine teams for seamless, round-the-clock cardiac care.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, heart care goes beyond symptom relief — the focus is on long-term cardiovascular health and disease prevention. Whether you need a cardiac health check-up in Bangalore, treatment for hypertension, or ongoing management of a diagnosed heart condition, our cardiologists provide clear, personalised guidance at every step — from first consultation to long-term follow-up and recovery.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:345:\"<p>Heart Care focuses on identifying and managing cardiovascular risks early, before complications arise. Timely cardiac evaluation plays a crucial role in preventing life-threatening events.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, cardiology services are integrated with emergency and critical care systems to ensure rapid response and continuity of care.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:888:\"<h3><strong>Cardiac Diagnostic Services</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Electrocardiogram (ECG) for rhythm assessment</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography for heart structure and function</p></li><li><p>Cardiac risk profiling and clinical evaluation</p></li><li><p>Monitoring of heart function in medical and surgical patients</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Medical Management</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Hypertension management</p></li><li><p>Heart failure medical treatment</p></li><li><p>Arrhythmia management</p></li><li><p>Medical treatment for coronary artery disease</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Preventive &amp; Emergency Cardiac Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Cardiac risk assessment and lifestyle counselling</p></li><li><p>Monitoring high-risk patients (diabetes, obesity, family history)</p></li><li><p>Immediate evaluation of chest pain</p></li><li><p>Cardiac monitoring in ICU and wards</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:370:\"<ul><li><p>ECG machines for rapid rhythm assessment</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography systems</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory medicine for cardiac markers</p></li><li><p>ICU and emergency services for continuous monitoring</p></li><li><p>Digital X-Ray, CT, and MRI support when required</p></li><li><p>24×7 pharmacy for uninterrupted medication access</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:349:\"<ul><li><p>Hypertension and coronary artery disease</p></li><li><p>Heart rhythm disorders and heart failure</p></li><li><p>Chest pain, breathlessness, palpitations</p></li><li><p>Dizziness or fainting episodes</p></li><li><p>Cardiac involvement in diabetes and kidney disease</p></li><li><p>Pre-operative cardiac assessment for surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:223:\"<ul><li><p>Early detection over late intervention</p></li><li><p>Evidence-based medical management</p></li><li><p>Patient education and lifestyle modification</p></li><li><p>Continuous monitoring and follow-up</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:174:\"<ul><li><p>Preventive Cardiology</p></li><li><p>Heart Failure Management</p></li><li><p>Medical Cardiology</p></li><li><p>Cardiac Risk Assessment and Monitoring</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:67:\"Best Heart Care & Cardiology Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:258:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted cardiology and heart care hospital in Bangalore offering expert diagnosis and treatment for heart disease, hypertension, arrhythmia, heart failure, and chest pain. Consult experienced cardiologists — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:14:30\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:16:18\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/a7cdc4e0-1622-45f5-8253-216e12293df9.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:5;s:4:\"name\";s:22:\"Cardiology(heart care)\";s:4:\"slug\";s:10:\"heart-care\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/d4b79b00-5783-4b32-b927-54cde29747bd.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8CGZ01K9DDBXQ95FXYXRV.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:569:\"<p>Nano Hospitals is a trusted cardiology and heart care hospital in Bangalore, offering specialised services for the prevention, early detection, and treatment of all heart-related conditions. Heart disease — including coronary artery disease, hypertension, heart failure, and arrhythmia — often develops silently before warning signs like chest pain, breathlessness, palpitations, or fatigue appear. Our experienced cardiologists in Bangalore ensure cardiac risk is identified and treated at the earliest stage, before it becomes a life-threatening emergency.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:937:\"<p>The cardiology department at Nano Hospitals Bangalore is equipped with advanced diagnostics including ECG, 2D Echocardiography, and cardiac risk profiling for patients with diabetes, high blood pressure, obesity, or a family history of heart disease. Each patient receives a personalised, evidence-based heart treatment plan tailored to their age, lifestyle, and condition — with the department working in close coordination with Emergency, ICU, and General Medicine teams for seamless, round-the-clock cardiac care.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, heart care goes beyond symptom relief — the focus is on long-term cardiovascular health and disease prevention. Whether you need a cardiac health check-up in Bangalore, treatment for hypertension, or ongoing management of a diagnosed heart condition, our cardiologists provide clear, personalised guidance at every step — from first consultation to long-term follow-up and recovery.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:345:\"<p>Heart Care focuses on identifying and managing cardiovascular risks early, before complications arise. Timely cardiac evaluation plays a crucial role in preventing life-threatening events.</p><p>At Nano Hospitals, cardiology services are integrated with emergency and critical care systems to ensure rapid response and continuity of care.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:888:\"<h3><strong>Cardiac Diagnostic Services</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Electrocardiogram (ECG) for rhythm assessment</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography for heart structure and function</p></li><li><p>Cardiac risk profiling and clinical evaluation</p></li><li><p>Monitoring of heart function in medical and surgical patients</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Medical Management</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Hypertension management</p></li><li><p>Heart failure medical treatment</p></li><li><p>Arrhythmia management</p></li><li><p>Medical treatment for coronary artery disease</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Preventive &amp; Emergency Cardiac Care</strong></h3><ul><li><p>Cardiac risk assessment and lifestyle counselling</p></li><li><p>Monitoring high-risk patients (diabetes, obesity, family history)</p></li><li><p>Immediate evaluation of chest pain</p></li><li><p>Cardiac monitoring in ICU and wards</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:370:\"<ul><li><p>ECG machines for rapid rhythm assessment</p></li><li><p>2D Echocardiography systems</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory medicine for cardiac markers</p></li><li><p>ICU and emergency services for continuous monitoring</p></li><li><p>Digital X-Ray, CT, and MRI support when required</p></li><li><p>24×7 pharmacy for uninterrupted medication access</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:349:\"<ul><li><p>Hypertension and coronary artery disease</p></li><li><p>Heart rhythm disorders and heart failure</p></li><li><p>Chest pain, breathlessness, palpitations</p></li><li><p>Dizziness or fainting episodes</p></li><li><p>Cardiac involvement in diabetes and kidney disease</p></li><li><p>Pre-operative cardiac assessment for surgery</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:223:\"<ul><li><p>Early detection over late intervention</p></li><li><p>Evidence-based medical management</p></li><li><p>Patient education and lifestyle modification</p></li><li><p>Continuous monitoring and follow-up</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:174:\"<ul><li><p>Preventive Cardiology</p></li><li><p>Heart Failure Management</p></li><li><p>Medical Cardiology</p></li><li><p>Cardiac Risk Assessment and Monitoring</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:67:\"Best Heart Care & Cardiology Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:258:\"Nano Hospitals is a trusted cardiology and heart care hospital in Bangalore offering expert diagnosis and treatment for heart disease, hypertension, arrhythmia, heart failure, and chest pain. Consult experienced cardiologists — book your appointment today.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:14:30\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-06-12 13:16:18\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/a7cdc4e0-1622-45f5-8253-216e12293df9.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:1;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:13;s:4:\"name\";s:11:\"Dermatology\";s:4:\"slug\";s:11:\"dermatology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/33f1af24-e94c-4e94-b63b-96a7342e4fab.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8FYYNHKB9GR2ZA7Q7X83V.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:268:\"<p>Dermatology at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of conditions affecting the skin, hair, and nails. The department manages medical, surgical, and cosmetic dermatological concerns across all age groups.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:658:\"<p>Skin problems may begin with mild symptoms such as itching, rashes, acne, pigmentation, or hair thinning, but can progress to chronic infections, scarring, or systemic disease manifestations if left untreated. At Nano Hospitals, care aims not only to relieve visible symptoms but also to identify underlying causes and restore healthy skin function and appearance.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, dermatoscopic assessment, laboratory support, procedural dermatology, and long-term skincare guidance. Each care plan is tailored according to skin type, condition severity, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:375:\"<p>Dermatology deals with disorders of the skin, hair, nails, and related mucous membranes. Early symptoms such as persistent itching, discoloration, unusual moles, hair loss, or non-healing skin lesions should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis, targeted treatment, and preventive skincare education to maintain long-term skin health.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1015:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical treatment for acne, eczema, and psoriasis</p></li><li><p>Allergy and skin infection management</p></li><li><p>Pigmentation disorder treatment</p></li><li><p>Hair loss evaluation and medical therapy</p></li><li><p>Nail infection and disorder treatment</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Chemical peels for pigmentation and acne scars</p></li><li><p>Cryotherapy for warts and small lesions</p></li><li><p>Intralesional injections for keloids and alopecia</p></li><li><p>PRP (Platelet-Rich Plasma) therapy for hair restoration</p></li><li><p>Dermatoscopic mole evaluation</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical &amp; Advanced Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Minor skin surgeries for cysts and benign growths</p></li><li><p>Skin biopsies for diagnosis</p></li><li><p>Mole and skin lesion removal</p></li><li><p>Laser treatments for scars, pigmentation, and vascular lesions</p></li><li><p>Treatment of skin cancers (in coordination with oncology)</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:342:\"<ul><li><p>Dermatoscopy for detailed skin lesion analysis</p></li><li><p>Laser therapy systems for skin and hair treatments</p></li><li><p>Cryotherapy units</p></li><li><p>Minor procedure rooms for dermatologic surgery</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory support for skin testing</p></li><li><p>Allergy and patch testing services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:410:\"<ul><li><p>Acne and acne scars</p></li><li><p>Eczema and dermatitis</p></li><li><p>Psoriasis</p></li><li><p>Fungal, bacterial, and viral skin infections</p></li><li><p>Pigmentation disorders (melasma, vitiligo)</p></li><li><p>Hair loss and scalp disorders</p></li><li><p>Nail infections and deformities</p></li><li><p>Skin allergies and urticaria</p></li><li><p>Benign and suspicious skin growths</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:300:\"<ul><li><p>Chronic recurrence in conditions like eczema and psoriasis</p></li><li><p>Risk of scarring without timely treatment</p></li><li><p>Spread of untreated infections</p></li><li><p>Cosmetic concerns affecting self-confidence</p></li><li><p>Need for long-term skincare maintenance</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:195:\"<ul><li><p>Medical Dermatology</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Dermatology</p></li><li><p>Cosmetic Dermatology</p></li><li><p>Dermatosurgery</p></li><li><p>Trichology (Hair and Scalp Care)</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:55:\"Best Dermatology Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:150:\"Nano Hospitals offers advanced Dermatology services in Bangalore for acne, pigmentation, hair loss, and other skin conditions with expert specialists.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:46:27\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:29:59\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/8fed089e-c444-42eb-97fc-8537abb40dad.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:13;s:4:\"name\";s:11:\"Dermatology\";s:4:\"slug\";s:11:\"dermatology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/33f1af24-e94c-4e94-b63b-96a7342e4fab.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8FYYNHKB9GR2ZA7Q7X83V.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:268:\"<p>Dermatology at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of conditions affecting the skin, hair, and nails. The department manages medical, surgical, and cosmetic dermatological concerns across all age groups.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:658:\"<p>Skin problems may begin with mild symptoms such as itching, rashes, acne, pigmentation, or hair thinning, but can progress to chronic infections, scarring, or systemic disease manifestations if left untreated. At Nano Hospitals, care aims not only to relieve visible symptoms but also to identify underlying causes and restore healthy skin function and appearance.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, dermatoscopic assessment, laboratory support, procedural dermatology, and long-term skincare guidance. Each care plan is tailored according to skin type, condition severity, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:375:\"<p>Dermatology deals with disorders of the skin, hair, nails, and related mucous membranes. Early symptoms such as persistent itching, discoloration, unusual moles, hair loss, or non-healing skin lesions should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis, targeted treatment, and preventive skincare education to maintain long-term skin health.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1015:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical treatment for acne, eczema, and psoriasis</p></li><li><p>Allergy and skin infection management</p></li><li><p>Pigmentation disorder treatment</p></li><li><p>Hair loss evaluation and medical therapy</p></li><li><p>Nail infection and disorder treatment</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Chemical peels for pigmentation and acne scars</p></li><li><p>Cryotherapy for warts and small lesions</p></li><li><p>Intralesional injections for keloids and alopecia</p></li><li><p>PRP (Platelet-Rich Plasma) therapy for hair restoration</p></li><li><p>Dermatoscopic mole evaluation</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical &amp; Advanced Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Minor skin surgeries for cysts and benign growths</p></li><li><p>Skin biopsies for diagnosis</p></li><li><p>Mole and skin lesion removal</p></li><li><p>Laser treatments for scars, pigmentation, and vascular lesions</p></li><li><p>Treatment of skin cancers (in coordination with oncology)</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:342:\"<ul><li><p>Dermatoscopy for detailed skin lesion analysis</p></li><li><p>Laser therapy systems for skin and hair treatments</p></li><li><p>Cryotherapy units</p></li><li><p>Minor procedure rooms for dermatologic surgery</p></li><li><p>Advanced laboratory support for skin testing</p></li><li><p>Allergy and patch testing services</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:410:\"<ul><li><p>Acne and acne scars</p></li><li><p>Eczema and dermatitis</p></li><li><p>Psoriasis</p></li><li><p>Fungal, bacterial, and viral skin infections</p></li><li><p>Pigmentation disorders (melasma, vitiligo)</p></li><li><p>Hair loss and scalp disorders</p></li><li><p>Nail infections and deformities</p></li><li><p>Skin allergies and urticaria</p></li><li><p>Benign and suspicious skin growths</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:300:\"<ul><li><p>Chronic recurrence in conditions like eczema and psoriasis</p></li><li><p>Risk of scarring without timely treatment</p></li><li><p>Spread of untreated infections</p></li><li><p>Cosmetic concerns affecting self-confidence</p></li><li><p>Need for long-term skincare maintenance</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:195:\"<ul><li><p>Medical Dermatology</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Dermatology</p></li><li><p>Cosmetic Dermatology</p></li><li><p>Dermatosurgery</p></li><li><p>Trichology (Hair and Scalp Care)</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:55:\"Best Dermatology Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:150:\"Nano Hospitals offers advanced Dermatology services in Bangalore for acne, pigmentation, hair loss, and other skin conditions with expert specialists.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:46:27\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:29:59\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/8fed089e-c444-42eb-97fc-8537abb40dad.webp\";}s:10:\"\0*\0changes\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0previous\";a:0:{}s:8:\"\0*\0casts\";a:0:{}s:17:\"\0*\0classCastCache\";a:0:{}s:21:\"\0*\0attributeCastCache\";a:0:{}s:13:\"\0*\0dateFormat\";N;s:10:\"\0*\0appends\";a:0:{}s:19:\"\0*\0dispatchesEvents\";a:0:{}s:14:\"\0*\0observables\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0relations\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0touches\";a:0:{}s:27:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadCallback\";N;s:26:\"\0*\0relationAutoloadContext\";N;s:10:\"timestamps\";b:1;s:13:\"usesUniqueIds\";b:0;s:9:\"\0*\0hidden\";a:0:{}s:10:\"\0*\0visible\";a:0:{}s:11:\"\0*\0fillable\";a:16:{i:0;s:4:\"name\";i:1;s:4:\"slug\";i:2;s:12:\"banner_image\";i:3;s:4:\"icon\";i:4;s:13:\"related_image\";i:5;s:11:\"about_intro\";i:6;s:10:\"about_more\";i:7;s:16:\"overview_content\";i:8;s:18:\"treatments_content\";i:9;s:18:\"facilities_content\";i:10;s:18:\"conditions_content\";i:11;s:13:\"risks_content\";i:12;s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";i:13;s:10:\"meta_title\";i:14;s:16:\"meta_description\";i:15;s:9:\"is_active\";}s:10:\"\0*\0guarded\";a:1:{i:0;s:1:\"*\";}s:16:\"\0*\0scoutMetadata\";a:0:{}}i:2;O:21:\"App\\Models\\Speciality\":34:{s:13:\"\0*\0connection\";s:5:\"mysql\";s:8:\"\0*\0table\";s:12:\"specialities\";s:13:\"\0*\0primaryKey\";s:2:\"id\";s:10:\"\0*\0keyType\";s:3:\"int\";s:12:\"incrementing\";b:1;s:7:\"\0*\0with\";a:0:{}s:12:\"\0*\0withCount\";a:0:{}s:19:\"preventsLazyLoading\";b:0;s:10:\"\0*\0perPage\";i:15;s:6:\"exists\";b:1;s:18:\"wasRecentlyCreated\";b:0;s:28:\"\0*\0escapeWhenCastingToString\";b:0;s:13:\"\0*\0attributes\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:10;s:4:\"name\";s:27:\"Diabetology & Endocrinology\";s:4:\"slug\";s:25:\"diabetology-endocrinology\";s:12:\"banner_image\";s:62:\"specialities/banners/aa2fba41-cb73-4339-b7e5-547c4dfb1507.webp\";s:4:\"icon\";s:50:\"specialities/icons/01KGJ8DX2W3E0QMVZEGKA6NVQF.webp\";s:9:\"is_active\";i:1;s:11:\"about_intro\";s:280:\"<p>Diabetology &amp; Endocrinology at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of endocrine disorders — conditions caused by imbalance of hormones that regulate metabolism, growth, reproduction, and overall body function.</p>\";s:10:\"about_more\";s:737:\"<p>Hormonal problems often develop gradually, with symptoms such as unexplained weight changes, fatigue, excessive thirst, frequent urination, mood fluctuations, menstrual irregularities, or growth concerns. If left untreated, these disorders can affect the heart, kidneys, nerves, bones, and reproductive health. At Nano Hospitals, care is aimed not only at controlling symptoms but also at restoring hormonal balance and preventing long-term complications.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining laboratory evaluation, advanced imaging, medication management, lifestyle guidance, and continuous monitoring. Each care plan is individualised based on age, gender, lifestyle, and the specific hormonal condition.</p>\";s:16:\"overview_content\";s:459:\"<p>This specialty (Endocrinology) deals with disorders of hormone-producing glands such as the pancreas, thyroid, adrenal glands, pituitary gland, and reproductive glands. Early detection of hormonal imbalance is essential, as many endocrine conditions silently damage organs over time.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early screening, precise diagnosis, personalised medication plans, and long-term follow-up to maintain metabolic and hormonal stability.</p>\";s:18:\"treatments_content\";s:1017:\"<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Diabetes management with oral medications and insulin therapy</p></li><li><p>Continuous glucose monitoring guidance</p></li><li><p>Thyroid disorder management (hypothyroidism and hyperthyroidism)</p></li><li><p>Hormone therapy for adrenal and pituitary disorders</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle and dietary counselling for metabolic health</p></li><li><p>Bone health and osteoporosis management</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Fine-needle aspiration (FNA) for thyroid nodules</p></li><li><p>Hormone level testing with dynamic endocrine evaluations</p></li><li><p>Image-guided procedures for certain gland-related conditions</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Thyroid surgery for nodules, goiter, or thyroid cancer</p></li><li><p>Adrenal gland surgery for hormone-secreting tumors</p></li><li><p>Pituitary gland surgery (in coordination with neurosurgery)</p></li><li><p>Parathyroid surgery for calcium imbalance disorder</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"facilities_content\";s:407:\"<ul><li><p>Advanced hormone laboratory testing</p></li><li><p>Continuous glucose monitoring systems</p></li><li><p>Thyroid ultrasound imaging</p></li><li><p>CT Scan and MRI for endocrine gland evaluation</p></li><li><p>Bone density scan (DEXA) for osteoporosis detection</p></li><li><p>Dedicated diabetes education and counselling support</p></li><li><p>Long-term metabolic monitoring programs</p></li></ul>\";s:18:\"conditions_content\";s:440:\"<ul><li><p>Type 1 and Type 2 Diabetes</p></li><li><p>Gestational diabetes</p></li><li><p>Thyroid disorders (hypothyroidism, hyperthyroidism, nodules)</p></li><li><p>Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS)</p></li><li><p>Obesity and metabolic syndrome</p></li><li><p>Osteoporosis and calcium disorders</p></li><li><p>Pituitary gland disorders</p></li><li><p>Adrenal gland disorders</p></li><li><p>Hormonal growth and puberty disorders</p></li></ul>\";s:13:\"risks_content\";s:302:\"<ul><li><p>Organ damage from uncontrolled diabetes</p></li><li><p>Heart, kidney, and nerve complications</p></li><li><p>Hormonal imbalances affecting fertility and growth</p></li><li><p>Bone loss leading to fractures</p></li><li><p>Lifelong monitoring needed for many endocrine conditions</p></li></ul>\";s:22:\"subspecialties_content\";s:233:\"<ul><li><p>Diabetology and Metabolic Care</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and Parathyroid Disorders</p></li><li><p>Reproductive Endocrinology</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Endocrinology</p></li><li><p>Bone and Mineral Metabolism Care</p></li></ul>\";s:10:\"meta_title\";s:57:\"Diabetology & Endocrinology in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals\";s:16:\"meta_description\";s:160:\"Nano Hospitals offers expert diabetes and hormone care in Bangalore with specialized endocrinologists for diabetes, thyroid, PCOS, and other hormonal disorders.\";s:10:\"created_at\";s:19:\"2026-02-02 17:32:01\";s:10:\"updated_at\";s:19:\"2026-04-21 13:06:53\";s:13:\"related_image\";s:76:\"specialities/banners/relatedimages/ad21344f-1601-4dfa-bb47-5105d2c9beed.webp\";}s:11:\"\0*\0original\";a:19:{s:2:\"id\";i:10;s:4:\"name\";s:27:\"Diabetology & Endo