INSERT INTO `condition_faqs` VALUES (1,1,'What is hypertension and what are its main causes?','Hypertension is a chronic condition where blood pressure consistently reads above 130/80 mmHg. Main causes include unhealthy diet, physical inactivity, obesity, stress, smoking, excessive alcohol consumption, and genetic factors.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(2,1,'What are the warning signs of high blood pressure?','Hypertension is often called the \"silent killer\" as it rarely shows symptoms. However, some patients may experience severe headaches, dizziness, blurred vision, chest pain, and shortness of breath in advanced stages.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(3,1,'How is hypertension diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, hypertension is diagnosed through regular blood pressure monitoring, blood tests, urine tests, ECG, echocardiogram, and 24-hour ambulatory blood pressure monitoring for accurate assessment.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(4,1,'What are the best treatment options for hypertension in Bangalore?','The best hypertension treatment in Bangalore includes lifestyle modifications, dietary changes, regular exercise, stress management, and antihypertensive medications prescribed by our experienced cardiologists at Nano Hospitals.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(5,1,'Can hypertension be completely cured?','While hypertension cannot always be completely cured, it can be effectively controlled with the right treatment plan, regular monitoring, and healthy lifestyle changes under the guidance of our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(6,1,'What complications can arise from untreated hypertension?','Untreated hypertension can lead to serious complications including heart attack, stroke, kidney failure, heart failure, vision loss, and peripheral artery disease, making timely treatment absolutely critical.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(7,1,'is hypertension treatment available for elderly patients in Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers specialized hypertension management programs for elderly patients, with customized treatment plans that consider age-related health factors and co-existing medical conditions.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(8,1,'What lifestyle changes help control high blood pressure?','Key lifestyle changes include reducing salt intake, following a DASH diet, regular physical activity, maintaining healthy weight, quitting smoking, limiting alcohol, and managing stress through yoga and meditation.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(9,1,'How often should I get my blood pressure checked in Bangalore?','Adults above 18 should get blood pressure checked at least once a year. Patients with existing hypertension or risk factors should monitor blood pressure more frequently as advised by our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(10,1,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for hypertension treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best hypertension care with experienced cardiologists, advanced diagnostic technology, personalized treatment plans, and comprehensive follow-up care for long-term blood pressure management.',0,'2026-06-11 12:40:19','2026-06-11 12:40:19'),(11,2,' What is diabetes and what are its main types?','Diabetes is a chronic metabolic disorder characterized by high blood sugar levels. The main types include Type 1 diabetes (insulin deficiency), Type 2 diabetes (insulin resistance), and gestational diabetes occurring during pregnancy.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(12,2,'What are the early symptoms of diabetes?','Early symptoms of diabetes include frequent urination, excessive thirst, unexplained weight loss, fatigue, blurred vision, slow wound healing, frequent infections, and tingling or numbness in hands and feet.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(13,2,'How is diabetes diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, diabetes is diagnosed through fasting blood sugar test, postprandial blood sugar test, HbA1c test, oral glucose tolerance test, and comprehensive metabolic panel for accurate assessment and staging.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(14,2,'What are the best diabetes treatment options in Bangalore?','The best diabetes treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes dietary management, physical activity plans, oral hypoglycemic medications, insulin therapy, continuous glucose monitoring, and comprehensive diabetes education programs.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(15,2,'Can Type 2 diabetes be reversed in Bangalore?','Type 2 diabetes can be significantly improved and even reversed in early stages through aggressive lifestyle modifications, dietary changes, weight management, and medical supervision at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(16,2,'What complications can arise from uncontrolled diabetes?','Uncontrolled diabetes can lead to serious complications including diabetic neuropathy, nephropathy, retinopathy, cardiovascular disease, foot ulcers, and increased risk of infections requiring urgent medical attention.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(17,2,'Is diabetes management available for children at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized pediatric diabetes care for children with Type 1 and Type 2 diabetes, with age-appropriate treatment plans, dietary guidance, and family education programs.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(18,2,'What diet should a diabetic patient follow in Bangalore?','A diabetic patient should follow a low glycemic index diet rich in vegetables, whole grains, lean proteins, and healthy fats while avoiding sugary foods, refined carbohydrates, and processed foods as advised by our dietitians at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(19,2,'How often should diabetic patients visit Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Q9. How often should diabetic patients visit Nano Hospitals Bangalore?\nDiabetic patients should visit their specialist every 3 months for HbA1c monitoring, annual eye examinations, kidney function tests, foot examinations, and cardiovascular risk assessment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(20,2,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for diabetes treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best diabetes care with experienced endocrinologists, diabetologists, dietitians, and a comprehensive diabetes management program designed for long-term blood sugar control and complication prevention.',0,'2026-06-11 12:43:54','2026-06-11 12:43:54'),(21,6,'What is osteoarthritis and how does it differ from rheumatoid arthritis?','Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint disease caused by cartilage breakdown due to wear and tear, primarily affecting older adults. Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition causing joint inflammation, affecting younger patients and multiple joints simultaneously.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(22,6,' What are the most common symptoms of osteoarthritis?','Common osteoarthritis symptoms include persistent joint pain, stiffness especially in the morning, swelling, reduced range of motion, clicking or grinding sensation in joints, and progressive difficulty performing daily activities.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(23,6,'How is osteoarthritis diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, osteoarthritis is diagnosed through detailed clinical examination, X-rays, MRI scans, joint fluid analysis, and blood tests to accurately assess the severity of cartilage degeneration and joint damage.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(24,6,'What are the best osteoarthritis treatment options in Bangalore?','The best osteoarthritis treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes physiotherapy, pain management, anti-inflammatory medications, hyaluronic acid injections, platelet-rich plasma (PRP) therapy, and joint replacement surgery for advanced cases.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(25,6,'Is joint replacement surgery always necessary for osteoarthritis?','No, joint replacement surgery is only recommended for severe osteoarthritis cases. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers a range of effective non-surgical treatments including physiotherapy, injections, and pain management to delay or avoid surgery.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(26,6,'Which joints are most commonly affected by osteoarthritis?','Osteoarthritis most commonly affects the knees, hips, spine, hands, and feet. Knee osteoarthritis is particularly prevalent among middle-aged and elderly patients across Bangalore seeking treatment at Nano Hospitals.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(27,6,' Can osteoarthritis be prevented in Bangalore?','While osteoarthritis cannot be completely prevented, risk can be significantly reduced through maintaining healthy weight, regular low-impact exercise, joint protection techniques, and avoiding repetitive joint stress as advised by our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(28,6,'How long is recovery after knee replacement surgery at Nano Hospitals?','Most patients recover significantly within 6-12 weeks after knee replacement surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore, with complete recovery and full mobility restoration typically achieved within 3-6 months with dedicated physiotherapy.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(29,6,'Is osteoarthritis treatment available for elderly patients in Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized osteoarthritis care for elderly patients with customized treatment plans considering age-related health factors, co-existing conditions, and mobility requirements for the best outcomes.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(30,6,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for osteoarthritis treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best osteoarthritis care with experienced orthopedic surgeons, rheumatologists, physiotherapists, advanced joint care technology, and comprehensive rehabilitation programs for complete recovery and improved mobility.',0,'2026-06-11 12:55:49','2026-06-11 12:55:49'),(31,6,'What is osteoarthritis and how does it differ from rheumatoid arthritis?','Osteoarthritis is a degenerative joint disease caused by cartilage breakdown due to wear and tear, primarily affecting older adults. Rheumatoid arthritis is an autoimmune condition causing joint inflammation, affecting younger patients and multiple joints simultaneously.',0,'2026-06-11 12:56:15','2026-06-11 12:56:15'),(32,11,'What is chronic bronchitis and how is it different from acute bronchitis?','Chronic bronchitis is a long-term inflammation of the bronchial tubes causing persistent cough with mucus for at least 3 months over 2 consecutive years. Acute bronchitis is a short-term infection typically lasting 2-3 weeks.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(33,11,'What are the main symptoms of chronic bronchitis?','Main symptoms include persistent productive cough, excessive mucus production, wheezing, shortness of breath, chest discomfort, frequent respiratory infections, fatigue, and progressive breathing difficulty worsening over time.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(34,11,'How is chronic bronchitis diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, chronic bronchitis is diagnosed through spirometry, chest X-ray, CT scan, sputum culture, blood tests, pulse oximetry, and arterial blood gas analysis for comprehensive lung function assessment.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(35,11,'What are the best treatment options for chronic bronchitis in Bangalore?','The best chronic bronchitis treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes bronchodilators, inhaled corticosteroids, pulmonary rehabilitation, oxygen therapy, smoking cessation programs, and antibiotics for bacterial infections.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(36,11,'Is chronic bronchitis caused only by smoking?','While smoking is the leading cause, chronic bronchitis can also be caused by long-term exposure to air pollution, dust, chemical fumes, and recurring respiratory infections, which are increasingly relevant concerns in Bangalore\'s urban environment.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(37,11,' Can chronic bronchitis lead to COPD?','Yes, chronic bronchitis is a major component of COPD (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease). Without proper treatment, it can progressively worsen lung function and develop into full COPD requiring advanced care at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(38,11,'Can chronic bronchitis be cured completely?','Chronic bronchitis cannot be completely cured but can be effectively managed with the right treatment plan. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our pulmonologists help patients significantly reduce symptoms, slow progression, and improve quality of life.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(39,11,'How does Bangalore\'s air pollution affect chronic bronchitis patients?','Bangalore\'s increasing vehicular emissions, construction dust, and industrial pollution significantly worsen chronic bronchitis symptoms. Our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide tailored management plans to help patients cope with environmental triggers effectively.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(40,11,' Is pulmonary rehabilitation available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers comprehensive pulmonary rehabilitation programs including breathing exercises, physical conditioning, nutritional counseling, and education to help chronic bronchitis patients improve lung function and daily activity tolerance.',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(41,11,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for chronic bronchitis treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best chronic bronchitis care with experienced pulmonologists, advanced respiratory diagnostics, comprehensive COPD management programs, and personalized treatment protocols for improved lung health and quality of life.s',0,'2026-06-11 12:59:58','2026-06-11 12:59:58'),(42,13,'What is tuberculosis and how does it spread?','Tuberculosis (TB) is a highly infectious bacterial disease caused by Mycobacterium tuberculosis, primarily spreading through airborne droplets when an infected person coughs, sneezes, or speaks in close proximity to others.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(43,13,'What are the early symptoms of tuberculosis?','Early TB symptoms include persistent cough lasting more than 2 weeks, coughing up blood, unexplained weight loss, night sweats, fever, fatigue, chest pain, and loss of appetite requiring immediate medical attention.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(44,13,'How is tuberculosis diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, TB is diagnosed through sputum smear microscopy, GeneXpert test, TB culture and sensitivity, chest X-ray, CT scan, tuberculin skin test, and IGRA blood test for accurate and rapid diagnosis.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(45,13,'What is the best tuberculosis treatment available in Bangalore?','The best tuberculosis treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals follows the WHO-recommended DOTS protocol using a combination of anti-TB medications including Isoniazid, Rifampicin, Pyrazinamide, and Ethambutol for 6-9 months.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(46,13,'What is drug-resistant tuberculosis and how is it treated?','Drug-resistant TB (MDR-TB and XDR-TB) occurs when TB bacteria become resistant to standard medications. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized treatment with second-line anti-TB drugs and advanced management protocols for drug-resistant TB cases.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(47,13,'How long does tuberculosis treatment take in Bangalore?','Standard TB treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore typically takes 6 months for drug-sensitive TB and 18-24 months for drug-resistant TB. Completing the full course without interruption is critical to prevent drug resistance and ensure complete recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(48,13,' Is tuberculosis completely curable in Bangalore?','Yes, tuberculosis is completely curable with timely diagnosis and adherence to the full prescribed treatment course. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our TB specialists ensure comprehensive monitoring and support throughout the entire treatment journey.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(49,13,' Can tuberculosis affect organs other than the lungs?','Yes, extrapulmonary TB can affect lymph nodes, spine, kidneys, brain, intestines, and other organs. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides comprehensive diagnosis and treatment for both pulmonary and extrapulmonary tuberculosis with specialized multidisciplinary care.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(50,13,' How can tuberculosis be prevented in Bangalore?','TB prevention measures include BCG vaccination, early diagnosis and treatment of active TB, improving ventilation, wearing masks in crowded areas, and maintaining good nutrition and immunity as advised by our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(51,13,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for tuberculosis treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best tuberculosis care with experienced pulmonologists, infectious disease specialists, advanced TB diagnostic technology, WHO-approved treatment protocols, and comprehensive patient support for complete TB recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:08:44','2026-06-11 13:08:44'),(52,7,'What are the most common causes of back and neck pain?','Common causes of back and neck pain include poor posture, sedentary lifestyle, herniated discs, cervical spondylosis, muscle strain, sciatica, spinal stenosis, osteoarthritis, and sports or workplace injuries treated effectively at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(53,7,' When should I see a doctor for back and neck pain in Bangalore?','You should consult a specialist at Nano Hospitals Bangalore if your back or neck pain persists for more than 2 weeks, is accompanied by numbness, tingling, weakness in limbs, difficulty walking, or loss of bladder and bowel control.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(54,7,' How is back and neck pain diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, back and neck pain is diagnosed through detailed clinical examination, X-rays, MRI scan, CT scan, nerve conduction studies, electromyography, and blood tests for comprehensive spinal assessment and accurate diagnosis.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(55,7,' What are the best treatment options for back and neck pain in Bangalore?','The best back and neck pain treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes physiotherapy, pain management injections, anti-inflammatory medications, chiropractic care, minimally invasive spine procedures, and advanced spine surgery for severe cases.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(56,7,'Is surgery always required for back and neck pain treatment?','No, surgery is only recommended for severe or unresponsive cases. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers a wide range of highly effective non-surgical treatments including physiotherapy, epidural injections, nerve blocks, and spinal rehabilitation programs.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(57,7,' What is cervical spondylosis and how is it treated in Bangalore?','Cervical spondylosis is age-related wear and tear of the cervical spine causing neck pain, stiffness, and radiating arm pain. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides comprehensive cervical spondylosis treatment including physiotherapy, medications, and surgical intervention when necessary.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(58,7,'Can back and neck pain be caused by sitting at a desk all day?','Yes, prolonged sitting with poor posture is one of the leading causes of back and neck pain among IT professionals and office workers in Bangalore. Our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide targeted treatment and ergonomic guidance for workplace-related spinal conditions.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(59,7,'What is sciatica and how is it treated at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Sciatica is a condition where the sciatic nerve is compressed causing sharp radiating pain from the lower back through the leg. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides advanced sciatica treatment including physiotherapy, nerve block injections, and minimally invasive surgical decompression.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(60,7,'How long does recovery take after spine surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Recovery after spine surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore typically takes 4-12 weeks depending on the procedure performed, with comprehensive physiotherapy, rehabilitation, and regular follow-up care ensuring complete and safe recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(61,7,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for back and neck pain treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best back and neck pain care with experienced spine surgeons, orthopedic specialists, neurologists, advanced spinal diagnostic technology, and comprehensive rehabilitation programs for complete pain relief and restored mobility.',0,'2026-06-11 13:26:15','2026-06-11 13:26:15'),(62,4,'What is a stroke and what are its main types?','A stroke occurs when blood supply to the brain is interrupted causing brain cell death. Main types include ischemic stroke (caused by blood clot blocking a brain artery), hemorrhagic stroke (caused by bleeding in the brain), and transient ischemic attack (TIA) — all treated emergently at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(63,4,'What are the warning signs of a stroke?','The most recognized warning signs follow the FAST acronym — Face drooping, Arm weakness, Speech difficulty, and Time to call emergency. Other symptoms include sudden severe headache, vision loss, confusion, dizziness, and loss of balance requiring immediate emergency care at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(64,4,'How is stroke diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, stroke is diagnosed through emergency CT scan, MRI brain imaging, CT angiography, carotid ultrasound, echocardiogram, blood tests, and neurological examination for rapid and accurate assessment to initiate the fastest possible treatment.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(65,4,'What are the best stroke treatment options in Bangalore?','The best stroke treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes emergency thrombolysis (clot-dissolving medication), mechanical thrombectomy, surgical intervention for hemorrhagic stroke, intensive neurological monitoring, and comprehensive stroke rehabilitation programs for complete recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(66,4,'How quickly should a stroke patient reach Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Stroke treatment is most effective within the first 4.5 hours — often called the \"golden window.\" At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our dedicated 24/7 stroke response team ensures the fastest possible diagnosis and treatment initiation to minimize brain damage and maximize recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(67,4,'Can a stroke patient fully recover at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Recovery depends on stroke severity, affected brain area, and speed of treatment. With timely intervention and comprehensive rehabilitation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore, many stroke patients achieve significant neurological recovery and regain independence in daily activities.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(68,4,'What are the risk factors for stroke in Bangalore?','Major stroke risk factors include hypertension, diabetes, heart disease, high cholesterol, smoking, obesity, atrial fibrillation, sedentary lifestyle, and excessive alcohol consumption — all addressable through preventive care at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(69,4,'What does stroke rehabilitation involve at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Stroke rehabilitation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore includes physiotherapy for motor recovery, speech therapy, occupational therapy, cognitive rehabilitation, psychological support, and family education programs designed to help every stroke patient regain maximum independence and quality of life.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(70,4,'Can a young person have a stroke in Bangalore?','Yes, strokes are increasingly occurring in younger adults in Bangalore due to rising hypertension, diabetes, stress, smoking, and sedentary lifestyles. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized stroke care for patients of all ages with tailored treatment and rehabilitation programs.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(71,4,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for stroke treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best stroke care with a dedicated 24/7 stroke response team, experienced neurologists and neurosurgeons, advanced neuroimaging technology, rapid thrombolysis protocols, and comprehensive rehabilitation programs for the fastest and most complete stroke recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:32:30','2026-06-11 13:32:30'),(72,8,'What is osteoporosis and who is most at risk?','Osteoporosis is a progressive bone disorder characterized by decreased bone density and increased fracture risk. Those most at risk include postmenopausal women, elderly individuals, patients with calcium and vitamin D deficiency, and those with a family history of osteoporosis — all receiving specialized care at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(73,8,'What are the common symptoms of osteoporosis?','Osteoporosis is often called the \"silent disease\" as it develops without symptoms until a fracture occurs. Warning signs include back pain from vertebral fractures, loss of height over time, stooped posture, and fractures from minor falls requiring prompt evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(74,8,' How is osteoporosis diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, osteoporosis is diagnosed through DEXA (Dual Energy X-ray Absorptiometry) bone density scan, blood tests for calcium, vitamin D and parathyroid hormone levels, X-rays, and FRAX fracture risk assessment for comprehensive and accurate bone health evaluation.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(75,8,'What are the best treatment options for osteoporosis in Bangalore?','The best osteoporosis treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes calcium and vitamin D supplementation, bisphosphonate medications, hormone replacement therapy, denosumab injections, teriparatide therapy, fall prevention programs, and comprehensive physiotherapy for bone strengthening.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(76,8,'Can osteoporosis be reversed with treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','While osteoporosis cannot be completely reversed, bone density can be significantly improved and fracture risk substantially reduced with the right treatment plan at Nano Hospitals Bangalore. Early intervention produces the best outcomes for long-term bone health.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(77,8,' Is osteoporosis only a condition affecting elderly women in Bangalore?','No, while postmenopausal women are at highest risk, osteoporosis can affect men, younger adults, and patients on long-term corticosteroid medications. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized osteoporosis care for patients across all age groups and genders.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(78,8,'How does menopause increase osteoporosis risk in Bangalore women?','Menopause causes a significant drop in estrogen levels which plays a critical role in maintaining bone density. This hormonal change accelerates bone loss substantially in postmenopausal women. Our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide targeted hormone and bone health management for menopausal women.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(79,8,'What lifestyle changes help prevent osteoporosis in Bangalore?','Key preventive measures include adequate calcium and vitamin D intake, regular weight-bearing exercise, quitting smoking, limiting alcohol consumption, fall prevention strategies, and regular bone density screening as advised by our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(80,8,' Is physiotherapy helpful for osteoporosis patients at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, physiotherapy plays a crucial role in osteoporosis management at Nano Hospitals Bangalore. Our physiotherapists design specialized bone-strengthening exercise programs, balance training, and postural correction routines to reduce fracture risk and improve mobility in osteoporosis patients.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(81,8,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for osteoporosis treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best osteoporosis care with experienced orthopedic specialists, rheumatologists, endocrinologists, advanced DEXA scanning technology, personalized bone health treatment plans, and comprehensive fracture prevention programs for stronger bones and improved quality of life.',0,'2026-06-11 13:37:04','2026-06-11 13:37:04'),(82,16,'What are gallstones and how do they form?','Gallstones are hardened crystalline deposits forming inside the gallbladder when bile contains excessive cholesterol, bilirubin, or insufficient bile salts. They range from tiny sand-like granules to large golf ball-sized stones — all requiring comprehensive evaluation and treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(83,16,'What are the common symptoms of gallstones?','Common gallstone symptoms include sudden severe pain in the upper right abdomen or between shoulder blades, nausea, vomiting, fever, jaundice, dark urine, pale stools, and bloating after fatty meals — symptoms requiring immediate evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(84,16,'How are gallstones diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, gallstones are diagnosed through abdominal ultrasound, CT scan, MRI cholangiopancreatography (MRCP), endoscopic ultrasound, liver function tests, and complete blood count for comprehensive and accurate hepatobiliary assessment.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(85,16,'What are the best treatment options for gallstones in Bangalore?','The best gallstones treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes laparoscopic cholecystectomy (minimally invasive gallbladder removal), ERCP for bile duct stones, medication therapy for small cholesterol stones, and comprehensive post-surgical care for complete recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(86,16,' Is laparoscopic surgery the best option for gallstone removal in Bangalore?','Yes, laparoscopic cholecystectomy is the gold standard treatment for gallstones offering minimal scarring, shorter hospital stay, faster recovery, and excellent outcomes. Nano Hospitals Bangalore performs advanced laparoscopic gallstone surgery with experienced surgeons and state-of-the-art facilities.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(87,16,'Can gallstones dissolve without surgery in Bangalore?','Small cholesterol gallstones may sometimes be dissolved using ursodeoxycholic acid medication, but this approach takes months and has a high recurrence rate. For most patients, laparoscopic surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore remains the most effective and permanent solution.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(88,16,'What complications can arise from untreated gallstones?','Untreated gallstones can lead to serious complications including acute cholecystitis, choledocholithiasis, gallstone pancreatitis, bile duct infection (cholangitis), and increased risk of gallbladder cancer — making timely treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore critically important.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(89,16,'How long is recovery after gallstone surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Most patients recover fully within 1-2 weeks after laparoscopic cholecystectomy at Nano Hospitals Bangalore, with minimal post-operative pain, early return to normal activities, and comprehensive follow-up care ensuring complete and safe recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(90,16,'What dietary changes should gallstone patients follow in Bangalore?','Gallstone patients should avoid high-fat, fried, and spicy foods, reduce cholesterol intake, increase fiber consumption, maintain healthy weight, and stay well hydrated. Our dietary specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide personalized nutrition plans for gallstone prevention and management.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(91,16,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for gallstones treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best gallstones care with experienced laparoscopic surgeons, gastroenterologists, hepatobiliary specialists, advanced minimally invasive surgical technology, and comprehensive digestive health programs for complete, safe, and permanent gallstone relief.',0,'2026-06-11 13:40:22','2026-06-11 13:40:22'),(92,27,'What are thyroid disorders and what are their main types?','Thyroid disorders are conditions affecting the thyroid gland\'s hormone production. Main types include hypothyroidism (underactive thyroid), hyperthyroidism (overactive thyroid), thyroid nodules, goiter, Hashimoto\'s thyroiditis, Graves\' disease, and thyroid cancer — all treated comprehensively at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(93,27,'What are the common symptoms of thyroid disorders?','Common symptoms of hypothyroidism include fatigue, weight gain, cold intolerance, depression, dry skin, and hair loss. Hyperthyroidism symptoms include unexplained weight loss, rapid heartbeat, anxiety, excessive sweating, and tremors — all requiring prompt evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(94,27,'How are thyroid disorders diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, thyroid disorders are diagnosed through TSH, T3, and T4 blood tests, thyroid ultrasound, radioactive iodine uptake scan, fine needle aspiration biopsy (FNAB), and thyroid antibody tests for comprehensive and accurate hormonal assessment.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(95,27,'What are the best treatment options for thyroid disorders in Bangalore?','The best thyroid disorders treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes thyroid hormone replacement therapy for hypothyroidism, anti-thyroid medications, radioactive iodine therapy, and surgical thyroidectomy for hyperthyroidism, nodules, and thyroid cancer cases.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(96,27,'Are thyroid disorders more common in women in Bangalore?','Yes, thyroid disorders are significantly more common in women than men, with women being 5-8 times more likely to develop thyroid conditions. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized thyroid care programs tailored specifically for women across all age groups.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(97,27,'Can thyroid disorders affect pregnancy in Bangalore?','Yes, uncontrolled thyroid disorders can significantly affect fertility, pregnancy outcomes, and fetal development. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized thyroid management for pregnant women and those planning conception to ensure safe and healthy pregnancies.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(98,27,'Can thyroid disorders cause weight gain or weight loss?','Yes, hypothyroidism commonly causes unexplained weight gain due to slowed metabolism, while hyperthyroidism causes unexplained weight loss due to accelerated metabolism. Our endocrinologists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide targeted treatment to restore healthy thyroid function and body weight.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(99,27,'Is thyroid surgery safe at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, thyroid surgery (thyroidectomy) at Nano Hospitals Bangalore is performed by experienced thyroid surgeons using advanced minimally invasive techniques, ensuring maximum safety, minimal scarring, faster recovery, and excellent surgical outcomes for every patient.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(100,27,'Can thyroid disorders be completely cured in Bangalore?','Hypothyroidism is typically managed lifelong with hormone replacement therapy. Hyperthyroidism can be permanently resolved with radioactive iodine therapy or surgery. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our specialists design the most effective and personalized treatment plan for every thyroid patient.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(101,27,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for thyroid disorders treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best thyroid disorders care with experienced endocrinologists, thyroid surgeons, nuclear medicine specialists, advanced hormonal diagnostic technology, and comprehensive thyroid management programs for complete hormonal balance and lasting health.',0,'2026-06-13 12:02:16','2026-06-13 12:02:16'),(102,5,'What is obesity and how is it medically defined?','Obesity is a chronic medical condition defined by a Body Mass Index (BMI) of 30 or above, characterized by excessive body fat accumulation that significantly impairs health and increases the risk of serious diseases.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(103,5,'What are the main causes of obesity?','Obesity is caused by a combination of factors including poor dietary habits, sedentary lifestyle, hormonal imbalances, genetic predisposition, stress, inadequate sleep, and certain medications that contribute to excessive weight gain.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(104,5,'What health risks are associated with obesity?','Obesity significantly increases the risk of Type 2 diabetes, heart disease, hypertension, sleep apnea, joint disorders, fatty liver disease, certain cancers, and mental health conditions including depression and anxiety.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(105,5,'What are the best obesity treatment options available in Bangalore?','The best obesity treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes dietary counseling, exercise therapy, behavioral modification, medication management, and advanced bariatric surgical procedures for eligible patients.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(106,5,' Is bariatric surgery the only option for obesity treatment?','No, bariatric surgery is not the only option. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers comprehensive non-surgical obesity management programs including medical nutrition therapy, physical activity plans, and behavioral counseling before considering surgical options.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(107,5,' How much weight can I realistically lose with treatment at Nano Hospitals?','With the right combination of medical treatment, dietary guidance, and lifestyle modifications at Nano Hospitals Bangalore, patients can achieve significant and sustainable weight loss tailored to their individual health goals.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(108,5,'Is obesity treatment covered under health insurance in Bangalore?','Several health insurance policies in India cover obesity-related treatments and bariatric surgery. Our team at Nano Hospitals Bangalore can guide you through insurance eligibility and coverage options for your treatment.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(109,5,'Can children and teenagers receive obesity treatment at Nano Hospitals?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized childhood and adolescent obesity management programs with age-appropriate dietary plans, physical activity guidance, and family-centered behavioral counseling.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(110,5,'How long does obesity treatment take to show results?','Results vary based on the treatment approach and individual health profile. Most patients at Nano Hospitals Bangalore begin noticing significant improvements in weight, energy levels, and overall health within the first few months of treatment.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(111,5,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for obesity treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best obesity care with experienced bariatric surgeons, endocrinologists, dietitians, and a multidisciplinary team dedicated to providing personalized, comprehensive, and long-term weight management solutions.',0,'2026-06-13 12:30:25','2026-06-13 12:30:25'),(112,10,'What is asthma and what causes it?','Asthma is a chronic respiratory condition characterized by airway inflammation, narrowing, and excessive mucus production causing breathing difficulty. Common causes include allergens, air pollution, dust mites, pet dander, respiratory infections, and genetic factors.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(113,10,'What are the common symptoms of asthma?','Common asthma symptoms include persistent cough especially at night, wheezing, shortness of breath, chest tightness, and difficulty breathing during physical activity or exposure to triggers.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(114,10,'How is asthma diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, asthma is diagnosed through detailed medical history, physical examination, spirometry test, peak flow measurement, allergy testing, chest X-ray, and FeNO test for airway inflammation assessment.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(115,10,'What are the best treatment options for asthma in Bangalore?','The best asthma treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes inhaler therapy, bronchodilators, corticosteroids, allergen immunotherapy, biologic medications for severe asthma, and comprehensive asthma action planning.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(116,10,'Can asthma be permanently cured?','Currently, asthma cannot be permanently cured but can be very effectively controlled with the right treatment plan and trigger avoidance. Most patients at Nano Hospitals Bangalore achieve excellent symptom control and lead normal, active lives.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(117,10,'Is asthma dangerous for children in Bangalore?','Asthma is one of the most common chronic conditions in children. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we provide specialized pediatric asthma care with child-friendly treatment plans to effectively manage symptoms and ensure healthy development.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(118,10,'What triggers asthma attacks in Bangalore\'s environment?','Bangalore\'s increasing air pollution, dust, vehicle emissions, construction activity, pollen, and seasonal weather changes are common asthma triggers. Our specialists at Nano Hospitals help patients identify and manage their specific triggers effectively.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(119,10,'What is the difference between mild, moderate, and severe asthma?','Mild asthma causes occasional symptoms with minimal impact on daily life. Moderate asthma causes more frequent symptoms affecting daily activities. Severe asthma causes persistent, debilitating symptoms requiring advanced treatment available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(120,10,'Can I exercise if I have asthma?','Yes, with proper asthma management and guidance from our specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore, most asthma patients can safely exercise and participate in physical activities with appropriate precautions and medication.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(121,10,' Why choose Nano Hospitals for asthma treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best asthma care with experienced pulmonologists, advanced respiratory diagnostics, personalized treatment plans, and comprehensive asthma management programs for children and adults.',0,'2026-06-13 12:33:19','2026-06-13 12:33:19'),(122,19,'What is breast cancer and how does it develop?','Breast cancer develops when cells in the breast tissue grow abnormally and uncontrollably, forming a tumor. It is the most common cancer among women in India and can affect both women and, rarely, men.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(123,19,'What are the early warning signs of breast cancer?','Early warning signs include a new lump in the breast or armpit, changes in breast shape or size, nipple discharge, skin dimpling, redness, or persistent breast pain that should never be ignored.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(124,19,'How is breast cancer diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, breast cancer is diagnosed through clinical breast examination, mammography, ultrasound, MRI, biopsy, hormone receptor testing, and HER2 status evaluation for precise staging and treatment planning.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(125,19,'What are the best breast cancer treatment options in Bangalore?','The best breast cancer treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes surgery (lumpectomy or mastectomy), chemotherapy, radiation therapy, hormone therapy, targeted therapy, and immunotherapy based on cancer type and stage.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(126,19,'What is the survival rate for breast cancer patients in Bangalore?','When detected at an early stage, breast cancer has a survival rate of over 90%. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our multidisciplinary oncology team works to ensure the best possible outcomes through timely and advanced cancer care.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(127,19,' How often should women get breast cancer screening in Bangalore?','Women above 40 should get annual mammograms. Women with a family history of breast cancer should begin screening earlier. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers comprehensive breast cancer screening programs for early detection.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(128,19,'is breast cancer treatment painful?','Some breast cancer treatments may cause discomfort or side effects. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our oncology team provides comprehensive supportive and palliative care to manage treatment side effects and ensure patient comfort throughout the journey.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(129,19,'Can younger women get breast cancer in Bangalore?','Yes, breast cancer can affect younger women, though it is more common after age 40. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized breast cancer care for women of all ages with age-appropriate diagnostic and treatment protocols.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(130,19,'Is breast reconstruction surgery available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers advanced breast reconstruction surgery following mastectomy, with our experienced plastic and reconstructive surgeons helping patients restore their appearance and confidence after cancer treatment.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(131,19,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for breast cancer treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best breast cancer care with a dedicated multidisciplinary oncology team, advanced diagnostic and treatment technology, compassionate patient support, and comprehensive cancer care programs for the best outcomes.',0,'2026-06-13 12:36:12','2026-06-13 12:36:12'),(132,3,'What is heart disease and what are its main types?','Heart disease refers to a range of conditions affecting the heart\'s structure, blood supply, and function. Common types include coronary artery disease, heart failure, arrhythmia, valvular heart disease, and congenital heart defects treated at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(133,3,'What are the early warning signs of heart disease?','Early warning signs include chest pain or discomfort, shortness of breath, palpitations, fatigue, dizziness, swelling in legs, and irregular heartbeat — symptoms that should never be ignored and require immediate evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(134,3,'How is heart disease diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, heart disease is diagnosed through ECG, echocardiogram, stress test, cardiac CT scan, coronary angiography, blood tests, and Holter monitoring for comprehensive and accurate cardiac assessment.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(135,3,'What are the best heart disease treatment options in Bangalore?','The best heart disease treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes medication management, angioplasty, coronary artery bypass surgery, valve repair or replacement, cardiac resynchronization therapy, and comprehensive cardiac rehabilitation programs.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(136,3,'Can heart disease be prevented in Bangalore?','Yes, heart disease can be significantly prevented through regular health screenings, healthy diet, regular exercise, weight management, quitting smoking, controlling blood pressure and diabetes as advised by our cardiologists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(137,3,'What is the difference between a heart attack and cardiac arrest?','A heart attack occurs when blood supply to the heart is blocked causing muscle damage. Cardiac arrest is a sudden loss of heart function requiring immediate resuscitation. Both are life-threatening emergencies treated at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(138,3,'Is heart bypass surgery available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers advanced coronary artery bypass grafting (CABG) surgery performed by experienced cardiac surgeons using the latest minimally invasive and conventional surgical techniques for the best outcomes.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(139,3,'Can young people get heart disease in Bangalore?','Yes, heart disease is increasingly affecting younger adults in Bangalore due to sedentary lifestyles, stress, obesity, smoking, and poor dietary habits. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized cardiac care for patients of all age groups.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(140,3,'How long is recovery after heart surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Recovery after heart surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore typically takes 6-12 weeks, with comprehensive cardiac rehabilitation, physiotherapy, dietary guidance, and regular follow-up care ensuring complete and safe recovery.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(141,3,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for heart disease treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best heart disease care with experienced cardiologists, cardiac surgeons, advanced interventional cardiology facilities, personalized treatment plans, and comprehensive cardiac rehabilitation for complete heart health recovery.',0,'2026-06-15 07:13:44','2026-06-15 07:13:44'),(142,14,'What is acid reflux and how does it differ from GERD?','Acid reflux is a condition where stomach acid flows back into the esophagus causing heartburn and discomfort. When acid reflux occurs frequently — more than twice a week — it is diagnosed as GERD (Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease) requiring comprehensive treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:56','2026-06-15 07:20:56'),(143,14,'What are the most common symptoms of acid reflux?','Common acid reflux symptoms include persistent heartburn, sour or bitter taste in the mouth, regurgitation, chest pain, difficulty swallowing, chronic cough, hoarseness, bloating, and nausea — symptoms that require prompt evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(144,14,'What are the main causes of acid reflux in Bangalore?','Main causes of acid reflux in Bangalore include irregular eating habits, spicy and oily food consumption, obesity, stress, smoking, excessive caffeine and alcohol intake, hiatal hernia, and prolonged use of certain medications.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(145,14,'How is acid reflux diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, acid reflux is diagnosed through detailed clinical evaluation, upper GI endoscopy, esophageal pH monitoring, esophageal manometry, barium swallow test, and H. pylori testing for comprehensive and accurate gastroenterological assessment.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(146,14,'What are the best treatment options for acid reflux in Bangalore?','The best acid reflux treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes dietary and lifestyle modifications, proton pump inhibitor therapy, H2 blockers, antacid medications, endoscopic procedures, and laparoscopic fundoplication surgery for severe or refractory cases.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(147,14,'Can acid reflux lead to serious complications if untreated?','Yes, untreated acid reflux can lead to serious complications including esophagitis, Barrett\'s esophagus, esophageal stricture, chronic cough, dental erosion, and increased risk of esophageal cancer — making timely treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore critically important.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(148,14,'What foods should acid reflux patients avoid in Bangalore?','Acid reflux patients should avoid spicy foods, fried and fatty foods, citrus fruits, tomatoes, chocolate, caffeine, carbonated drinks, and alcohol. Our dietary specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide personalized nutrition plans for effective acid reflux management.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(149,14,' Is surgery required for acid reflux treatment in Bangalore?','Surgery is only recommended for severe or medication-resistant acid reflux cases. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers advanced laparoscopic fundoplication surgery as a highly effective permanent solution for patients who do not respond to conservative treatment.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(150,14,'Can stress cause acid reflux in Bangalore\'s working population?','Yes, stress is a significant trigger for acid reflux, particularly among Bangalore\'s IT professionals and working population. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our gastroenterologists provide comprehensive treatment addressing both physical and stress-related causes of acid reflux.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(151,14,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for acid reflux treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best acid reflux and GERD care with experienced gastroenterologists, advanced endoscopic diagnostic technology, personalized treatment plans, and comprehensive digestive health programs for complete and lasting relief.',0,'2026-06-15 07:20:57','2026-06-15 07:20:57'),(152,21,'What is Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia and is it cancerous?','Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH) is a non-cancerous enlargement of the prostate gland commonly occurring in aging men due to hormonal changes. While BPH is not cancerous, its urinary symptoms can significantly impact quality of life and require comprehensive evaluation and treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(153,21,'What are the common symptoms of BPH in men?','Common BPH symptoms include frequent urination especially at night, weak or intermittent urine stream, difficulty starting urination, sensation of incomplete bladder emptying, urinary urgency, and straining during urination — all requiring prompt evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(154,21,'How is BPH diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, BPH is diagnosed through detailed clinical examination, digital rectal examination (DRE), PSA blood test, uroflowmetry, post-void residual urine measurement, ultrasound of prostate and bladder, and urodynamic studies for comprehensive urological assessment.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(155,21,'What are the best treatment options for BPH in Bangalore?','The best BPH treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes alpha blocker medications, 5-alpha reductase inhibitors, minimally invasive procedures, laser prostatectomy, transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP), and HoLEP surgery for severe or medication-resistant cases.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(156,21,' Is surgery always necessary for BPH treatment in Bangalore?','No, surgery is only recommended for severe or medication-resistant BPH cases. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers highly effective non-surgical BPH management including alpha blocker medications, combination drug therapy, and minimally invasive procedures before considering surgical intervention.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(157,21,'What is TURP surgery and is it available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Transurethral Resection of the Prostate (TURP) is a minimally invasive surgical procedure that removes excess prostate tissue obstructing urine flow. Nano Hospitals Bangalore performs advanced TURP and laser prostatectomy procedures with experienced urologists for safe, effective, and lasting BPH relief.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(158,21,' Can BPH lead to serious complications if left untreated in Bangalore?','Yes, untreated BPH can lead to serious complications including urinary tract infections, bladder stones, acute urinary retention, bladder damage, and kidney damage due to chronic urinary obstruction — making timely treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore critically important.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(159,21,'What is the difference between BPH and prostate cancer in Bangalore?','BPH is a non-cancerous prostate enlargement causing urinary symptoms, while prostate cancer involves malignant growth of prostate cells. Both conditions can cause similar urinary symptoms, making accurate diagnosis through PSA testing and biopsy at Nano Hospitals Bangalore essential for correct treatment.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(160,21,'At what age should men in Bangalore get screened for BPH?','Men above 50 years should undergo regular prostate health screening. Men with a family history of prostate conditions should begin screening at 40. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers comprehensive prostate health screening programs for early BPH detection and timely intervention.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(161,21,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for BPH treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best BPH and prostate enlargement care with experienced urologists, advanced minimally invasive surgical technology, comprehensive urological diagnostic facilities, and personalized treatment plans designed for complete urinary relief and restored prostate health.',0,'2026-06-15 08:13:07','2026-06-15 08:13:07'),(162,26,'What is endometriosis and how does it affect women?','Endometriosis is a chronic gynecological condition where tissue similar to the uterine lining grows outside the uterus on the ovaries, fallopian tubes, and pelvic organs. It causes progressive inflammation, scar tissue formation, severe pain, and infertility — affecting millions of women across Bangalore and Bengaluru requiring specialist care at Nano Hospitals.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(163,26,'What are the most common symptoms of endometriosis?','Common endometriosis symptoms include severe painful periods (dysmenorrhea), chronic pelvic pain, pain during intercourse, painful bowel movements or urination, heavy menstrual bleeding, bloating, fatigue, and difficulty conceiving — all requiring prompt evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(164,26,'How is endometriosis diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, endometriosis is diagnosed through detailed clinical examination, transvaginal ultrasound, MRI pelvis, CA-125 blood test, and diagnostic laparoscopy — the gold standard procedure for definitive endometriosis diagnosis, staging, and simultaneous surgical treatment.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(165,26,'What are the best treatment options for endometriosis in Bangalore?','The best endometriosis treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes hormonal therapy (combined oral contraceptives, GnRH agonists, progestins), laparoscopic excision or ablation surgery, ovarian endometrioma removal, and fertility-preserving surgical procedures for women planning pregnancy.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(166,26,'Can endometriosis cause infertility in women in Bangalore?','Yes, endometriosis is one of the most common causes of female infertility, affecting approximately 30-50% of women with the condition. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized fertility-preserving endometriosis treatment and assisted reproductive technology (ART) support for women trying to conceive.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(167,26,'What is the difference between endometriosis and adenomyosis?','Endometriosis involves uterine-like tissue growing outside the uterus on pelvic organs, while adenomyosis involves this tissue growing within the uterine muscle wall. Both conditions cause painful periods and heavy bleeding but require different treatment approaches available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(168,26,'Is laparoscopic surgery the best option for endometriosis treatment in Bangalore?','Yes, laparoscopic surgery is the gold standard treatment for moderate to severe endometriosis, offering precise excision of endometrial tissue, minimal scarring, faster recovery, and excellent pain relief outcomes. Nano Hospitals Bangalore performs advanced laparoscopic endometriosis surgery with experienced gynecological surgeons.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(169,26,'Can endometriosis come back after treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Endometriosis can recur after treatment, particularly after conservative surgical approaches. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our gynecologists develop comprehensive long-term management plans including hormonal suppression therapy and regular monitoring to minimize recurrence risk and maintain quality of life.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(170,26,'What stage of endometriosis requires surgery in Bangalore?','Stages 3 and 4 endometriosis with extensive pelvic involvement, ovarian endometriomas, or significant adhesions typically require laparoscopic surgical intervention. However, even mild Stage 1 and 2 endometriosis causing significant pain or infertility may benefit from surgical treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(171,26,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for endometriosis treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best endometriosis care with experienced gynecologists, reproductive specialists, advanced laparoscopic surgical technology, comprehensive hormonal management programs, and compassionate fertility-focused care for complete endometriosis relief and improved reproductive health.',0,'2026-06-15 08:20:43','2026-06-15 08:20:43'),(172,9,'What are fractures and what are their main types?','Fractures are breaks or cracks in bones caused by trauma, accidents, falls, sports injuries, or conditions like osteoporosis. Main types include simple, compound, comminuted, stress, hairline, greenstick, and pathological fractures — all requiring expert evaluation and treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(173,9,'What are the common signs and symptoms of a fracture?','Common fracture symptoms include sudden severe pain at the injury site, swelling, bruising, visible deformity, inability to move the affected limb, numbness, tenderness, and in open fractures, bone protruding through the skin — all requiring immediate emergency care at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(174,9,'How are fractures diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, fractures are diagnosed through detailed clinical examination, X-rays, CT scan, MRI imaging, bone scan, and vascular assessment for open or complex fractures to ensure accurate diagnosis and the most appropriate surgical or non-surgical treatment planning.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(175,9,'What are the best treatment options for fractures in Bangalore?','The best fracture treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes cast and splint immobilization, closed reduction, internal fixation with plates and screws, intramedullary nailing, external fixation for complex fractures, and comprehensive physiotherapy and rehabilitation for complete recovery.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(176,9,'When is surgery required for fracture treatment in Bangalore?','Surgery is required for displaced, unstable, open, or complex fractures that cannot be adequately aligned or stabilized with casting alone. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers advanced minimally invasive fracture fixation surgery with experienced orthopedic trauma surgeons for the best outcomes.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(177,9,'How long does fracture healing take at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Fracture healing time varies by fracture type, location, and patient age. Simple fractures typically heal in 6-8 weeks, while complex fractures may take 3-6 months. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides comprehensive follow-up care and physiotherapy to ensure optimal and complete fracture healing.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(178,9,'What is polytrauma and how is it treated at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Polytrauma refers to multiple simultaneous injuries affecting different body systems, commonly resulting from road accidents and falls. Nano Hospitals Bangalore has a dedicated polytrauma team with orthopedic surgeons, neurosurgeons, and critical care specialists providing 24/7 emergency trauma care for the most complex cases.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(179,9,' Can fractures in elderly patients be treated safely at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized fracture care for elderly patients including hip fracture surgery, osteoporotic fracture management, and minimally invasive fixation techniques designed to minimize surgical risk and enable faster, safer recovery in older adults.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(180,9,'What is the role of physiotherapy after fracture treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Physiotherapy is a critical component of fracture recovery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore. Our expert physiotherapists design personalized rehabilitation programs including range of motion exercises, strength training, gait retraining, and functional rehabilitation to help every patient regain full mobility and strength after fracture treatment.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(181,9,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for fracture and trauma treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best fracture and injury trauma care with experienced orthopedic surgeons, dedicated trauma specialists, advanced surgical infrastructure, 24/7 emergency trauma response, and comprehensive rehabilitation programs for the fastest and most complete fracture recovery.',0,'2026-06-15 08:30:01','2026-06-15 08:30:01'),(182,17,' What is fatty liver disease and what are its main types?','Fatty liver disease occurs when excess fat accumulates in liver cells impairing normal liver function. The two main types are Non-Alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease (NAFLD) caused by metabolic factors, and Alcoholic Liver Disease (ALD) caused by excessive alcohol consumption — both requiring comprehensive treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(183,17,'What are the common symptoms of fatty liver disease?','Fatty liver disease often develops without noticeable symptoms in early stages. When symptoms appear they may include persistent fatigue, upper right abdominal discomfort, unexplained weight loss, weakness, jaundice, and abdominal swelling — all requiring prompt evaluation at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(184,17,'How is fatty liver disease diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, fatty liver disease is diagnosed through liver function tests, abdominal ultrasound, FibroScan (liver elastography), CT scan, MRI liver imaging, lipid profile, blood glucose tests, and liver biopsy for comprehensive and accurate hepatological assessment.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(185,17,'What are the best treatment options for fatty liver disease in Bangalore?','The best fatty liver disease treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes dietary and lifestyle modifications, weight management programs, diabetes and cholesterol control, vitamin E supplementation, anti-inflammatory medications, alcohol cessation support, and comprehensive liver health monitoring.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(186,17,' Can fatty liver disease be completely reversed in Bangalore?','Yes, early-stage fatty liver disease can be completely reversed with the right combination of dietary changes, regular exercise, weight loss, and medical management at Nano Hospitals Bangalore. Advanced stages with fibrosis or cirrhosis require more intensive treatment to slow progression and prevent further liver damage.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(187,17,'What are the risk factors for fatty liver disease in Bangalore?','Major risk factors include obesity, Type 2 diabetes, high cholesterol, metabolic syndrome, sedentary lifestyle, unhealthy dietary habits, excessive alcohol consumption, and rapid weight loss — all increasingly common among Bangalore\'s urban population seeking treatment at Nano Hospitals.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(188,17,'Can fatty liver disease progress to liver cancer?','Yes, untreated fatty liver disease can progressively advance from simple steatosis to NASH, liver fibrosis, cirrhosis, and ultimately hepatocellular carcinoma (liver cancer). Early diagnosis and timely treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore are critical to prevent this dangerous progression.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(189,17,'What diet should fatty liver patients follow in Bangalore?','Fatty liver patients should follow a low-fat, low-sugar, high-fiber diet rich in vegetables, fruits, whole grains, and lean proteins while avoiding fried foods, refined carbohydrates, sugary beverages, and alcohol. Our nutritional specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide personalized dietary plans for optimal liver health.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(190,17,'Is fatty liver disease related to diabetes in Bangalore patients?','Yes, there is a strong bidirectional relationship between fatty liver disease and Type 2 diabetes — insulin resistance drives fat accumulation in the liver while fatty liver worsens insulin resistance. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides integrated management of both conditions through our endocrinology and hepatology teams.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(191,17,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for fatty liver disease treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best fatty liver disease care with experienced hepatologists, gastroenterologists, nutritional specialists, advanced liver diagnostic technology including FibroScan, and comprehensive liver health programs for complete recovery and long-term hepatic wellness.',0,'2026-06-15 08:36:22','2026-06-15 08:36:22'),(192,18,'What is Irritable Bowel Syndrome and how does it affect daily life?','Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) is a chronic functional bowel disorder causing persistent abdominal pain, bloating, and unpredictable changes in bowel habits including constipation and diarrhea. IBS can significantly disrupt daily activities, work productivity, social life, and emotional wellbeing — requiring comprehensive specialist care at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(193,18,'What are the most common symptoms of IBS?','Common IBS symptoms include recurrent abdominal cramps and pain, uncomfortable bloating, excessive gas, constipation, diarrhea or alternating between both, mucus in stool, and urgency to use the bathroom — all requiring thorough evaluation and personalized treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(194,18,'How is IBS diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, IBS is diagnosed through detailed clinical evaluation using Rome IV diagnostic criteria, stool tests, blood tests, colonoscopy, flexible sigmoidoscopy, abdominal ultrasound, and food intolerance testing to accurately rule out other gastrointestinal conditions and confirm IBS diagnosis.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(195,18,'What are the best treatment options for IBS in Bangalore?','The best IBS treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes dietary modification with low FODMAP diet, fiber supplementation, antispasmodic medications, probiotic therapy, gut motility regulators, psychological counseling, stress management therapy, and comprehensive bowel health programs for lasting relief.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(196,18,'What triggers IBS symptoms in Bangalore\'s population?','Common IBS triggers in Bangalore include spicy and oily food consumption, irregular meal timings, chronic workplace stress, inadequate sleep, caffeine and alcohol intake, antibiotic use, hormonal changes, and certain food intolerances — all addressable through personalized management at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(197,18,'Is IBS a serious condition that can lead to cancer?','IBS is not a serious structural disease and does not increase the risk of colon cancer or cause permanent bowel damage. However, its chronic symptoms can significantly impair quality of life. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our gastroenterologists provide accurate diagnosis to rule out serious conditions and deliver effective long-term IBS management.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(198,18,'What is the low FODMAP diet and how does it help IBS patients in Bangalore?','The low FODMAP diet restricts fermentable carbohydrates that trigger gut symptoms in IBS patients. It is one of the most evidence-based dietary interventions for IBS management. Our dietary specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore provide personalized low FODMAP diet plans tailored to each patient\'s specific food triggers and nutritional needs.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(199,18,'Can stress and anxiety worsen IBS symptoms in Bangalore?','Yes, IBS is strongly linked to the gut-brain axis where psychological stress, anxiety, and depression can significantly worsen bowel symptoms. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides integrated IBS management addressing both gastrointestinal and psychological factors through gastroenterology and mental health support.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(200,18,' Is IBS more common in women in Bangalore?','Yes, IBS is approximately twice as common in women as in men, with hormonal fluctuations playing a significant role in symptom severity. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized IBS care for women with treatment plans that account for hormonal influences on gut function and bowel health.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(201,18,' Why choose Nano Hospitals for IBS treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best IBS care with experienced gastroenterologists, dietary specialists, psychological support services, advanced gastrointestinal diagnostic technology, and comprehensive bowel health programs combining medical, dietary, and lifestyle interventions for complete and lasting digestive relief.',0,'2026-06-15 08:46:55','2026-06-15 08:46:55'),(202,25,'What are ovarian cysts and are they dangerous?','Ovarian cysts are fluid-filled sacs forming on or inside the ovaries, commonly occurring due to hormonal changes during the menstrual cycle. Most ovarian cysts are benign and resolve naturally, but larger, complex, or ruptured cysts can be dangerous and require immediate specialist evaluation and treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(203,25,'What are the common symptoms of ovarian cysts?','Common ovarian cyst symptoms include pelvic pain or pressure, bloating, irregular periods, pain during intercourse, frequent urination, and difficulty emptying the bladder. Severe sudden pelvic pain may indicate cyst rupture or ovarian torsion requiring emergency care at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(204,25,'How are ovarian cysts diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, ovarian cysts are diagnosed through detailed pelvic examination, transvaginal ultrasound, abdominal ultrasound, pelvic MRI, CA-125 blood test, hormone profile, and comprehensive gynecological assessment for accurate cyst characterization and treatment planning.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(205,25,'What are the best treatment options for ovarian cysts in Bangalore?','The best ovarian cyst treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals includes watchful waiting for small functional cysts, hormonal therapy with oral contraceptives, laparoscopic cystectomy for persistent or large cysts, and emergency surgical intervention for ruptured or twisted ovarian cysts.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(206,25,'When is surgery required for ovarian cysts in Bangalore?','Surgery is recommended for ovarian cysts that are large (over 5cm), persistent, complex, causing severe symptoms, suspicious for malignancy, or complicated by rupture or torsion. Nano Hospitals Bangalore performs advanced laparoscopic ovarian cyst surgery with experienced gynecological surgeons for safe and effective treatment.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(207,25,'Can ovarian cysts affect fertility in women in Bangalore?','Yes, certain types of ovarian cysts including endometriomas and large functional cysts can affect fertility by disrupting ovulation and damaging ovarian tissue. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized fertility-preserving ovarian cyst treatment for women planning conception with comprehensive reproductive health support.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(208,25,'What is the difference between ovarian cysts and PCOS?','Ovarian cysts are individual fluid-filled sacs forming on ovaries due to various causes. PCOS (Polycystic Ovary Syndrome) is a hormonal disorder characterized by multiple small follicular cysts, irregular periods, and hormonal imbalances requiring different treatment approaches available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(209,25,'Can ovarian cysts become cancerous in Bangalore women?','While most ovarian cysts are benign, certain complex cysts including cystadenomas and dermoid cysts carry a small risk of malignancy. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our gynecologists perform comprehensive evaluation including CA-125 testing and imaging to accurately assess malignancy risk and determine the safest treatment approach.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(210,25,'How long is recovery after laparoscopic ovarian cyst surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Most patients recover fully within 1-2 weeks after laparoscopic ovarian cyst surgery at Nano Hospitals Bangalore, with minimal post-operative pain, small incisions, early return to normal activities, and comprehensive follow-up care ensuring complete gynecological recovery and ovarian health restoration.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(211,25,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for ovarian cysts treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best ovarian cysts care with experienced gynecologists, reproductive specialists, advanced laparoscopic surgical technology, comprehensive hormonal management programs, and compassionate patient-centered care for complete ovarian health restoration and improved reproductive wellbeing.',0,'2026-06-15 09:53:19','2026-06-15 09:53:19'),(212,23,'What is infertility and when should couples seek treatment in Bangalore?','Infertility is defined as the inability to conceive after one year of regular unprotected intercourse. Couples under 35 should seek specialist evaluation after one year of trying, while couples above 35 should consult our fertility specialists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore after six months for the best treatment outcomes.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(213,23,'What are the most common causes of infertility in couples in Bangalore?','Common causes of infertility include ovulation disorders, blocked fallopian tubes, endometriosis, PCOS, uterine abnormalities, low sperm count, poor sperm motility, hormonal imbalances, lifestyle factors including stress, obesity, and smoking — all comprehensively evaluated and treated at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(214,23,'How is infertility diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, infertility is diagnosed through comprehensive fertility evaluation including semen analysis, hormone profile testing, transvaginal ultrasound, hysterosalpingography (HSG), diagnostic laparoscopy, genetic testing, and ovarian reserve assessment for accurate diagnosis and personalized treatment planning.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(215,23,'What are the best infertility treatment options available in Bangalore?','The best infertility treatment options in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals include ovulation induction, intrauterine insemination (IUI), in vitro fertilization (IVF), intracytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI), surgical correction of reproductive abnormalities, and comprehensive hormonal management for both male and female infertility.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(216,23,'What is the difference between IVF and IUI treatment in Bangalore?','IUI (Intrauterine Insemination) involves placing prepared sperm directly into the uterus during ovulation and is suitable for mild infertility cases. IVF (In Vitro Fertilization) involves fertilizing eggs outside the body and transferring embryos into the uterus, suitable for complex infertility cases — both available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(217,23,' What is the success rate of IVF treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','IVF success rates depend on age, diagnosis, embryo quality, and overall health. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, our fertility specialists use the most advanced embryology laboratory technology and evidence-based protocols to maximize IVF success rates and give every couple the best possible chance of conception.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(218,23,'Can male infertility be treated at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides comprehensive male infertility treatment including semen analysis, hormonal therapy, surgical sperm retrieval (TESA/PESA), varicocele treatment, lifestyle modification counseling, and advanced ICSI treatment for couples where male factor infertility is identified as the primary concern.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(219,23,'Can PCOS cause infertility and how is it treated in Bangalore?','Yes, PCOS is one of the most common causes of female infertility due to irregular ovulation. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides specialized PCOS-related infertility treatment including ovulation induction with medication, lifestyle modification, weight management, and IVF when required for successful conception.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(220,23,'Is infertility treatment emotionally supported at Nano Hospitals Bangalore?','Yes, Nano Hospitals Bangalore understands that infertility is an emotionally challenging journey for couples. Our dedicated fertility counselors and psychological support team provide compassionate emotional guidance, stress management counseling, and couple support throughout every stage of the infertility treatment process.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25'),(221,23,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for infertility treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers the best infertility care with experienced fertility specialists, reproductive endocrinologists, state-of-the-art embryology laboratory, advanced ART procedures including IVF and ICSI, comprehensive male and female fertility evaluation, and compassionate couple-centered care for the best possible parenthood outcomes.',0,'2026-06-15 09:57:25','2026-06-15 09:57:25');
