llstone relief, restored digestive health, and improved quality of life.</p>','<p>Gallstones are hardened crystalline deposits that form inside the gallbladder, blocking normal bile flow and causing severe abdominal pain, nausea, vomiting, and potentially dangerous infections — a condition increasingly common among individuals across Bangalore and Bengaluru due to dietary habits, obesity, and sedentary lifestyles. Often remaining silent until a painful gallstone attack occurs, early detection and timely treatment are absolutely critical to prevent serious complications including cholecystitis, pancreatitis, and bile duct obstruction. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are equipped with the best state-of-the-art laparoscopic and endoscopic surgical infrastructure, combining advanced minimally invasive technology with evidence-based treatment protocols to help every patient achieve permanent, safe, and effective gallstone relief.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Severe right upper abdominal pain\"},{\"value\":\"Nausea\\/vomiting\"},{\"value\":\"Indigestion after fatty meals\"},{\"value\":\"Jaundice (if bile duct blocked)\"}]','[{\"value\":\"High cholesterol in bile\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity\"},{\"value\":\"Rapid weight loss\"},{\"value\":\"Genetics\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Gallbladder infection\"},{\"value\":\"Pancreatitis\"},{\"value\":\"Jaundice\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Ultrasound\"},{\"value\":\"CT\\/MRI\"},{\"value\":\"Blood tests (liver function)\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Cholecystectomy (surgical removal)\"},{\"value\":\"ERCP for bile duct stones\"}]','<p>Safe and effective; patients live normally without gallbladder.<br></p>',0,1,'2026-02-03 01:24:40','2026-06-11 13:40:22','Best Gallstones Treatment in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Experiencing severe abdominal pain or bloating? Get the best Gallstones treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore from expert gastro surgeons for lasting relief.',NULL,'Best Gallstones Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(17,'Fatty Liver Disease','fatty-liver-disease',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Nano Hospitals is one of the best fatty liver disease treatment hospitals in Bangalore, providing advanced and comprehensive hepatology and gastroenterology care for patients suffering from non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), alcoholic liver disease (ALD), liver inflammation, and related hepatic conditions across Bengaluru. Our best team of experienced hepatologists, gastroenterologists, and nutritional specialists collaborates closely to deliver precise liver health assessment and personalized treatment plans, ensuring every patient achieves complete liver recovery, restored hepatic function, and improved overall health.</p>','<p>Fatty liver disease occurs when excess fat accumulates abnormally within liver cells — either due to alcohol consumption (ALD) or metabolic factors such as obesity, diabetes, and high cholesterol (NAFLD) — increasingly affecting a significant number of individuals across Bangalore and Bengaluru due to sedentary lifestyles and unhealthy dietary habits. Often progressing silently without noticeable symptoms until serious liver damage develops, fatty liver disease demands early detection and timely medical intervention to prevent progression to liver fibrosis, cirrhosis, and liver failure. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are equipped with the best state-of-the-art hepatological diagnostic and treatment infrastructure, combining advanced liver imaging technology with evidence-based medical and lifestyle intervention protocols to help every patient restore healthy liver function and prevent long-term complications.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Often asymptomatic\"},{\"value\":\"Fatigue\"},{\"value\":\"Abdominal discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Enlarged liver\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Obesity\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity\"},{\"value\":\"Alcohol abuse\"},{\"value\":\"High cholesterol\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Cirrhosis\"},{\"value\":\"Liver cancer\"},{\"value\":\"Liver failure\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Ultrasound\"},{\"value\":\"Liver function tests\"},{\"value\":\"Biopsy\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Lifestyle modification\"},{\"value\":\"Medications (experimental for NAFLD)\"},{\"value\":\"Alcohol cessation\"}]','<p>Reversible in early stages; advanced cases need transplant.<br></p>',0,1,'2026-02-03 01:27:26','2026-06-15 08:36:22','Best Fatty Liver Treatment in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Diagnosed with fatty liver or NAFLD? Get the best Fatty Liver Disease treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore from expert hepatologists for complete liver health.',NULL,'Best Fatty Liver Disease Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(18,'Irritable Bowel Syndrome','irritable-bowel-syndrome',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Nano Hospitals is one of the best Irritable Bowel Syndrome (IBS) treatment hospitals in Bangalore, providing advanced and comprehensive gastroenterology care for patients suffering from chronic abdominal pain, bloating, constipation, diarrhea, and altered bowel habits across Bengaluru. Our best team of experienced gastroenterologists, digestive health specialists, and dietary counselors collaborates closely to deliver precise diagnosis and highly personalized treatment plans, ensuring every patient achieves complete digestive relief, restored bowel function, and significantly improved quality of life</p>','<p>Irritable Bowel Syndrome is a chronic functional bowel disorder characterized by persistent abdominal pain, uncomfortable bloating, and unpredictable changes in bowel habits including constipation and diarrhea — increasingly affecting working professionals, students, and individuals under chronic stress across Bangalore and Bengaluru. Often misdiagnosed or left untreated due to its variable and overlapping symptoms, IBS can significantly disrupt daily life, work productivity, and emotional wellbeing without timely specialist intervention. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are equipped with the best state-of-the-art gastrointestinal diagnostic infrastructure, combining advanced gut health assessment with evidence-based dietary, pharmacological, and psychological treatment protocols to help every patient achieve lasting digestive comfort and improved bowel health.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Abdominal pain\"},{\"value\":\"Bloating\"},{\"value\":\"Diarrhea or constipation\"},{\"value\":\"Mucus in stool\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Stress\"},{\"value\":\"Food intolerance\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal changes\"},{\"value\":\"Gut microbiome imbalance\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Chronic discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Reduced quality of life\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Clinical evaluation\"},{\"value\":\"Colonoscopy (to rule out other causes)\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Dietary changes (low FODMAP diet)\"},{\"value\":\"Fiber supplements\"},{\"value\":\"Medications (antispasmodics, laxatives)\"},{\"value\":\"Counseling for stress\"}]','<p>IBS is chronic but manageable with lifestyle and medication.<br></p>',0,1,'2026-02-03 01:29:38','2026-06-15 08:46:55','Best IBS Treatment in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Suffering from bloating, abdominal pain or irregular bowel habits? Get the best IBS treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore from expert gastroenterologists today.',NULL,'Best Irritable Bowel Syndrome Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(19,'Breast Cancer','breast-cancer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Nano Hospitals is one of the best breast cancer treatment hospitals in Bangalore, offering compassionate and comprehensive oncology care for women diagnosed with early and advanced stage breast cancer across Bengaluru. Our best multidisciplinary team of surgical oncologists, medical oncologists, and radiation specialists collaborates closely to design precise, personalized cancer treatment plans for the best possible outcomes.</p>','<p>Breast cancer, when detected early, has significantly higher survival and recovery rates — making regular screening and timely medical intervention absolutely essential. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are committed to providing the best clinical excellence, empathy, and advanced treatment technology to every patient throughout their cancer journey.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Lump in breast\"},{\"value\":\"Change in breast shape\\/size\"},{\"value\":\"Nipple discharge\"},{\"value\":\"Skin dimpling\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Genetic mutations (BRCA1\\/2)\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal factors\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity\"},{\"value\":\"Radiation exposure\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Cancer spread (metastasis)\"},{\"value\":\"Death\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Regular screening (mammogram)\"},{\"value\":\"Healthy lifestyle\"},{\"value\":\"Genetic counseling for high-risk women\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Surgery (lumpectomy, mastectomy)\"},{\"value\":\"Chemotherapy\"},{\"value\":\"Radiation therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Targeted therapy\"}]','<p>Early detection improves survival; advanced cases need multimodal treatment.<br></p>',0,1,'2026-02-03 01:31:46','2026-06-13 12:36:12','Best Breast Cancer Treatment in Bangalore | Top Oncologists in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Nano Hospitals is a trusted breast cancer treatment hospital in Bangalore offering advanced oncology care. Our experienced cancer specialists provide compassionate, evidence-based treatment for early and advanced stage breast cancer.',NULL,'Best Breast Cancer Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(20,'Kidney Stones','kidney-stones',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Kidney stones are solid crystal formations that develop in the kidneys and may cause severe pain when passing through the urinary tract.','These stones form due to the buildup of minerals and salts in the urine. Depending on their size and location, they may pass naturally or require medical treatment.','Kidney stones are hard mineral deposits that form inside the kidneys. They can cause intense pain, urinary blockage, and complications if not treated promptly.','[{\"value\":\"Severe back or side pain\"},{\"value\":\"Blood in urine\"},{\"value\":\"Nausea\\/vomiting\"},{\"value\":\"Pain during urination\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent urination\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Dehydration\"},{\"value\":\"High oxalate foods\"},{\"value\":\"Excess salt intake\"},{\"value\":\"Family history\"},{\"value\":\"Certain medications\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Blocked urinary flow\"},{\"value\":\"Kidney infection\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic kidney disease\"},{\"value\":\"Recurrence\"},{\"value\":\"Severe pain episodes\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Urine examination\"},{\"value\":\"Blood tests\"},{\"value\":\"Ultrasound scan\"},{\"value\":\"CT scan for stone detection\"},{\"value\":\"X-ray of urinary tract\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hydration therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Pain relief medications\"},{\"value\":\"ESWL (shock wave therapy)\"},{\"value\":\"Laser treatment\"},{\"value\":\"Surgery for large stones\"}]','With proper hydration, dietary modifications, and timely treatment, most patients recover fully from kidney stones. Lifestyle changes help reduce the risk of recurrence.',5,1,'2026-03-16 12:32:08','2026-05-06 07:31:04','Kidney Stones Treatment Bangalore – Advanced Stone Care','Get expert kidney stone treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Advanced care with ESWL, laser lithotripsy, and minimally invasive stone removal procedures.','kidney stones treatment Bangalore, renal stone treatment Bangalore, laser kidney stone treatment Bangalore, ESWL Bangalore, kidney stone surgery Bangalore, urology hospital Uttarahalli, Nano Hospitals Hulimavu','Kidney Stones Treatment in Bangalore'),(21,'Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia ','benign-prostatic-hyperplasia',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Nano Hospitals is one of the best Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia (BPH) treatment hospitals in Bangalore, providing advanced and comprehensive urological care for men suffering from prostate enlargement, urinary obstruction, and related bladder conditions across Bengaluru. Our best team of experienced urologists, uro-surgeons, and bladder health specialists collaborates closely to deliver precise diagnosis and personalized treatment plans, ensuring every patient achieves complete urinary relief, restored prostate health, and significantly improved quality of life.</p>','<p>Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia is a non-cancerous enlargement of the prostate gland occurring due to hormonal changes during aging — causing the enlarged prostate to press against the urethra and disrupt normal urine flow in men across Bangalore and Bengaluru. Symptoms including frequent urination, weak urine stream, difficulty emptying the bladder, and disrupted sleep can significantly impact daily life and overall wellbeing if left untreated. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are equipped with the best state-of-the-art urological diagnostic and surgical infrastructure, combining advanced minimally invasive technology with evidence-based treatment protocols to help every patient restore normal urinary function and reclaim their quality of life.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Frequent urination\"},{\"value\":\"Weak urine stream\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty starting urination\"},{\"value\":\"Nighttime urination\"},{\"value\":\"Feeling of incomplete bladder emptying\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Aging \\u2013 The risk of prostate enlargement increases as men grow older\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal Changes \\u2013 Changes in male hormones such as testosterone and dihydrotestosterone (DHT) can stimulate prostate growth.\"},{\"value\":\"Family History \\u2013 Men with relatives who have BPH may have a higher risk of developing the condition.\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity \\u2013 Being overweight can increase the likelihood of prostate enlargement.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Age above 50 years \\u2013 BPH is uncommon in younger men but becomes more common with age.\"},{\"value\":\"Family History of Prostate Problems \\u2013 Genetic factors may increase the risk.\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity and Metabolic Syndrome \\u2013 Excess body weight can affect hormone levels and prostate health.\"},{\"value\":\"Diabetes \\u2013 Men with diabetes have a higher chance of developing BPH.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Digital Rectal Examination (DRE) \\u2013 The doctor checks the size and shape of the prostate by inserting a gloved finger into the rectum.\"},{\"value\":\"Prostate-Specific Antigen (PSA) Test \\u2013 A blood test used to measure PSA levels and assess prostate health.\"},{\"value\":\"Urine Test (Urinalysis) \\u2013 Helps detect infections, blood, or other urinary abnormalities.\"},{\"value\":\"Ultrasound \\u2013 Imaging used to evaluate prostate size and check for bladder or kidney problems.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Antibiotic medications\"},{\"value\":\"Increased water intake\"},{\"value\":\"Pain relief medications\"}]','<p>UTIs usually respond quickly to antibiotics when treated early. Symptoms typically improve within a few days of starting treatment. Drinking plenty of water helps flush bacteria from the urinary tract and speeds recovery. Maintaining proper hygiene and hydration can help prevent recurrent infections. Some patients may require longer treatment if infections recur frequently. With proper care and early treatment, most UTIs heal completely without complications.</p>',0,1,'2026-03-16 12:39:52','2026-06-15 08:13:07','Best BPH Treatment in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Get the best BPH & Prostate Enlargement treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore from expert urologists for complete and lasting urinary relief.',NULL,'Best Benign Prostatic Hyperplasia Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(22,'Polycystic Ovary Syndrome ','polycystic-ovary-syndrome',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) is a hormonal disorder affecting women during their reproductive years. It occurs when the ovaries produce higher levels of male hormones (androgens), disrupting normal ovulation.</p>','<p>Women with PCOS may develop multiple small cysts in their ovaries and experience irregular menstrual cycles. Symptoms may include weight gain, acne, and excessive hair growth. PCOS is one of the most common causes of infertility in women. Early diagnosis helps manage symptoms and prevent long-term health risks such as diabetes.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Irregular menstrual cycles\"},{\"value\":\"Excess facial or body hair\"},{\"value\":\"Acne or oily skin\"},{\"value\":\"Weight gain\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hormonal Imbalance \\u2013 Excess production of androgens (male hormones) interferes with normal ovulation.\"},{\"value\":\"Insulin Resistance \\u2013 The body does not use insulin effectively, leading to higher insulin levels that increase androgen production.\"},{\"value\":\"Genetic Factors \\u2013 PCOS often runs in families, suggesting a hereditary component.\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic Low-Grade Inflammation \\u2013 Inflammation can stimulate the ovaries to produce excess androgens.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Family History \\u2013 Having a mother or sister with PCOS increases the risk.\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity or Overweight \\u2013 Excess body weight can worsen insulin resistance and hormonal imbalance.\"},{\"value\":\"Insulin Resistance or Type 2 Diabetes \\u2013 Women with these conditions are more likely to develop PCOS.\"},{\"value\":\"Sedentary Lifestyle \\u2013 Lack of regular physical activity can contribute to metabolic and hormonal imbalance.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Medical History and Symptom Evaluation \\u2013 Assessment of irregular periods, acne, excessive hair growth, and weight gain.\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic Ultrasound \\u2013 Used to detect enlarged ovaries and multiple small cysts.\"},{\"value\":\"Blood Tests \\u2013 Hormone tests to measure androgen levels, insulin levels, and other reproductive hormones.\"},{\"value\":\"Menstrual Cycle Evaluation \\u2013 Checking the frequency and regularity of menstrual cycles.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Lifestyle changes and weight management\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal medications\"},{\"value\":\"Fertility treatments\"}]','<p>Although PCOS cannot be completely cured, symptoms can be effectively managed. Maintaining a healthy weight and balanced diet helps regulate hormones and improve menstrual cycles. Medical treatment can control acne, excessive hair growth, and fertility issues. Early diagnosis also helps reduce long-term risks such as diabetes and heart disease. Many women with PCOS successfully conceive with proper treatment. Regular medical monitoring helps maintain hormonal balance.</p>',0,1,'2026-03-16 12:46:04','2026-03-16 12:46:04',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(23,'Infertility Treatment','infertility-treatment',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Infertility refers to the inability of a couple to conceive after one year of regular unprotected intercourse. It may occur due to issues affecting either the male or female reproductive system. Hormonal imbalance, ovulation problems, blocked fallopian tubes, or low sperm count are common causes.</p>','<p>Lifestyle factors such as stress, smoking, alcohol consumption, and obesity may also affect fertility. Infertility can be emotionally challenging for couples. Fortunately, advances in reproductive medicine offer effective treatment options.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Difficulty conceiving\"},{\"value\":\"Irregular menstrual cycles\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal imbalance\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Ovulation Disorders \\u2013 Problems with ovulation due to hormonal imbalance or conditions like PCOS.\"},{\"value\":\"Blocked Fallopian Tubes \\u2013 Tubal damage or blockage prevents the egg and sperm from meeting.\"},{\"value\":\"Endometriosis \\u2013 Tissue similar to the uterine lining grows outside the uterus and affects fertility.\"},{\"value\":\"Low Sperm Count or Poor Sperm Quality \\u2013 Reduced sperm production or abnormal sperm function can cause male infertility.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Advanced Age \\u2013 Women over 35 and men over 40 may experience reduced fertility.\"},{\"value\":\"Obesity or Underweight \\u2013 Extreme body weight can affect hormone balance and ovulation.\"},{\"value\":\"Smoking and Alcohol Consumption \\u2013 These habits can reduce sperm quality and affect reproductive health.\"},{\"value\":\"Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs) \\u2013 Untreated infections can damage reproductive organs.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Medical History and Physical Examination \\u2013 Evaluation of reproductive history and overall health.\"},{\"value\":\"Ovulation Testing \\u2013 Blood or urine tests to confirm whether ovulation is occurring regularly.\"},{\"value\":\"Semen Analysis \\u2013 Laboratory test to evaluate sperm count, motility, and morphology.\"},{\"value\":\"Ultrasound Scan \\u2013 Imaging used to assess the uterus and ovaries.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Fertility medications\"},{\"value\":\"Intrauterine insemination (IUI)\"},{\"value\":\"In-vitro fertilization (IVF)\"}]','<p>Modern fertility treatments have significantly improved success rates for couples struggling with infertility. Depending on the cause, doctors may recommend medications, assisted reproductive techniques, or lifestyle modifications. Emotional counseling and support are also important during treatment. Early consultation with fertility specialists improves the chances of successful pregnancy. Many couples achieve successful conception through modern reproductive technologies. Continuous medical guidance ensures better outcomes.</p>',0,1,'2026-03-16 12:49:34','2026-06-15 10:00:24','Best Infertility Treatment in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Struggling to conceive? Get the best Infertility treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore from expert fertility specialists for your dream of parenthood.',NULL,'Best Infertility Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(24,'Uterine Fibroids','uterine-fibroids',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Uterine fibroids are non-cancerous growths that develop in or around the uterus, most commonly affecting women during their reproductive years. These growths are made of muscle and fibrous tissue and can vary in size from very small to large masses. Fibroids may occur as a single growth or in multiple numbers within the uterus. While some women may not experience symptoms, others may develop heavy menstrual bleeding</p>','<p>, pelvic pressure, or frequent urination. Hormonal factors such as estrogen and progesterone play an important role in their development. Early diagnosis and treatment help reduce symptoms and improve quality of life.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Heavy or prolonged menstrual bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic pain or pressure\"},{\"value\":\"Frequent urination\"},{\"value\":\"Lower back pain\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty during pregnancy in some cases\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hormonal Imbalance \\u2013 High levels of estrogen and progesterone can stimulate the growth of fibroids in the uterus.\"},{\"value\":\"Genetic Factors \\u2013 Family history may increase the likelihood of developing uterine fibroids.\"},{\"value\":\"Extracellular Matrix (ECM) Changes \\u2013 Increased ECM can make fibroids larger and more fibrous.\"},{\"value\":\"Growth Factors \\u2013 Substances that help the body maintain tissues may promote fibroid growth.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Pelvic Examination \\u2013 A doctor may detect irregularities in the uterus during a physical exam.\"},{\"value\":\"Ultrasound \\u2013 The most common imaging test used to detect fibroids and evaluate their size and location.\"},{\"value\":\"MRI Scan \\u2013 Provides detailed images of fibroids and helps in treatment planning.\"},{\"value\":\"Hysteroscopy \\u2013 A thin camera is inserted into the uterus to view fibroids inside the uterine cavity.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hormonal Imbalance \\u2013 High levels of estrogen and progesterone can stimulate the growth of fibroids in the uterus.\"},{\"value\":\"Genetic Factors \\u2013 Family history may increase the likelihood of developing uterine fibroids.\"},{\"value\":\"Growth Factors \\u2013 Substances that help the body maintain tissues may promote fibroid growth.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Medications to control bleeding and hormones\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Minimally invasive procedures\"},{\"value\":\"Surgical removal of fibroids (myomectomy)\"},{\"value\":\"Hysterectomy in severe cases\"}]','<p>Many women with fibroids live normal lives with proper treatment and monitoring. Medications and hormonal therapies can help control symptoms and reduce the size of fibroids. In cases where fibroids cause severe symptoms, surgical procedures provide effective long-term relief. Modern minimally invasive treatments allow faster recovery and minimal hospital stay. Lifestyle changes and regular gynecological checkups help monitor fibroid growth. With timely medical care, most patients experience significant symptom improvement.</p>',0,1,'2026-03-16 12:54:24','2026-03-16 12:54:24',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(25,'Ovarian Cysts','ovarian-cysts',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Nano Hospitals is one of the best ovarian cysts treatment hospitals in Bangalore, providing advanced and comprehensive gynecological care for women suffering from functional ovarian cysts, endometriomas, polycystic ovaries, dermoid cysts, and complex ovarian masses across Bengaluru. Our best team of experienced gynecologists, reproductive specialists, and laparoscopic surgeons collaborates closely to deliver precise diagnosis and highly personalized treatment plans, ensuring every woman receives compassionate, evidence-based care for complete ovarian health restoration and improved reproductive wellbeing.</p>','<p>Ovarian cysts are fluid-filled sacs developing on or inside the ovaries — extremely common among women of reproductive age and frequently occurring due to hormonal changes during the menstrual cycle across Bangalore and Bengaluru. While many ovarian cysts resolve naturally without treatment, larger cysts causing persistent pelvic pain, bloating, irregular periods, or complications such as rupture or ovarian torsion demand immediate specialist evaluation and timely medical intervention. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are equipped with the best state-of-the-art gynecological diagnostic and laparoscopic surgical infrastructure, combining advanced transvaginal ultrasound imaging with evidence-based hormonal and surgical treatment protocols to help every woman achieve complete ovarian health and peace of mind.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Pelvic pain or discomfort\"},{\"value\":\"Abdominal bloating\"},{\"value\":\"rregular menstrual cycles\"},{\"value\":\"Pain during intercourse\"},{\"value\":\"Feeling of fullness in the abdomen\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hormonal Imbalance \\u2013 Changes in hormone levels can lead to the formation of cysts in the ovaries.\"},{\"value\":\"Ovulation Problems \\u2013 When the follicle does not release the egg properly, it may continue to grow and form a cyst.\"},{\"value\":\"Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) \\u2013 A condition that causes multiple small cysts to develop in the ovaries.\"},{\"value\":\"Endometriosis \\u2013 Endometrial tissue growing outside the uterus can attach to the ovary and form cysts called endometriomas.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Hormonal Problems \\u2013 Hormonal imbalances can increase the likelihood of cyst formation.\"},{\"value\":\"PCOS \\u2013 Women with polycystic ovary syndrome are more prone to developing ovarian cysts.\"},{\"value\":\"Pregnancy \\u2013 Functional cysts can sometimes develop during early pregnancy.\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic Infections \\u2013 Untreated infections can spread to reproductive organs and increase the risk.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Pelvic Examination \\u2013 A doctor may detect swelling or abnormalities in the ovary during a physical exam.\"},{\"value\":\"Ultrasound Scan \\u2013 The most common imaging test used to detect ovarian cysts and determine their size and type.\"},{\"value\":\"Pregnancy Test \\u2013 Performed to rule out pregnancy-related cysts.\"},{\"value\":\"Blood Tests \\u2013 Used to measure hormone levels and check for tumor markers if needed.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Monitoring with ultrasound\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal medications\"},{\"value\":\"Pain management\"},{\"value\":\"Surgical removal if cysts are large or persistent\"}]','<p>Most ovarian cysts resolve on their own within a few menstrual cycles without medical intervention. Doctors may recommend regular monitoring through ultrasound scans to ensure the cyst is shrinking. Hormonal medications may be prescribed to prevent the formation of new cysts. In rare cases, surgery may be required to remove large or painful cysts. With proper treatment and monitoring, complications are uncommon. Early detection helps maintain reproductive health and prevents serious issues.</p>',0,1,'2026-03-16 13:04:55','2026-06-15 09:53:19','Best Ovarian Cysts Treatment in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Experiencing pelvic pain or irregular periods? Get the best Ovarian Cysts treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore from expert gynecologists for complete relief.',NULL,'Best Ovarian Cysts Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(26,'Endometriosis','endometriosis',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Nano Hospitals is one of the best endometriosis treatment hospitals in Bangalore, providing advanced and comprehensive gynecological care for women suffering from chronic pelvic pain, painful menstruation, endometriotic cysts, and endometriosis-related infertility across Bengaluru. Our best team of experienced gynecologists, reproductive medicine specialists, and laparoscopic surgeons collaborates closely to deliver precise diagnosis and highly personalized treatment plans, ensuring every woman receives compassionate, evidence-based care for complete endometriosis management and improved reproductive health.</p>','<p>Endometriosis is a complex gynecological condition where tissue similar to the uterine lining grows abnormally outside the uterus — affecting the ovaries, fallopian tubes, and other pelvic organs — causing severe inflammation, scar tissue formation, chronic pain, and fertility challenges in women across Bangalore and Bengaluru. As one of the most common yet frequently underdiagnosed causes of chronic pelvic pain and female infertility, early detection and timely medical intervention are absolutely critical for effective symptom management. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are equipped with the best state-of-the-art gynecological diagnostic and laparoscopic surgical infrastructure, combining advanced imaging technology with evidence-based hormonal and surgical treatment protocols to help every woman reclaim her health, comfort, and fertility.</p>','<p></p>','[{\"value\":\"Severe menstrual cramps\"},{\"value\":\"Chronic pelvic pain\"},{\"value\":\"Pain during intercourse\"},{\"value\":\"Heavy menstrual bleeding\"},{\"value\":\"Difficulty conceiving\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Retrograde Menstruation \\u2013 Menstrual blood flows backward through the fallopian tubes into the pelvic cavity, allowing endometrial cells to grow outside the uterus.\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal Imbalance \\u2013 High estrogen levels may promote the growth of endometrial tissue outside the uterus.\"},{\"value\":\"Genetic Factors \\u2013 Endometriosis often runs in families, suggesting a hereditary link.\"},{\"value\":\"Immune System Disorders \\u2013 A weakened immune system may fail to destroy endometrial cells growing outside the uterus.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Family History \\u2013 Women with a mother or sister who has endometriosis have a higher risk.\"},{\"value\":\"Early Menstruation \\u2013 Starting periods at an early age may increase the risk.\"},{\"value\":\"Short Menstrual Cycles \\u2013 Cycles shorter than 27 days may contribute to the condition.\"},{\"value\":\"Heavy or Prolonged Periods \\u2013 Excessive menstrual bleeding may be associated with endometriosis.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Medical History and Symptom Evaluation \\u2013 Assessment of symptoms such as pelvic pain, painful periods, and infertility.\"},{\"value\":\"Pelvic Examination \\u2013 Doctors check for cysts, nodules, or scar tissue in the pelvic region.\"},{\"value\":\"Ultrasound Scan \\u2013 Helps identify ovarian cysts related to endometriosis (endometriomas).\"},{\"value\":\"MRI Scan \\u2013 Provides detailed images to determine the location and severity of endometrial tissue.\"}]','[{\"value\":\"Pain relief medications\"},{\"value\":\"Hormonal therapy\"},{\"value\":\"Laparoscopic surgery\"},{\"value\":\"Fertility treatments\"}]','<p>Endometriosis is a long-term condition, but symptoms can be effectively managed with proper treatment. Medications help control pain and slow the growth of abnormal tissue. Hormonal therapy may regulate menstrual cycles and reduce symptoms. In some cases, minimally invasive surgery removes endometrial tissue and improves fertility outcomes. Regular follow-up with a gynecologist helps monitor the condition. Early management significantly improves quality of life for many women.</p>',0,1,'2026-03-16 13:18:31','2026-06-15 08:17:07','Best Endometriosis Treatment in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Suffering from chronic pelvic pain or painful periods? Get the best Endometriosis treatment at Nano Hospitals Bangalore from expert gynecologists for lasting relief.',NULL,'Best Endometriosis Treatment Hospital In Bangalore'),(27,'Thyroid Disorders','thyroid-disorders',NULL,NULL,NULL,'<p>Nano Hospitals is one of the best thyroid disorders treatment hospitals in Bangalore, providing advanced and comprehensive endocrinology care for patients suffering from hypothyroidism, hyperthyroidism, thyroid nodules, goiter, and thyroid cancer across Bengaluru. Our best team of endocrinologists, thyroid specialists, and nuclear medicine experts collaborates closely to deliver precise diagnosis and personalized treatment plans, ensuring every patient achieves optimal thyroid health and hormonal balance.</p>','<p>Thyroid disorders occur when the thyroid gland produces too much or too little thyroid hormone — directly affecting metabolism, energy levels, heart rate, body weight, mood, and overall health of patients across Bangalore and Bengaluru. Particularly common among women and increasingly prevalent in urban populations, thyroid disorders demand early detection and timely medical intervention for effective management. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, we are equipped with the best state-of-the-art th