li><p>Improved mobility and flexibility</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Avoidance of surgical risks</p></li><li><p>Faster recovery and return to daily activities</p></li><li><p>Improved patient comfort and quality of life</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Reduces dependency on spine surgeries</p></li><li><p>Promotes non-invasive pain management solutions</p></li><li><p>Supports early treatment of spinal disorders</p></li></ul>','<p>Mild soreness after initial sessions</p><p>Temporary discomfort during traction</p><p>Rare cases of symptom aggravation if not properly assessed</p><p>Requires multiple sessions for best results</p><p>Not suitable for severe spinal instability or fractures</p><p>Patient adherence to therapy schedule is essential</p>','<ul><li><p>Non-surgical solution for disc-related spine problems</p></li><li><p>Effective pain relief with improved spinal function</p></li><li><p>Reduced dependency on medications and injections</p></li><li><p>Customized therapy tailored to patient condition</p></li><li><p>Safe, controlled, and evidence-based treatment approach</p></li><li><p>Seamless integration with multidisciplinary spine care</p></li></ul>','[]','<p><strong>Is IDD Therapy painful?</strong><br>No, it is generally comfortable with mild stretching sensation.</p><p><strong>How long does a session take?</strong><br>Around 20–45 minutes.</p><p><strong>How many sessions are required?</strong><br>Typically 10–20 sessions depending on the condition.</p><p><strong>Is surgery required after IDD Therapy?</strong><br>In many cases, surgery can be avoided.</p><p><strong>Is it safe for elderly patients?</strong><br>Yes, after proper medical evaluation.</p>','IDD Therapy for Spine & Disc Problems in Bengaluru',NULL,1,'2026-02-19 08:04:45','2026-05-27 04:54:46','Intervertebral Disc Dynamics (IDD) Therapy for Back Pain'),(32,'hysteroscopy','Hysteroscopy','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/373370df-8354-4c7c-b7f6-233e856f3e2e.webp','<p>Hysteroscopy is a minimally invasive gynecological procedure used to examine the inside of the uterus (uterine cavity) using a thin, lighted instrument called a hysteroscope.</p>','<p></p>','<ul><li><p>Evaluates abnormal uterine bleeding</p></li><li><p>Detects fibroids, polyps, adhesions, and uterine abnormalities</p></li><li><p>Assists in infertility evaluation</p></li><li><p>Enables removal of small growths or correction of uterine defects</p></li><li><p>Helps in diagnosis of recurrent miscarriages</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Patient Preparation</strong><br>Patient undergoes clinical evaluation; mild anesthesia or sedation may be given.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Scope Insertion</strong><br>A hysteroscope is gently inserted through the vagina and cervix into the uterus.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Uterine Visualization</strong><br>The uterine cavity is expanded using fluid or gas for clear visualization.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Diagnosis / Treatment</strong><br>Abnormalities are identified and treated (e.g., polyp removal, biopsy).</p><p><strong>Step 5: Completion &amp; Recovery</strong><br>Procedure is completed within a short duration; patient recovers quickly.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Reporting</strong><br>Findings are documented and discussed with the patient.</p>','<p>Hysteroscopy Services at Nano Hospitals are delivered through advanced endoscopic systems, experienced gynecologists, and standardized protocols to ensure safe and precise uterine evaluation and treatment.</p><ul><li><p>High-definition hysteroscopy systems for clear visualization</p></li><li><p>Skilled gynecologists and trained OT staff</p></li><li><p>Day-care procedure setup with minimal hospital stay</p></li><li><p>Safe anesthesia and continuous patient monitoring</p></li><li><p>On-site biopsy and pathology support</p></li><li><p>Integration with fertility, gynecology, and surgical teams</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned safety and quality standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li>