<p>Integration with orthopedics, physiotherapy, and diabetic care units</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned diagnostic and safety standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Early detection of foot and posture problems</p></li><li><p>Pain prevention in feet, knees, and lower back</p></li><li><p>Personalized orthotic solutions</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Helps manage diabetic foot complications</p></li><li><p>Prevents falls and mobility issues in elderly</p></li><li><p>Supports rehabilitation and recovery</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes preventive musculoskeletal health</p></li><li><p>Reduces risk of chronic orthopedic issues</p></li><li><p>Encourages awareness of posture and gait health</p></li></ul>','<p>No significant risks (completely safe procedure)</p><p>Requires expert interpretation of gait data</p><p>May need follow-up assessments for accurate correction</p>','<ul><li><p>Early detection of foot and gait abnormalities</p></li><li><p>Supports customized orthotic insole design</p></li><li><p>Prevents complications in diabetic and elderly patients</p></li><li><p>Improves posture, balance, and walking efficiency</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive, quick, and highly accurate assessment</p></li><li><p>Integrated care approach with multidisciplinary teams</p></li></ul>',NULL,'<p><strong>Is Pedoscan painful?</strong><br>No, it is completely painless and non-invasive.</p><p><strong>How long does it take?</strong><br>Approximately 10–20 minutes.</p><p><strong>Is it safe for diabetic patients?</strong><br>Yes, it is highly recommended for diabetic foot evaluation.</p><p><strong>Do I need special preparation?</strong><br>No preparation is required.</p><p><strong>Can it help with back pain?</strong><br>Yes, improper foot alignment can contribute to back pain, which can be identified through this scan.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-20 06:33:33','2026-03-03 07:06:09',NULL),(34,'bioflex-laser','Bioflex Laser','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/61ca938b-ca9b-4e72-92f0-ec5301c0496a.webp','<p>Bioflex Laser Therapy is an advanced low-level laser therapy (LLLT) used for pain relief, inflammation reduction, and tissue healing.</p>','<p>It utilizes specific wavelengths of light to stimulate cellular repair and improve blood circulation in affected areas.</p>','<ul><li><p>Treats musculoskeletal pain such as back pain, neck pain, and joint pain</p></li><li><p>Effective in sports injuries, ligament sprains, and tendonitis</p></li><li><p>Helps in arthritis management and chronic inflammation</p></li><li><p>Promotes wound healing and tissue regeneration</p></li><li><p>Reduces nerve pain and improves mobility</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Clinical Assessment</strong><br>Patient is evaluated to identify pain areas and treatment suitability.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Treatment Planning</strong><br>Customized laser settings are selected based on condition and severity.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Laser Application</strong><br>Laser probes are applied to the targeted area.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Light Penetration &amp; Therapy</strong><br>Light energy penetrates tissues to stimulate healing and reduce inflammation.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Monitoring</strong><br>Patient response is monitored during the session.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Session Completion &amp; Follow-up</strong><br>Each session lasts 10–30 minutes; multiple sessions may be recommended.</p>','<p>Bioflex Laser Therapy at Nano Hospitals is delivered through advanced laser systems, trained physiotherapists, and evidence-based rehabilitation protocols to ensure safe and effective pain management.</p><ul><li><p>Advanced low-level laser therapy (LLLT) equipment</p></li><li><p>Experienced physiotherapists and rehabilitation specialists</p></li><li><p>Customized treatment protocols based on patient condition</p></li><li><p>Continuous monitoring during therapy sessions</p></li><li><p>Integration with orthopedics, sports medicine, and pain management teams</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned safety and treatment standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Non-invasive and painless treatment</p></li><li><p>Quick pain relief and reduced inflammation</p></li><li><p>Accelerated healing of tissues</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Reduces dependency on pain medications</p></li><li><p>Supports faster recovery from injuries</p></li><li><p>Improves patient comfort and quality of life</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes non-drug pain management solutions</p></li><li><p>Reduces chronic pain burden</p></li><li><p>Encourages advanced physiotherapy care</p></li></ul>','<p>Minimal to no side effects</p><p>Rare mild skin sensitivity</p><p>Requires multiple sessions for optimal results</p><p>Effectiveness depends on proper diagnosis and protocol</p>','<ul><li><p>Effective non-invasive pain relief solution</p></li><li><p>Accelerates tissue healing and recovery</p></li><li><p>Reduces inflammation without medication</p></li><li><p>Improves mobility and functional outcomes</p></li><li><p>Safe, painless, and quick procedure</p></li><li><p>Integrated multidisciplinary rehabilitation approach</p></li></ul>','[]','<p><strong>Is Bioflex Laser Therapy painful?</strong><br>No, it is completely painless.</p><p><strong>How long does a session take?</strong><br>Usually 10–30 minutes.</p><p><strong>How many sessions are required?</strong><br>Depends on the condition; typically multiple sessions are needed.</p><p><strong>Is it safe?</strong><br>Yes, it is safe when performed by trained professionals.</p><p><strong>Can it replace surgery?</strong><br>In some cases, it helps avoid surgery, but it depends on the condition.</p>','Bioflex Laser Therapy Treatment in Bengaluru',NULL,1,'2026-02-20 06:41:28','2026-05-27 04:43:01','Bioflex Laser Therapy for Pain Relief & Healing'),(35,'ncs','NCS','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/e974746b-2866-495d-b31c-50710246983b.webp','<p>Nerve Conduction Study (NCS) is a diagnostic test used to evaluate the function and conduction speed of peripheral nerves.</p>','<p>It measures how quickly electrical signals travel through nerves to detect nerve damage, compression, or dysfunction.</p>','<ul><li><p>Diagnoses nerve disorders such as neuropathy and nerve compression</p></li><li><p>Helps detect conditions like carpal tunnel syndrome and sciatica</p></li><li><p>Evaluates nerve injuries and muscle weakness</p></li><li><p>Assesses diabetic neuropathy and peripheral nerve damage</p></li><li><p>Often performed along with Electromyography (EMG) for comprehensive evaluation</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Patient Preparation</strong><br>Patient is positioned comfortably; no major preparation required.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Electrode Placement</strong><br>Surface electrodes are placed on the skin over specific nerves.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Electrical Stimulation</strong><br>Mild electrical impulses are delivered to stimulate the nerve.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Signal Recording</strong><br>Response signals are recorded to measure conduction speed and strength.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Data Analysis</strong><br>Neurologist analyzes nerve response patterns.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Reporting</strong><br>Results are documented and explained to the patient.</p>','<p>NCS Services at Nano Hospitals are delivered through advanced electrodiagnostic equipment, experienced neurologists, and standardized testing protocols to ensure precise and reliable nerve assessment.</p><ul><li><p>Advanced nerve conduction study systems with high accuracy</p></li><li><p>Skilled neurologists and trained technicians</p></li><li><p>Real-time signal analysis and interpretation</p></li><li><p>Integration with EMG and neurological evaluations</p></li><li><p>Comfortable testing environment with patient monitoring</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned diagnostic and safety standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Accurate diagnosis of nerve-related conditions</p></li><li><p>Helps identify cause of numbness, tingling, or weakness</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive and quick procedure</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Early detection of nerve damage</p></li><li><p>Supports timely medical intervention</p></li><li><p>Helps monitor progression of neurological conditions</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes early diagnosis of neurological disorders</p></li><li><p>Reduces long-term disability from untreated nerve conditions</p></li><li><p>Supports awareness of nerve health and diabetes complications</p></li></ul>','<p>Mild discomfort during electrical stimulation</p><p>No major risks or complications</p><p>Slight discomfort may affect patient cooperation</p><p>Requires expert interpretation for accurate diagnosis</p>','<ul><li><p>Accurate detection of nerve disorders and neuropathies</p></li><li><p>Early diagnosis enabling timely treatment</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive and quick procedure</p></li><li><p>Helps differentiate nerve vs muscle conditions</p></li><li><p>Reliable and reproducible diagnostic results</p></li><li><p>Integrated care with neurology and rehabilitation teams</p></li></ul>','[{\"question\":\"1. Is NCS test available at Nano Hospitals in Hulimavu and Uttarahalli?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Yes, NCS (Nerve Conduction Study) testing is available at both Hulimavu and Uttarahalli branches for diagnosing nerve-related conditions.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"2. What is a Nerve Conduction Study (NCS)?\",\"answer\":\"<p>NCS is a diagnostic test that measures how quickly electrical signals travel through nerves to detect nerve damage.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"3. When is an NCS test recommended?\",\"answer\":\"<p>NCS is recommended for patients experiencing numbness, tingling, muscle weakness, nerve pain, or suspected neuropathy.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"4. What is the cost of NCS test in Bengaluru at Nano Hospitals?\",\"answer\":\"<p>The cost of an NCS test varies based on the number of nerves tested, but Nano Hospitals provides affordable testing in Bengaluru.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"5. How long does an NCS test take?\",\"answer\":\"<p>An NCS test typically takes 30 to 60 minutes depending on the complexity of the case.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"6. Is NCS test painful or uncomfortable?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Patients may feel mild discomfort or tingling during the test, but it is generally well tolerated.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"7. Do I need any preparation before an NCS test?\",\"answer\":\"<p>No major preparation is required, but patients should avoid applying lotions or creams on the skin before the test.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"8. Can NCS detect nerve damage accurately?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Yes, NCS is highly effective in detecting nerve damage, neuropathy, and nerve compression conditions like carpal tunnel syndrome.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"9. Are NCS reports available quickly?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Yes, Nano Hospitals provides accurate and timely reports for faster diagnosis and treatment.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"10. Is NCS safe for all patients?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Yes, NCS is a safe procedure with minimal risks when performed by trained professionals.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"11. Can NCS be done for diabetic patients?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Yes, NCS is commonly used to detect diabetic neuropathy in patients with diabetes.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"12. Is NCS available for emergency cases?\",\"answer\":\"<p>NCS is usually scheduled but may be performed urgently if required for diagnosis.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"13. Why choose Nano Hospitals for NCS test in Bengaluru?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Nano Hospitals offers advanced diagnostic equipment, experienced specialists, accurate results, and affordable pricing in Hulimavu and Uttarahalli.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"14. Can I walk in for an NCS test or is appointment required?\",\"answer\":\"<p>Appointments are recommended, but walk-in patients are accepted based on availability.<\\/p>\"},{\"question\":\"15. What happens after an NCS test?\",\"answer\":\"<p>A specialist reviews the results and recommends further treatment, medication, or additional tests if needed.<\\/p>\"}]','<p><strong>Is NCS painful?</strong><br>It may cause mild tingling or discomfort but is generally well tolerated.</p><p><strong>How long does the test take?</strong><br>Approximately 20–45 minutes.</p><p><strong>Is fasting required?</strong><br>No, fasting is not required.</p><p><strong>Can it detect nerve damage?</strong><br>Yes, it is specifically used to detect nerve damage and dysfunction.</p><p><strong>Is it safe for elderly patients?</strong><br>Yes, it is safe and commonly performed in all age groups.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-20 06:46:44','2026-05-05 12:40:35',NULL),(36,'neurotouch','Neurotouch','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/bb87e0c5-58e0-42a1-97fe-41cd0272a711.webp','<p>NeuroTouch is an advanced neuro-rehabilitation therapy system designed to improve sensory and motor function in patients with neurological conditions</p>','<p>It uses sensor-based, interactive technology to stimulate nerve pathways, enhance coordination, and promote functional recovery.</p>','<ul><li><p>Used in stroke rehabilitation and nerve injury recovery</p></li><li><p>Improves hand function, grip strength, and coordination</p></li><li><p>Enhances sensory feedback and motor control</p></li><li><p>Supports recovery in conditions like paralysis and neuropathy</p></li><li><p>Aids in cognitive-motor integration and functional independence</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Clinical Assessment</strong><br>Patient is evaluated for neurological deficits and functional limitations.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Therapy Planning</strong><br>Customized rehabilitation protocol is designed based on patient needs.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Device Setup</strong><br>Patient interacts with NeuroTouch system using hands or affected limbs.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Sensor-Based Training</strong><br>Interactive exercises stimulate nerves and improve motor response.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Real-Time Feedback</strong><br>System provides visual and sensory feedback for performance improvement.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Progress Monitoring &amp; Reporting</strong><br>Therapy outcomes are tracked and adjusted over sessions.</p>','<p>NeuroTouch Therapy at Nano Hospitals is delivered through advanced neuro-rehabilitation systems, trained therapists, and personalized therapy protocols to ensure effective neurological recovery.</p><ul><li><p>Sensor-based NeuroTouch rehabilitation systems</p></li><li><p>Experienced physiotherapists and neuro-rehabilitation specialists</p></li><li><p>Customized therapy programs based on patient condition</p></li><li><p>Real-time performance tracking and feedback</p></li><li><p>Integration with neurology, physiotherapy, and rehabilitation teams</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned safety and care standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Improves motor skills and coordination</p></li><li><p>Enhances sensory recovery</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive and engaging therapy</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Faster rehabilitation outcomes</p></li><li><p>Improved patient confidence and functionality</p></li><li><p>Reduced long-term disability burden</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Supports advanced neurological rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Reduces long-term impact of stroke and nerve injuries</p></li><li><p>Promotes awareness of neuro-recovery technologies</p></li></ul>','<p>No significant risks (safe and non-invasive)</p><p>Requires multiple therapy sessions for optimal results</p><p>Effectiveness depends on patient engagement and consistency</p>','<ul><li><p>Enhances neurological recovery and motor function</p></li><li><p>Improves coordination, strength, and sensory feedback</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive and patient-friendly therapy</p></li><li><p>Data-driven progress monitoring</p></li><li><p>Supports faster and more effective rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Integrated multidisciplinary neuro-care approach</p></li></ul>',NULL,'<p><strong>Is NeuroTouch therapy painful?</strong><br>No, it is completely painless and non-invasive.</p><p><strong>How long does a session take?</strong><br>Typically 20–45 minutes.</p><p><strong>Who can benefit from NeuroTouch?</strong><br>Patients with stroke, nerve injuries, or neurological disorders.</p><p><strong>Is it safe for elderly patients?</strong><br>Yes, it is safe and beneficial for all age groups.</p><p><strong>How many sessions are required?</strong><br>Depends on the condition; usually multiple sessions are recommended.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-20 06:51:01','2026-03-03 06:55:39',NULL),(37,'abi','ABI','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/015cab27-5a79-492c-8b2a-85fd90afb55b.webp','<p>Ankle-Brachial Index (ABI) is a simple, non-invasive diagnostic test used to compare blood pressure in the ankle and arm to assess blood flow and detect peripheral artery disease (PAD)</p>','<p>It helps identify blockages or narrowing in the arteries of the lower limbs.</p>','<ul><li><p>Detects peripheral artery disease (PAD)</p></li><li><p>Assesses risk of poor circulation in legs</p></li><li><p>Useful in diabetic and high-risk cardiac patients</p></li><li><p>Helps evaluate leg pain during walking (claudication)</p></li><li><p>Assists in monitoring vascular treatment outcomes</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Patient Positioning</strong><br>Patient lies in a relaxed, supine position.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Blood Pressure Measurement (Arm)</strong><br>Blood pressure cuff is placed on the arm and readings are taken.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Blood Pressure Measurement (Ankle)</strong><br>Cuff is placed on the ankle; Doppler device measures arterial pressure.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Ratio Calculation</strong><br>Ankle pressure is divided by arm pressure to calculate ABI.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Interpretation</strong><br>Values are analyzed to determine normal or reduced blood flow.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Reporting</strong><br>Results are documented and explained to the patient.</p>','<p>ABI Testing at Nano Hospitals is delivered through advanced Doppler systems, trained vascular specialists, and standardized protocols to ensure accurate and reliable vascular assessment.</p><ul><li><p>Handheld Doppler devices for precise pressure measurement</p></li><li><p>Trained technicians and vascular specialists</p></li><li><p>Quick, outpatient-based screening procedure</p></li><li><p>Integration with cardiology, diabetology, and vascular surgery teams</p></li><li><p>Immediate reporting for timely clinical decision-making</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned diagnostic and safety standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Early detection of circulation problems</p></li><li><p>Painless and quick screening test</p></li><li><p>Helps prevent serious complications like ulcers or amputation</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Identifies vascular risks early</p></li><li><p>Supports preventive care and lifestyle modification</p></li><li><p>Reduces complications from untreated PAD</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes awareness of vascular health</p></li><li><p>Reduces incidence of limb-related complications</p></li><li><p>Supports preventive screening programs</p></li></ul>','<p>No significant risks (completely safe procedure)</p><p>Accuracy may vary in patients with calcified arteries (e.g., diabetes)</p><p>Requires proper technique for reliable results</p>','<ul><li><p>Early detection of peripheral artery disease (PAD)</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive, quick, and cost-effective screening</p></li><li><p>Helps prevent serious complications like ulcers and amputations</p></li><li><p>Ideal for diabetic and high-risk patients</p></li><li><p>Supports timely intervention and treatment planning</p></li><li><p>Integrated care with multidisciplinary vascular and cardiac teams</p></li></ul>','[]','<p><strong>Is ABI test painful?</strong><br>No, it is completely painless.</p><p><strong>How long does it take?</strong><br>Approximately 10–15 minutes.</p><p><strong>Is fasting required?</strong><br>No preparation or fasting is required.</p><p><strong>Can it detect blocked arteries?</strong><br>Yes, it helps detect reduced blood flow due to blockages.</p><p><strong>Is it safe for elderly patients?</strong><br>Yes, it is safe and recommended for vascular screening.</p>','ABI Test for Peripheral Arterial Disease in Bengaluru',NULL,1,'2026-02-20 07:04:08','2026-05-27 04:30:36','Ankle-Brachial Index (ABI) Testing & Vascular Screening'),(38,'non-stress-test','Non-Stress Test (NST)','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/0c44fc2d-8fcf-4ad2-9502-2d8d87761568.webp','<p>Non-Stress Test (NST) is a non-invasive prenatal test used to monitor fetal heart rate and its response to movements.</p>','<p>. It helps assess the well-being of the fetus, especially in high-risk pregnancies. The test measures whether the baby’s heart rate increases appropriately with movement, indicating adequate oxygen supply.</p>','<ul><li><p>Evaluates fetal health and oxygenation</p></li><li><p>Monitors fetal heart rate in response to movements</p></li><li><p>Used in high-risk pregnancies (diabetes, hypertension, etc.)</p></li><li><p>Helps detect fetal distress or compromised conditions</p></li><li><p>Often performed in late pregnancy or when reduced fetal movements are noted</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Patient Preparation</strong><br>Mother is positioned comfortably, usually in a semi-reclining position.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Sensor Placement</strong><br>Two belts are placed on the abdomen—one for fetal heart rate and one for uterine activity.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Monitoring</strong><br>Fetal heart rate and movements are recorded over time.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Data Recording</strong><br>Graph (CTG tracing) is generated showing heart rate patterns.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Interpretation</strong><br>Doctor evaluates reactivity and variability of fetal heart rate.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Reporting</strong><br>Results are documented and explained to the patient.</p>','<p>NST Services at Nano Hospitals are delivered through advanced fetal monitoring systems, experienced obstetricians, and standardized antenatal care protocols to ensure accurate fetal assessment.</p><ul><li><p>Advanced cardiotocography (CTG) machines for real-time monitoring</p></li><li><p>Experienced obstetricians and trained nursing staff</p></li><li><p>Comfortable antenatal monitoring setup</p></li><li><p>Immediate evaluation and reporting of results</p></li><li><p>Integration with maternity, NICU, and emergency services</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned safety and maternal care standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Non-invasive and painless monitoring</p></li><li><p>Provides reassurance about baby’s well-being</p></li><li><p>Early detection of fetal distress</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Immediate information about fetal health</p></li><li><p>Reduces anxiety in high-risk pregnancies</p></li><li><p>Supports safe pregnancy management</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes safe maternal and fetal care</p></li><li><p>Reduces risk of complications during pregnancy</p></li><li><p>Encourages routine prenatal monitoring</p></li></ul>','<p>No significant risks (completely safe for mother and baby)</p><p>May require repeat testing if results are inconclusive</p><p>Interpretation depends on clinical expertise</p>','<ul><li><p>Early detection of fetal distress and complications</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive, safe, and reliable monitoring method</p></li><li><p>Provides real-time fetal heart rate assessment</p></li><li><p>Supports better decision-making in high-risk pregnancies</p></li><li><p>Quick and repeatable test without risk</p></li><li><p>Integrated care with obstetrics and neonatal teams</p></li></ul>',NULL,'<p><strong>Is NST painful?</strong><br>No, it is completely painless.</p><p><strong>How long does the test take?</strong><br>Usually 20–40 minutes.</p><p><strong>Is fasting required?</strong><br>No, no preparation is needed.</p><p><strong>When is NST recommended?</strong><br>Usually in the third trimester or high-risk pregnancies.</p><p><strong>Is it safe for all pregnancies?</strong><br>Yes, it is safe and widely used.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-20 07:09:14','2026-02-24 12:39:39',NULL),(39,'ust-ift-ultrasound-therapy-interferential-therapy','UST + IFT (Ultrasound Therapy + Interferential Therapy)','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/66342b03-44af-4d66-abc4-694d3db91f6a.webp','<p>UST (Ultrasound Therapy) + IFT (Interferential Therapy) is a combined physiotherapy treatment used for pain relief, inflammation reduction, and tissue healing</p>','<p>UST uses high-frequency sound waves to penetrate deep tissues, while IFT uses low-frequency electrical stimulation to relieve pain and improve circulation.</p>','<ul><li><p>Treats joint pain, muscle spasms, and ligament injuries</p></li><li><p>Effective for back pain, neck pain, and frozen shoulder</p></li><li><p>Helps reduce inflammation and swelling</p></li><li><p>Improves blood circulation and tissue healing</p></li><li><p>Used in sports injuries and post-surgical rehabilitation</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Clinical Assessment</strong><br>Physiotherapist evaluates pain area and condition.</p><p><strong>Step 2: UST Application</strong><br>Ultrasound gel is applied, and sound waves are delivered to deep tissues.</p><p><strong>Step 3: IFT Setup</strong><br>Electrodes are placed around the affected area.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Electrical Stimulation</strong><br>Low-frequency currents stimulate nerves and reduce pain.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Monitoring</strong><br>Therapy intensity is adjusted based on patient comfort.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Session Completion</strong><br>Session typically lasts 15–30 minutes; multiple sessions may be required.</p>','<p>UST + IFT Therapy at Nano Hospitals is delivered through advanced physiotherapy equipment, trained rehabilitation specialists, and evidence-based treatment protocols to ensure effective pain management and recovery.</p><ul><li><p>Modern ultrasound therapy and interferential therapy machines</p></li><li><p>Experienced physiotherapists and rehabilitation experts</p></li><li><p>Customized therapy plans based on patient condition</p></li><li><p>Continuous monitoring during sessions for safety and comfort</p></li><li><p>Integration with orthopedics, sports medicine, and pain management teams</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned safety and physiotherapy standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Effective pain relief without medication</p></li><li><p>Faster healing of muscles and soft tissues</p></li><li><p>Reduced inflammation and stiffness</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Faster recovery from injuries</p></li><li><p>Reduced dependency on painkillers</p></li><li><p>Improved patient comfort and daily functioning</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes non-invasive rehabilitation methods</p></li><li><p>Reduces chronic pain burden</p></li><li><p>Encourages physiotherapy-based recovery</p></li></ul>','<p>Mild skin irritation from electrodes (rare)</p><p>Temporary discomfort during stimulation</p><p>Requires multiple sessions for optimal results</p><p>Effectiveness depends on correct technique and consistency</p>','<ul><li><p>Combined therapy for enhanced pain relief and healing</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive and drug-free treatment option</p></li><li><p>Improves mobility and reduces stiffness</p></li><li><p>Accelerates recovery in musculoskeletal conditions</p></li><li><p>Safe, controlled, and patient-friendly procedure</p></li><li><p>Integrated rehabilitation approach with multidisciplinary care</p></li></ul>',NULL,'<p><strong>Is UST + IFT painful?</strong><br>No, it is generally comfortable; mild tingling may be felt during IFT.</p><p><strong>How long does a session take?</strong><br>Around 15–30 minutes.</p><p><strong>How many sessions are required?</strong><br>Depends on the condition; usually multiple sessions are needed.</p><p><strong>Is it safe?</strong><br>Yes, it is safe when performed by trained professionals.</p><p><strong>Can it replace medication?</strong><br>It can reduce the need for pain medications in many cases.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-20 07:14:18','2026-02-24 12:47:49',NULL),(40,'lymphopress','Lymphopress','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/66ec63cd-48be-4047-a435-86b711259369.webp','<p>Lymphopress Therapy is an advanced pneumatic compression treatment designed to improve lymphatic circulation and reduce fluid retention in the body</p>','<p>It uses controlled air pressure through specialized sleeves or boots to stimulate lymph flow, reduce swelling, and enhance detoxification.</p>','<ul><li><p>Treats lymphedema (swelling due to lymphatic fluid accumulation)</p></li><li><p>Reduces leg swelling, edema, and fluid retention</p></li><li><p>Supports recovery after surgery or injury</p></li><li><p>Improves blood circulation and detoxification</p></li><li><p>Helps in managing varicose veins and chronic venous insufficiency</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Clinical Assessment</strong><br>Patient is evaluated for swelling, circulation issues, and suitability.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Garment Application</strong><br>Compression sleeves/boots are placed on the affected limbs.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Device Setup</strong><br>Lymphopress machine is programmed with appropriate pressure settings.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Sequential Compression</strong><br>Air pressure is applied in cycles to stimulate lymphatic drainage.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Monitoring</strong><br>Therapy is monitored for comfort and effectiveness.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Session Completion</strong><br>Session lasts 20–45 minutes; multiple sessions may be recommended.</p>','<p>Lymphopress Therapy at Nano Hospitals is delivered through advanced pneumatic compression systems, trained physiotherapists, and structured treatment protocols to ensure safe and effective lymphatic drainage.</p><ul><li><p>Advanced Lymphopress compression therapy machines</p></li><li><p>Experienced physiotherapists and rehabilitation specialists</p></li><li><p>Customized pressure settings based on patient condition</p></li><li><p>Continuous monitoring for safety and comfort</p></li><li><p>Integration with vascular care, physiotherapy, and post-surgical rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned safety and care standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Faster diagnosis and treatment initiation</p></li><li><p>Reduced complications during critical conditions</p></li><li><p>Improved survival and recovery outcomes</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Reassurance that expert care is always available</p></li><li><p>Clear communication during stressful moments</p></li><li><p>Confidence in timely, ethical medical decisions</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Reliable emergency medical access at all times</p></li><li><p>Reduced risks associated with delayed care</p></li><li><p>Stronger emergency response support for the region</p></li></ul>','<p>Mild discomfort if pressure is too high</p><p>Not suitable for certain conditions (e.g., acute infections, severe cardiac issues)</p><p>Requires multiple sessions for sustained results</p>','<ul><li><p>Effective reduction of swelling and fluid retention</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive and comfortable therapy</p></li><li><p>Improves lymphatic and blood circulation</p></li><li><p>Supports faster recovery after surgery or injury</p></li><li><p>Reduces discomfort and heaviness in limbs</p></li><li><p>Integrated care approach with multidisciplinary teams</p></li></ul>',NULL,'<p><strong>Is Lymphopress Therapy painful?</strong><br>No, it is generally comfortable and relaxing.</p><p><strong>How long does a session take?</strong><br>Typically 20–45 minutes.</p><p><strong>Is it safe?</strong><br>Yes, when performed under medical supervision.</p><p><strong>Who can benefit from this therapy?</strong><br>Patients with swelling, lymphedema, or circulation issues.</p><p><strong>How many sessions are required?</strong><br>Depends on the condition; multiple sessions are usually recommended.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-02-20 07:30:28','2026-02-24 12:37:46',NULL),(41,'cuff-cryotherapy','CUFF/ CRYOTHERAPY','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/adfcbb20-e292-4c4f-aff6-dc2c6df67836.webp','<p>Cuff / Cryotherapy is a therapeutic treatment that uses controlled cold temperature combined with compression to reduce pain, swelling, and inflammation</p>','<p>It is commonly used in orthopedic injuries, post-surgical recovery, and sports rehabilitation.</p>','<ul><li><p>Reduces swelling and inflammation after injury or surgery</p></li><li><p>Provides pain relief in joints and soft tissues</p></li><li><p>Used in conditions like ligament injuries, fractures, and arthritis</p></li><li><p>Supports post-operative recovery (knee, shoulder, etc.)</p></li><li><p>Enhances healing by reducing tissue damage</p></li></ul>','<p><strong>Step 1: Clinical Assessment</strong><br>Patient is evaluated for injury, swelling, and treatment suitability.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Cuff Application</strong><br>Cold therapy cuff is placed around the affected area (knee, shoulder, ankle, etc.).</p><p><strong>Step 3: Device Setup</strong><br>Cryotherapy unit is connected to circulate chilled water.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Cold Compression Therapy</strong><br>Controlled cold and compression are applied simultaneously.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Monitoring</strong><br>Therapy intensity and duration are adjusted for patient comfort.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Session Completion</strong><br>Session lasts 15–30 minutes; repeated sessions may be advised.</p>','<p>Cuff / Cryotherapy at Nano Hospitals is delivered through advanced cold compression systems, trained physiotherapists, and evidence-based rehabilitation protocols to ensure effective pain and swelling management.</p><ul><li><p>Advanced cryotherapy units with controlled temperature and compression</p></li><li><p>Specialized cuffs for different body parts (knee, shoulder, ankle, etc.)</p></li><li><p>Experienced physiotherapists and rehabilitation experts</p></li><li><p>Customized therapy plans based on injury and recovery stage</p></li><li><p>Continuous monitoring for patient safety and comfort</p></li><li><p>Integration with orthopedics, sports medicine, and post-surgical care</p></li><li><p>NABH-aligned safety and treatment standards</p></li></ul>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Rapid pain relief</p></li><li><p>Reduced swelling and inflammation</p></li><li><p>Faster recovery after injury or surgery</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Helps manage post-surgical care effectively</p></li><li><p>Reduces need for pain medications</p></li><li><p>Supports quicker patient recovery</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes effective injury management</p></li><li><p>Reduces complications from untreated inflammation</p></li><li><p>Encourages sports injury rehabilitation awareness</p></li></ul>','<p>Temporary skin numbness or redness</p><p>Risk of cold injury if used improperly (rare)</p><p>Requires proper duration and monitoring</p><p>Not suitable for patients with cold sensitivity conditions</p>','<ul><li><p>Effective pain and inflammation control</p></li><li><p>Accelerates recovery after injury or surgery</p></li><li><p>Non-invasive and drug-free treatment</p></li><li><p>Improves joint mobility and function</p></li><li><p>Safe, controlled, and easy-to-administer therapy</p></li><li><p>Integrated rehabilitation approach with multidisciplinary care</p></li></ul>','[]','<p><strong>Is Cryotherapy painful?</strong><br>No, it provides a cooling sensation and pain relief.</p><p><strong>How long does a session take?</strong><br>Typically 15–30 minutes.</p><p><strong>Is it safe?</strong><br>Yes, when used under proper supervision.</p><p><strong>How often can it be used?</strong><br>As advised by the physiotherapist, often multiple times a day in acute cases.</p><p><strong>Can it be used after surgery?</strong><br>Yes, it is commonly used for post-operative recovery.</p>','Cryotherapy & Recovery Treatment in Bengaluru',NULL,1,'2026-02-20 07:38:21','2026-05-27 04:46:54','CUFF Cryotherapy for Pain Relief & Recovery'),(42,'icu','ICU','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/ae223eb3-8987-42f6-952f-2b47a997450c.webp','<p>The <strong>Intensive Care Unit (ICU)</strong> is a specialized hospital department designed to provide <strong>continuous monitoring, advanced life support, and critical care treatment</strong> for patients with life-threatening conditions.</p>','<p>ICU care involves highly trained doctors, specialized nurses, advanced monitoring systems, and life-support technologies to stabilize and treat critically ill patients.</p>','<p>• Provides <strong>24/7 monitoring of critically ill patients</strong></p><p>• Supports <strong>vital organ functions such as breathing, heart activity, and blood circulation</strong></p><p>• Manages <strong>severe infections, trauma, and organ failure</strong></p><p>• Provides care for <strong>patients after major surgeries</strong></p><p>• Stabilizes patients from <strong>medical emergencies like cardiac arrest or stroke</strong></p>','<p><strong>Step 1: Admission &amp; Risk Assessment</strong><br>Patients are admitted based on severity and clinical need, often from the Emergency Department, Operation Theatres, or other hospital units.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Stabilisation &amp; Life Support</strong><br>Immediate interventions may include ventilatory support, intravenous medications, fluid therapy, and emergency stabilization procedures.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Continuous Monitoring</strong><br>Advanced monitoring systems track vital parameters such as heart rate, blood pressure, oxygen levels, and organ function.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Critical Care Treatment</strong><br>Specialized treatments are provided for conditions such as severe infections, respiratory failure, cardiac complications, or organ dysfunction.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Multidisciplinary Care</strong><br>A team of intensivists, nurses, physiotherapists, and specialists collaborate to ensure comprehensive treatment and recovery.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Recovery &amp; Step-Down Care</strong><br>Once the patient&#039;s condition stabilizes, they may be shifted to a step-down unit or general ward for further recovery.</p>','<p>ICU services at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> are designed to deliver <strong>advanced critical care with modern technology, skilled specialists, and patient-centered treatment protocols</strong>.</p><p>• Advanced life-support equipment and ventilators</p><p>• Continuous patient monitoring systems</p><p>• Experienced intensivists and critical care specialists</p><p>• Dedicated ICU nursing staff available 24/7</p><p>• Infection control and sterile ICU environment</p><p>• Integration with emergency medicine, surgery, and specialty departments</p><p>• NABH-aligned patient safety and critical care standards</p>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Rapid pain relief</p></li><li><p>Reduced swelling and inflammation</p></li><li><p>Faster recovery after injury or surgery</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Helps manage post-surgical care effectively</p></li><li><p>Reduces need for pain medications</p></li><li><p>Supports quicker patient recovery</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes effective injury management</p></li><li><p>Reduces complications from untreated inflammation</p></li><li><p>Encourages sports injury rehabilitation awareness</p></li></ul>','<p>• ICU care requires <strong>continuous monitoring and specialized staff</strong></p><p>• Strict infection control protocols are maintained</p><p>• Advanced equipment requires <strong>trained medical supervision</strong></p><p>• Patient recovery may require <strong>gradual step-down care</strong></p>','<p>• Advanced life-support and monitoring technologies</p><p>• Highly trained critical care specialists</p><p>• Rapid response to medical emergencies</p><p>• Continuous patient observation and care</p><p>• Multidisciplinary treatment approach</p>','[]','<p><strong>What conditions require ICU care?</strong><br>Conditions such as severe infections, respiratory failure, heart attacks, trauma, stroke, and major post-surgical recovery may require ICU care.</p><p><strong>Are patients monitored continuously in the ICU?</strong><br>Yes, patients are monitored 24/7 using advanced medical equipment and trained staff.</p><p><strong>Can family members visit ICU patients?</strong><br>Visiting hours are usually limited to maintain patient safety and infection control.</p><p><strong>How long do patients stay in the ICU?</strong><br>The duration varies depending on the patient’s condition and response to treatment.</p><p><strong>What happens after ICU treatment?</strong><br>Once stable, patients are transferred to a step-down unit or general ward for further recovery.</p>','24/7 ICU & Critical Care Services in Bengaluru',NULL,1,'2026-03-04 08:26:37','2026-05-27 04:53:37','Advanced Intensive Care Unit (ICU) Facilities'),(43,'nicu','NICU','Explore Jobs',NULL,'health-facilities/f21189d3-1d98-4da8-a2f3-281c0f397b2f.webp','<p>The <strong>Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU)</strong> is a specialized department dedicated to the <strong>care of premature, low-birth-weight, and critically ill newborns</strong> who require advanced medical support immediately after birth.</p>','<p>NICU care combines <strong>specialized neonatal doctors, trained nurses, advanced incubators, and life-support systems</strong> to ensure newborns receive the safest and most comprehensive care during their early days of life.</p>','<p>• Provides <strong>advanced care for premature and low-birth-weight babies</strong></p><p>• Supports newborns with <strong>breathing difficulties or infections</strong></p><p>• Manages <strong>congenital conditions and birth complications</strong></p><p>• Provides <strong>temperature-controlled incubator care</strong></p><p>• Monitors vital signs such as <strong>heart rate, oxygen levels, and breathing</strong></p>','<p><strong>Step 1: Admission &amp; Initial Assessment</strong><br>Newborns requiring specialized care are admitted from the Labour Room, Operation Theatre, or referral centers. A detailed assessment of breathing, heart rate, weight, and overall condition is performed.</p><p><strong>Step 2: Stabilisation &amp; Immediate Care</strong><br>Doctors initiate immediate interventions such as oxygen therapy, temperature regulation in incubators, intravenous fluids, and medications if required.</p><p><strong>Step 3: Continuous Monitoring</strong><br>Advanced neonatal monitors track the baby’s heart rate, oxygen saturation, breathing pattern, and body temperature.</p><p><strong>Step 4: Specialized Neonatal Treatment</strong><br>Treatment may include respiratory support, phototherapy for jaundice, infection management, and nutritional support through feeding tubes if necessary.</p><p><strong>Step 5: Developmental &amp; Nutritional Care</strong><br>NICU teams ensure proper nutrition, growth monitoring, and developmental support to help the baby gain strength.</p><p><strong>Step 6: Recovery &amp; Discharge Planning</strong><br>Once the newborn is stable, feeding well, and maintaining body temperature independently, the baby is prepared for safe discharge with parental guidance.</p>','<p>The <strong>NICU at Nano Hospitals</strong> is designed to provide <strong>safe, advanced neonatal care for vulnerable newborns</strong> through specialized equipment and experienced neonatal teams.</p><p>• Advanced neonatal incubators and warmers</p><p>• Continuous monitoring systems for newborn vital signs</p><p>• Ventilators and respiratory support systems for infants</p><p>• Experienced neonatologists and trained NICU nurses</p><p>• Infection-controlled sterile NICU environment</p><p>• Integration with obstetrics, pediatrics, and emergency services</p><p>• NABH-aligned neonatal care and safety standards</p>','<h3>For Patients</h3><ul><li><p>Rapid pain relief</p></li><li><p>Reduced swelling and inflammation</p></li><li><p>Faster recovery after injury or surgery</p></li></ul><h3>For Caregivers &amp; Families</h3><ul><li><p>Helps manage post-surgical care effectively</p></li><li><p>Reduces need for pain medications</p></li><li><p>Supports quicker patient recovery</p></li></ul><h3>For the Community</h3><ul><li><p>Promotes effective injury management</p></li><li><p>Reduces complications from untreated inflammation</p></li><li><p>Encourages sports injury rehabilitation awareness</p></li></ul>','<p>• Strict <strong>infection control protocols</strong> are followed</p><p>• Babies are monitored <strong>24/7 by specialized NICU staff</strong></p><p>• Some newborns may require <strong>extended stay for growth and monitoring</strong></p><p>• Parents receive <strong>education on newborn care before discharge</strong></p>','<p>• Specialized care designed exclusively for newborns</p><p>• Advanced neonatal monitoring and life-support equipment</p><p>• Highly trained neonatologists and NICU nurses</p><p>• Safe temperature-controlled environment for premature babies</p><p>• Early detection and treatment of neonatal complications</p>',NULL,'<p><strong>Which babies need NICU care?</strong><br>Premature babies, low-birth-weight newborns, babies with breathing problems, infections, or birth complications may require NICU care.</p><p><strong>Can parents visit their baby in the NICU?</strong><br>Yes, most hospitals allow controlled parental visits while maintaining strict infection control protocols.</p><p><strong>How long do babies stay in the NICU?</strong><br>The duration varies depending on the baby’s condition, growth, and ability to feed and breathe independently.</p><p><strong>Is NICU care safe for newborns?</strong><br>Yes, NICUs follow strict medical protocols and continuous monitoring to ensure the safety of newborns.</p><p><strong>What happens after NICU discharge?</strong><br>Parents receive guidance on feeding, hygiene, follow-up visits, and developmental monitoring for the baby.</p>',NULL,NULL,1,'2026-03-04 08:30:54','2026-03-04 08:31:32',NULL);
