s, voice box, and related head and neck structures.</p>','<p>ENT problems often begin with common symptoms such as ear pain, hearing difficulty, nasal blockage, sinus headaches, sore throat, or voice changes. While many issues are mild, persistent or recurrent symptoms can indicate infections, structural problems, allergies, or more serious conditions. At Nano Hospitals, care is directed toward relieving symptoms, restoring normal function, and preventing complications.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, endoscopic assessment, hearing tests, imaging, and when needed, medical or surgical intervention. Care plans are tailored according to age, symptom severity, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>','<p>Otolaryngology (ENT) deals with conditions of hearing, balance, breathing, speech, and swallowing. Early symptoms such as persistent nasal congestion, frequent throat infections, dizziness, or hearing loss should not be ignored.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis using endoscopy, audiology testing, and imaging, followed by personalised treatment and rehabilitation when required.</p>','<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Medical treatment for ear, sinus, and throat infections</p></li><li><p>Allergy management and nasal spray therapy</p></li><li><p>Hearing aid fitting and hearing rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Voice therapy for vocal strain or hoarseness</p></li><li><p>Management of vertigo and balance disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Nasal endoscopy for sinus and nasal evaluation</p></li><li><p>Ear microsuction and minor ear procedures</p></li><li><p>Endoscopic sinus procedures</p></li><li><p>Injection therapy for vocal cord disorders</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Tonsillectomy and adenoidectomy</p></li><li><p>Functional Endoscopic Sinus Surgery (FESS)</p></li><li><p>Ear surgeries including eardrum repair</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and salivary gland surgeries</p></li><li><p>Head and neck tumor surgeries (in coordination with oncology)</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Nasal endoscopy and laryngoscopy systems</p></li><li><p>Audiometry and hearing assessment labs</p></li><li><p>CT Scan for sinus and temporal bone imaging</p></li><li><p>Microscopic ear surgery equipment</p></li><li><p>Voice analysis and speech therapy support</p></li><li><p>Dedicated ENT operation theatres</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Sinusitis and nasal polyps</p></li><li><p>Allergic rhinitis</p></li><li><p>Hearing loss and ear infections</p></li><li><p>Tinnitus (ringing in ears)</p></li><li><p>Tonsillitis and throat infections</p></li><li><p>Voice disorders</p></li><li><p>Vertigo and balance disorders</p></li><li><p>Deviated nasal septum (DNS)</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and salivary gland conditions</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Chronic sinus infections affecting breathing and sleep</p></li><li><p>Progressive hearing loss if untreated</p></li><li><p>Recurrent throat infections in children</p></li><li><p>Voice strain impacting communication</p></li><li><p>Balance disorders increasing fall risk</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Otology (Ear and Hearing Care)</p></li><li><p>Rhinology (Nose and Sinus Care)</p></li><li><p>Laryngology (Voice and Throat Care)</p></li><li><p>Head and Neck Surgery</p></li><li><p>Pediatric ENT</p></li></ul>','ENT Specialist in Bangalore | Ear Nose Throat Treatment – Nano Hospitals','Consult experienced ENT specialists in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals for sinus issues, ear infections, hearing problems, and throat conditions with advanced care.','2026-02-02 12:21:52','2026-04-21 07:45:20','specialities/banners/relatedimages/8b867e2e-4698-4bcf-a6c3-e53687f62a85.webp'),(16,'Psychiatry','psychiatry','specialities/banners/681b1fd5-4b29-44d4-b38d-5e4678c0cc16.webp','specialities/icons/01KGJ8JN4V85FV52HK507DG7C1.webp',1,'<p>Psychiatry at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term support of emotional, psychological, and behavioral health conditions. The department addresses challenges that affect mood, thinking, stress management, relationships, and overall mental well-being.</p>','<p>Psychiatry concerns may begin with subtle signs such as persistent stress, sleep disturbances, mood swings, difficulty concentrating, social withdrawal, or loss of interest in daily activities. If not addressed early, these issues can interfere with work performance, relationships, physical health, and quality of life. At Nano Hospitals, care is aimed not only at symptom relief but also at helping individuals regain emotional balance, resilience, and confidence.</p><p>Care is delivered through a compassionate, patient-centred approach that combines psychiatric evaluation, psychological therapies, medication when needed, and lifestyle-based mental wellness strategies. Each care plan is personalised based on age, life circumstances, medical history, and individual goals.</p>','<p>Psychiatry involves understanding how thoughts, emotions, and behaviors influence overall well-being. Early signs such as prolonged sadness, excessive worry, panic attacks, changes in appetite, or difficulty coping with daily stress should not be ignored.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early identification, confidential consultations, structured therapy programs, and long-term follow-up to support emotional stability and mental resilience.</p>','<h3>Non-Medication Therapies</h3><ul><li><p>Individual psychotherapy (talk therapy)</p></li><li><p>Cognitive Behavioral Therapy (CBT)</p></li><li><p>Stress management and relaxation therapy</p></li><li><p>Family and relationship counseling</p></li><li><p>Behavioral therapy for children and adolescents</p></li></ul><h3>Medication-Based Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Antidepressant and anti-anxiety medications</p></li><li><p>Mood stabilisers for bipolar disorder</p></li><li><p>Medication management for psychotic disorders</p></li><li><p>Sleep disorder treatment</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive and Advanced Care</h3><ul><li><p>De-addiction and substance use rehabilitation programs</p></li><li><p>Crisis intervention and emergency mental health care</p></li><li><p>Mindfulness and coping skill training</p></li><li><p>Occupational and social rehabilitation support</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Private and confidential consultation rooms</p></li><li><p>Psychological testing and assessment tools</p></li><li><p>Therapy and counseling suites</p></li><li><p>Day-care mental health programs</p></li><li><p>Inpatient mental health support (when required)</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation and follow-up care services</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Depression and mood disorders</p></li><li><p>Anxiety disorders and panic attacks</p></li><li><p>Stress-related disorders</p></li><li><p>Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder (OCD)</p></li><li><p>Bipolar disorder</p></li><li><p>Schizophrenia and psychotic disorders</p></li><li><p>Sleep disorders</p></li><li><p>Substance use and addiction</p></li><li><p>Emotional and behavioral issues in children and adolescents</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Impact on work, studies, and relationships</p></li><li><p>Physical health problems linked to chronic stress</p></li><li><p>Social withdrawal and isolation</p></li><li><p>Risk of self-harm if severe symptoms are untreated</p></li><li><p>Stigma preventing timely help-seeking</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Adult Psychiatry</p></li><li><p>Child and Adolescent Psychiatry</p></li><li><p>Clinical Psychology</p></li><li><p>De-addiction Psychiatry</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Mental Health Care</p></li></ul>','Best Mental Health Hospital in Bangalore | Psychiatry at Nano Hospitals','Get comprehensive psychiatry support in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Expert care for anxiety, depression, and overall psychological well-being.','2026-02-02 12:24:19','2026-05-12 10:03:10','specialities/banners/relatedimages/60a96ce2-5665-4524-9924-43b042a8ca6c.webp'),(17,'Rheumatology','rheumatology','specialities/banners/5caa94a9-dc01-41b9-9150-232f38ff5266.webp','specialities/icons/01KGJ8YH5EY1KCNNYK5PF1XCQF.webp',1,'<p>Rheumatology at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis, treatment, and long-term management of autoimmune and inflammatory diseases that primarily affect joints, muscles, bones, and connective tissues.</p>','<p>Rheumatologic conditions often begin gradually with symptoms such as joint pain, morning stiffness, swelling, fatigue, or muscle weakness. These disorders can be chronic and progressive, sometimes affecting internal organs like the lungs, heart, kidneys, or skin. At Nano Hospitals, care is aimed not only at controlling pain and inflammation but also at preventing joint damage, preserving mobility, and maintaining quality of life.</p><p>Care is delivered through a patient-centred, multidisciplinary approach combining clinical evaluation, laboratory testing, imaging, immunological assessment, medication therapy, and rehabilitation support. Each treatment plan is personalised based on disease type, severity, age, lifestyle, and overall health.</p>','<p>Rheumatology deals with autoimmune, inflammatory, and degenerative conditions of the musculoskeletal system and connective tissues. Early signs such as persistent joint stiffness (especially in the morning), symmetrical joint pain, or unexplained fatigue should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises early diagnosis, disease-modifying treatment, and long-term monitoring to prevent irreversible joint damage and organ complications.</p>','<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Disease-modifying anti-rheumatic drugs (DMARDs)</p></li><li><p>Biologic and targeted therapies for autoimmune diseases</p></li><li><p>Anti-inflammatory and pain management medications</p></li><li><p>Physiotherapy and joint mobility exercises</p></li><li><p>Lifestyle and dietary guidance for inflammation control</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Joint aspiration (removal of excess joint fluid)</p></li><li><p>Steroid injections for inflamed joints</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound-guided joint procedures</p></li><li><p>Minor procedures for soft tissue inflammation</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive and Advanced Care</h3><ul><li><p>Management of systemic autoimmune disorders</p></li><li><p>Bone protection therapy in inflammatory arthritis</p></li><li><p>Occupational therapy for joint function support</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation programs for long-term mobility</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Advanced autoimmune and inflammatory blood testing</p></li><li><p>Musculoskeletal ultrasound</p></li><li><p>Digital X-ray, CT Scan, and MRI for joint evaluation</p></li><li><p>Bone density scan (DEXA) for osteoporosis risk</p></li><li><p>Infusion therapy units for biologic treatments</p></li><li><p>Physiotherapy and rehabilitation services</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Rheumatoid arthritis</p></li><li><p>Osteoarthritis</p></li><li><p>Ankylosing spondylitis</p></li><li><p>Psoriatic arthritis</p></li><li><p>Systemic lupus erythematosus (SLE)</p></li><li><p>Gout and crystal arthritis</p></li><li><p>Vasculitis</p></li><li><p>Fibromyalgia</p></li><li><p>Connective tissue diseases</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Progressive joint damage without early treatment</p></li><li><p>Disability due to chronic pain and stiffness</p></li><li><p>Organ involvement in systemic autoimmune diseases</p></li><li><p>Need for lifelong monitoring and medication adjustment</p></li><li><p>Risk of osteoporosis in chronic inflammatory conditions</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Inflammatory Arthritis Management</p></li><li><p>Autoimmune Connective Tissue Disorders</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Rheumatology</p></li><li><p>Osteoporosis and Bone Health</p></li><li><p>Vasculitis and Systemic Disorders</p></li></ul>','Best Rheumatology Hospital in Bangalore | Joint & Autoimmune Care','Get specialized rheumatology treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Expert care for joint pain, autoimmune diseases, and chronic inflammation.','2026-02-02 12:26:48','202