res</h3><ul><li><p>Minor skin lesion and cyst removal</p></li><li><p>Scar revision procedures</p></li><li><p>Injectable treatments for facial symmetry correction</p></li><li><p>Laser therapy for scars and skin texture</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Trauma reconstruction (face, limbs, soft tissue)</p></li><li><p>Burn reconstruction and contracture release</p></li><li><p>Cleft lip and palate repair</p></li><li><p>Breast reconstruction after mastectomy</p></li><li><p>Hand and nerve reconstruction</p></li><li><p>Skin grafting and flap surgeries</p></li><li><p>Reconstructive surgery after tumor removal</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Advanced operation theatres with microsurgical equipment</p></li><li><p>Surgical loupes and operating microscopes</p></li><li><p>Laser systems for scar and skin treatment</p></li><li><p>Burn care and wound management units</p></li><li><p>Post-operative recovery and rehabilitation support</p></li><li><p>Physiotherapy and functional restoration services</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Facial injuries and deformities</p></li><li><p>Burn injuries and post-burn deformities</p></li><li><p>Congenital anomalies (cleft lip, cleft palate)</p></li><li><p>Hand injuries and nerve damage</p></li><li><p>Post-cancer reconstructive needs</p></li><li><p>Non-healing wounds and tissue loss</p></li><li><p>Severe scars and contractures</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Complex healing in large tissue injuries</p></li><li><p>Risk of infection in major reconstructive surgeries</p></li><li><p>Need for staged procedures in severe cases</p></li><li><p>Functional limitations if untreated</p></li><li><p>Emotional and psychological impact of visible deformities</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Trauma Reconstruction</p></li><li><p>Burn and Scar Reconstruction</p></li><li><p>Hand and Microsurgery</p></li><li><p>Craniofacial Surgery</p></li><li><p>Post-Oncologic Reconstruction</p></li></ul>','Advanced Plastic & Reconstructive Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Comprehensive plastic surgery services at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore. Specialized care for reconstruction, burns, trauma, and aesthetic procedures.','2026-02-02 12:29:10','2026-04-21 07:49:50','specialities/banners/relatedimages/e84a7b64-9e20-43cf-9f88-fa18dac89b36.webp'),(19,'Oral & Maxillofacial Surgery','oral-maxillofacial-surgery','specialities/banners/49b90c54-c090-415e-bb13-06c08c3a0ee1.webp','specialities/icons/fbf54498-b928-4237-a324-9ec4026df63a.webp',1,'<p>Oral &amp; Maxillofacial Surgery at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the diagnosis and surgical treatment of conditions affecting the mouth, jaws, face, and related structures. This specialty bridges dentistry and medical surgery, managing both functional and facial concerns.</p>','<p>Problems in this area may arise from impacted teeth, facial injuries, jaw misalignment, infections, tumors, or congenital deformities. These conditions can affect chewing, speaking, breathing, and facial appearance. At Nano Hospitals, care is directed toward restoring oral function, relieving pain, correcting structural problems, and improving facial balance.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach using detailed imaging, surgical planning, anesthesia expertise, and post-operative rehabilitation. Care plans are individualised based on age, severity, and functional needs.</p>','<p>This specialty deals with surgical conditions of the teeth, jaws, facial bones, and oral tissues. Early signs such as persistent jaw pain, difficulty opening the mouth, facial swelling, or impacted teeth should be evaluated promptly.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises accurate imaging, minimally invasive techniques where possible, and coordinated care with dental, ENT, and oncology teams when required.</p>','<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Infection management of oral and facial tissues</p></li><li><p>TMJ (jaw joint) pain management</p></li><li><p>Bite correction planning with orthodontic coordination</p></li><li><p>Pre-surgical evaluation and imaging</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Surgical removal of impacted teeth (including wisdom teeth)</p></li><li><p>Biopsy of oral lesions</p></li><li><p>Minor cyst and soft tissue removal</p></li><li><p>Temporomandibular joint injections</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Jaw fracture repair and facial trauma surgery</p></li><li><p>Corrective jaw surgery (orthognathic surgery)</p></li><li><p>Dental implant surgery</p></li><li><p>Removal of tumors and cysts in the jaw</p></li><li><p>Treatment of congenital facial deformities</p></li><li><p>Reconstruction after oral cancer surgery</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Digital dental X-rays and panoramic imaging</p></li><li><p>3D CT Scan for jaw and facial bone assessment</p></li><li><p>Surgical planning software for jaw correction</p></li><li><p>Advanced operation theatres with maxillofacial instruments</p></li><li><p>Dental implant systems</p></li><li><p>Post-operative recovery and pain management units</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Impacted wisdom teeth</p></li><li><p>Jaw fractures and facial injuries</p></li><li><p>Temporomandibular Joint (TMJ) disorders</p></li><li><p>Oral cysts and tumors</p></li><li><p>Misaligned jaws affecting bite and speech</p></li><li><p>Congenital deformities (cleft-related jaw issues)</p></li><li><p>Oral infections and abscesses</p></li><li><p>Bone loss requiring dental implants</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Pain and swelling affecting eating and speech</p></li><li><p>Risk of infection in untreated oral conditions</p></li><li><p>Facial asymmetry from trauma or deformity</p></li><li><p>Difficulty chewing due to jaw misalignment</p></li><li><p>Need for staged reconstruction in complex cases</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Facial Trauma Surgery</p></li><li><p>Orthognathic (Jaw Correction) Surgery</p></li><li><p>Oral Tumor and Cyst Surgery</p></li><li><p>Dental Implantology</p></li><li><p>TMJ Disorder Management</p></li></ul>','Best Oral & Maxillofacial Surgeons in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Get specialized maxillofacial treatment in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Expert care for facial trauma, jaw disorders, and oral surgery.','2026-02-02 12:31:44','2026-04-20 12:52:37','specialities/banners/relatedimages/eae281cc-d631-4030-8448-5c6c6cd9a2b4.webp'),(20,'General Surgery','general-surgery','specialities/banners/b2ff2995-3f03-4edb-b01d-745873f23215.webp','specialities/icons/743532e5-1351-4c45-b9b9-0d681d1876c8.webp',1,'<p>General Surgery at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the surgical management of a wide range of conditions affecting the abdomen, digestive tract, soft tissues, skin, and certain endocrine organs. It is one of the core surgical specialties, addressing both emergency and planned procedures.</p>','<p>Surgical conditions may present with symptoms such as persistent abdominal pain, swelling, lumps, hernias, infections, or digestive complications. Some conditions require urgent intervention, while others can be treated electively using minimally invasive techniques. At Nano Hospitals, care aims to provide safe surgery, faster recovery, minimal scarring, and reduced hospital stay whenever possible.</p><p>Treatment follows a patient-centred approach combining clinical evaluation, imaging, laboratory tests, anesthesia support, advanced laparoscopic techniques, and structured post-operative care. Each surgical plan is personalised based on the patient’s condition, age, overall health, and risk factors.</p>','<p>General Surgery deals with diseases that often require operative treatment, particularly those involving the abdomen and soft tissues. Early symptoms like severe abdominal pain, vomiting, swelling in the groin, or unexplained lumps should be medically evaluated without delay.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises timely diagnosis, minimally invasive approaches, infection control, and enhanced recovery protocols for improved patient outcomes.</p>','<h3>Non-Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Initial management of infections and abscesses</p></li><li><p>Medical management of early-stage surgical conditions</p></li><li><p>Wound care and dressing</p></li><li><p>Pre-surgical evaluation and stabilization</p></li></ul><h3>Minimally Invasive Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Laparoscopic appendectomy</p></li><li><p>Laparoscopic gallbladder removal</p></li><li><p>Laparoscopic hernia repair</p></li><li><p>Diagnostic laparoscopy</p></li><li><p>Minimally invasive abscess drainage</p></li></ul><h3>Surgical Treatments</h3><ul><li><p>Appendectomy for appendicitis</p></li><li><p>Hernia repair surgery</p></li><li><p>Gallbladder removal for gallstones</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction surgery</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and breast lump surgeries</p></li><li><p>Emergency abdominal surgeries</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Advanced laparoscopic surgery systems</p></li><li><p>High-definition imaging equipment</p></li><li><p>Modular operation theatres</p></li><li><p>Intensive Care Unit (ICU) support</p></li><li><p>Post-operative monitoring units</p></li><li><p>Sterile surgical environments with infection control</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Appendicitis</p></li><li><p>Hernias (inguinal, umbilical, incisional)</p></li><li><p>Gallstones and gallbladder disease</p></li><li><p>Piles (hemorrhoids) and anal fissures</p></li><li><p>Breast lumps and infections</p></li><li><p>Thyroid nodules and goiter</p></li><li><p>Abdominal infections and abscesses</p></li><li><p>Intestinal obstruction</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Risk of complications in emergency surgeries</p></li><li><p>Infection risk if wounds are not properly managed</p></li><li><p>Delayed treatment leading to severe complications</p></li><li><p>Need for post-operative lifestyle adjustments</p></li><li><p>Possibility of recurrence in certain conditions like hernias</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Laparoscopic (Minimally Invasive) Surgery</p></li><li><p>Gastrointestinal Surgery</p></li><li><p>Breast Surgery</p></li><li><p>Thyroid and Endocrine Surgery</p></li><li><p>Colorectal Surgery</p></li></ul>','Comprehensive General Surgery in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Trusted general surgery services at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore. Expert surgeons for a wide range of conditions and surgical treatments.','2026-02-02 12:34:07','2026-04-07 08:35:37','specialities/banners/relatedimages/38da333d-f9cb-4879-af67-1e028b207439.webp'),(21,'Emergency & Critical Care','emergency-critical-care','specialities/banners/24638eed-2bd6-4892-b285-7a8481dd71cb.webp','specialities/icons/988881f7-dded-4dac-b6b4-2149ec631368.webp',1,'<p>Emergency &amp; Critical Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> provides immediate, life-saving medical attention for patients with severe illness, injury, or life-threatening conditions. This department operates круглthe clock, ensuring rapid assessment, stabilization, and advanced medical support when every second matters.</p>','<p>Emergencies may include chest pain, breathing difficulty, severe trauma, stroke symptoms, seizures, poisoning, or sudden loss of consciousness. Critical care services support patients whose vital organs require continuous monitoring and advanced life support. At Nano Hospitals, care is focused on rapid response, precise diagnosis, and intensive monitoring to stabilise patients and prevent complications.</p><p>Treatment is delivered by a multidisciplinary team of emergency physicians, critical care specialists, nurses, and paramedical staff trained in advanced life support. Care plans are tailored in real time according to the patient’s evolving condition.</p>','<p>Emergency medicine deals with urgent medical and surgical conditions requiring immediate evaluation. Critical care focuses on patients with organ failure or unstable vital signs who need continuous monitoring and advanced interventions.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises rapid triage systems, evidence-based emergency protocols, and seamless transition from emergency care to intensive care or specialty departments.</p>','<h3>Emergency Medical Care</h3><ul><li><p>Cardiac emergency management (heart attack, arrhythmias)</p></li><li><p>Stroke stabilization and rapid response</p></li><li><p>Trauma and accident care</p></li><li><p>Poisoning and overdose treatment</p></li><li><p>Acute respiratory distress management</p></li></ul><h3>Critical Care Interventions</h3><ul><li><p>Mechanical ventilation for breathing support</p></li><li><p>Advanced cardiac life support (ACLS)</p></li><li><p>Invasive and non-invasive monitoring</p></li><li><p>Sepsis and multi-organ failure management</p></li><li><p>Dialysis support in critical kidney failure</p></li></ul><h3>Life-Saving Procedures</h3><ul><li><p>Intubation and airway management</p></li><li><p>Central line and arterial line placement</p></li><li><p>Emergency surgeries in coordination with surgical teams</p></li><li><p>Defibrillation and resuscitation</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>24/7 fully equipped Emergency Department</p></li><li><p>Advanced cardiac monitors and ventilators</p></li><li><p>Point-of-care laboratory testing</p></li><li><p>Portable ultrasound and bedside imaging</p></li><li><p>Dedicated Intensive Care Units (ICUs)</p></li><li><p>High-dependency units (HDU) for step-down care</p></li><li><p>Infection-controlled critical care environments</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Heart attacks and cardiac arrest</p></li><li><p>Stroke and sudden neurological emergencies</p></li><li><p>Severe infections and sepsis</p></li><li><p>Major trauma and road traffic injuries</p></li><li><p>Acute respiratory failure</p></li><li><p>Poisoning and drug overdose</p></li><li><p>Severe allergic reactions (anaphylaxis)</p></li><li><p>Uncontrolled bleeding</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Rapid deterioration without immediate treatment</p></li><li><p>Multi-organ failure in severe illness</p></li><li><p>Need for prolonged intensive monitoring</p></li><li><p>High emotional stress for patients and families</p></li><li><p>Risk of complications in critically ill patients</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Trauma and Emergency Surgery Support</p></li><li><p>Cardiac Critical Care</p></li><li><p>Neurocritical Care</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Critical Care</p></li><li><p>Respiratory and Pulmonary Critical Care</p></li></ul>','24/7 Emergency Hospital in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Nano Hospitals provides 24-hour emergency care in Bangalore with ICU support, trauma care, and quick response for critical conditions.','2026-02-02 12:37:30','2026-04-07 09:22:41','specialities/banners/relatedimages/52f60a9f-1d7e-4ca2-b1ca-982d89d2fdad.webp'),(22,'Physiotherapy & Rehabilitation','physiotherapy-rehabilitation','specialities/banners/43756dac-13b5-424c-8ce1-b001fd1d95e9.webp','specialities/icons/01KGJ8QX4QDCRW1FTYQ6JMG75F.webp',1,'<p>Physiotherapy &amp; Rehabilitation at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on restoring movement, strength, function, and independence after injury, surgery, illness, or long-term medical conditions. The department supports recovery for patients of all ages experiencing physical limitations, pain, or mobility challenges.</p>','<p>Physical problems may arise from fractures, joint surgeries, stroke, nerve injuries, chronic back pain, sports injuries, or prolonged bed rest. Without structured rehabilitation, stiffness, muscle weakness, and loss of function can persist. At Nano Hospitals, care is aimed not only at pain relief but also at rebuilding physical ability, improving balance, and enabling patients to return to daily activities safely.</p><p>Care is delivered through a patient-centred approach combining physiotherapy, exercise therapy, electrotherapy, occupational rehabilitation, and long-term recovery planning. Each program is personalised based on diagnosis, physical capacity, lifestyle, and recovery goals.</p>','<p>Rehabilitation medicine focuses on improving physical function and quality of life after injury or illness. Early physiotherapy intervention often shortens recovery time and prevents long-term disability.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises structured rehabilitation programs, functional training, and continuous progress monitoring to help patients regain independence and confidence.</p>','<h3>Non-Invasive Therapies</h3><ul><li><p>Therapeutic exercise programs</p></li><li><p>Manual therapy and joint mobilisation</p></li><li><p>Pain relief through electrotherapy modalities</p></li><li><p>Heat and cold therapy</p></li><li><p>Posture correction and ergonomic training</p></li></ul><h3>Specialized Rehabilitation Programs</h3><ul><li><p>Post-surgical rehabilitation (joint replacement, spine surgery)</p></li><li><p>Stroke and neurological rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Sports injury rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Pediatric physiotherapy</p></li><li><p>Geriatric mobility and balance training</p></li></ul><h3>Advanced Supportive Care</h3><ul><li><p>Gait training and mobility aid support</p></li><li><p>Occupational therapy for daily living skills</p></li><li><p>Respiratory physiotherapy for lung conditions</p></li><li><p>Chronic pain rehabilitation programs</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Exercise therapy and strength training equipment</p></li><li><p>Electrotherapy units (TENS, ultrasound therapy)</p></li><li><p>Balance and gait training systems</p></li><li><p>Parallel bars and mobility training aids</p></li><li><p>Neurological rehabilitation equipment</p></li><li><p>Dedicated physiotherapy and rehabilitation gym</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Post-fracture stiffness and weakness</p></li><li><p>Post-surgical recovery</p></li><li><p>Chronic back and neck pain</p></li><li><p>Stroke-related weakness and paralysis</p></li><li><p>Sports injuries</p></li><li><p>Arthritis-related mobility problems</p></li><li><p>Neurological disorders affecting movement</p></li><li><p>Balance disorders and fall risk in elderly</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Delayed recovery without guided rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Muscle wasting due to inactivity</p></li><li><p>Persistent pain limiting movement</p></li><li><p>Risk of falls in elderly without balance training</p></li><li><p>Reduced independence in daily life</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Orthopaedic Rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Neurological Rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Sports Physiotherapy</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Physiotherapy</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Cardio-pulmonary Rehabilitation</p></li></ul>',NULL,NULL,'2026-02-02 12:40:05','2026-04-21 07:56:15','specialities/banners/relatedimages/6dea5a6a-a6a0-4248-a12f-663e20bd865f.webp'),(23,'Geriatrics (Elder Care)','geriatrics','specialities/banners/0d72e63e-fd1d-427c-a360-747430272bc4.webp','specialities/icons/01KGJ8RK6FVB8NJHQ6KGJH998F.webp',1,'<p>Elder Care at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> focuses on the comprehensive healthcare needs of older adults. This specialty addresses age-related medical conditions, mobility challenges, memory concerns, and overall well-being to help seniors maintain independence and quality of life.</p>','<p>As people age, they may experience multiple health issues such as joint pain, balance problems, memory decline, vision or hearing loss, and chronic illnesses like diabetes or heart disease. These conditions often require coordinated care rather than treatment of a single problem. At Nano Hospitals, elder care is designed to provide holistic, respectful, and continuous support tailored to the unique needs of senior patients.</p><p>Care follows a patient-centred and family-inclusive approach, combining medical management, rehabilitation, nutritional guidance, mental health support, and preventive care. Treatment plans are personalised according to functional ability, lifestyle, and long-term health goals.</p>','<p>Geriatric care focuses on preventing, diagnosing, and managing health conditions common in older adults. Early recognition of mobility decline, memory changes, or increased fall risk can significantly improve long-term outcomes.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises preventive screenings, chronic disease management, fall prevention, and rehabilitation to support safe and active ageing.</p>','<h3>Medical Care</h3><ul><li><p>Management of chronic diseases (diabetes, hypertension, arthritis)</p></li><li><p>Medication review to prevent side effects and interactions</p></li><li><p>Memory and cognitive health evaluation</p></li><li><p>Vaccination and preventive health screening</p></li></ul><h3>Supportive Therapies</h3><ul><li><p>Physiotherapy for mobility and balance</p></li><li><p>Nutritional counselling for age-related needs</p></li><li><p>Pain management programs</p></li><li><p>Mental health support for depression, anxiety, and loneliness</p></li></ul><h3>Functional and Home Support</h3><ul><li><p>Fall risk assessment and prevention strategies</p></li><li><p>Home care guidance and caregiver education</p></li><li><p>Post-hospitalisation recovery programs</p></li><li><p>Palliative and comfort care when needed</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Senior-friendly consultation areas</p></li><li><p>Multidisciplinary geriatric assessment services</p></li><li><p>Rehabilitation and physiotherapy units</p></li><li><p>Cognitive screening and mental health support</p></li><li><p>Nutrition and lifestyle counselling services</p></li><li><p>Coordination with home healthcare services</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Arthritis and joint degeneration</p></li><li><p>Osteoporosis and fracture risk</p></li><li><p>Memory disorders and dementia</p></li><li><p>Balance disorders and frequent falls</p></li><li><p>Hearing and vision-related difficulties</p></li><li><p>Chronic heart, lung, and metabolic diseases</p></li><li><p>Urinary incontinence</p></li><li><p>Sleep disorders</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Increased risk of falls and fractures</p></li><li><p>Multiple medications causing side effects</p></li><li><p>Memory decline affecting daily independence</p></li><li><p>Social isolation impacting mental health</p></li><li><p>Slow recovery after illness or surgery</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Geriatric Medicine</p></li><li><p>Memory and Cognitive Health Care</p></li><li><p>Geriatric Rehabilitation</p></li><li><p>Palliative and Supportive Care</p></li><li><p>Preventive Geriatric Health</p></li></ul>','Comprehensive Elder & Senior Care in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Get specialized geriatric care in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Support for senior health, memory concerns, and independent living.','2026-02-02 12:43:23','2026-04-21 07:41:14','specialities/banners/relatedimages/fe45f2bc-389d-4ec0-afce-faac4e823222.webp'),(24,'Radiology & Imaging','radiology-imaging','specialities/banners/3a8a2a3b-3aba-40bd-863e-2ba1d54e4d07.webp','specialities/icons/01KGJ8TZX2TB0DJZCJR59HVY23.webp',1,'<p>Radiology &amp; Imaging at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> provides advanced diagnostic and interventional imaging services that help detect, monitor, and guide treatment for a wide range of medical conditions. Imaging plays a critical role in early diagnosis, treatment planning, and follow-up care across nearly all medical specialties.</p>','<p>Many diseases may not show clear external symptoms in early stages. Imaging tests allow doctors to see inside the body safely and accurately, helping identify infections, fractures, tumors, organ disorders, and vascular conditions. At Nano Hospitals, radiology services focus on delivering precise imaging with minimal discomfort and radiation exposure.</p><p>Care is delivered by experienced radiologists and technologists using modern imaging technology and evidence-based protocols. Each imaging study is tailored to the patient’s symptoms, age, and medical history.</p>','<p>Radiology uses medical imaging techniques to diagnose and sometimes treat diseases. Imaging can detect problems early, often before symptoms become severe, allowing timely medical intervention.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises accurate image interpretation, fast reporting, and integration with clinical teams for effective patient management.</p>','<h3>Basic Imaging</h3><ul><li><p>Digital X-rays for bones, chest, and joints</p></li><li><p>Ultrasound for abdomen, pelvis, thyroid, and pregnancy scans</p></li><li><p>Doppler studies for blood flow evaluation</p></li></ul><h3>Advanced Imaging</h3><ul><li><p>CT Scan for detailed cross-sectional images of organs and bones</p></li><li><p>MRI for brain, spine, joints, and soft tissue evaluation</p></li><li><p>Mammography for breast screening</p></li><li><p>Bone density scan (DEXA) for osteoporosis assessment</p></li></ul><h3>Interventional Radiology</h3><ul><li><p>Image-guided biopsies</p></li><li><p>Drainage of fluid collections or abscesses</p></li><li><p>Vascular procedures such as angiography</p></li><li><p>Catheter-based minimally invasive treatment</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>High-resolution Digital X-ray systems</p></li><li><p>Multi-slice CT scanner</p></li><li><p>Advanced MRI scanner</p></li><li><p>3D/4D Ultrasound machines</p></li><li><p>Mammography units with low radiation dose</p></li><li><p>Picture Archiving and Communication System (PACS) for digital reporting</p></li><li><p>Dedicated interventional radiology suite</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Bone fractures and joint disorders</p></li><li><p>Brain and spine conditions</p></li><li><p>Lung infections and chest diseases</p></li><li><p>Abdominal organ disorders</p></li><li><p>Tumors and abnormal growths</p></li><li><p>Kidney stones and urinary tract issues</p></li><li><p>Vascular blockages and clots</p></li><li><p>Pregnancy and fetal development monitoring</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Minimising radiation exposure through safety protocols</p></li><li><p>Ensuring patient comfort during longer scans (e.g., MRI)</p></li><li><p>Need for contrast agents in some imaging studies</p></li><li><p>Claustrophobia concerns during MRI scans</p></li><li><p>Special precautions for pregnant patients</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Diagnostic Radiology</p></li><li><p>Interventional Radiology</p></li><li><p>Neuroradiology</p></li><li><p>Musculoskeletal Imaging</p></li><li><p>Women’s Imaging</p></li><li><p>Pediatric Radiology</p></li></ul>','Advanced Radiology & Imaging Care in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Expert radiology services at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore. Advanced imaging for diagnosis, monitoring, and guided treatment across specialties.','2026-02-02 12:45:59','2026-04-21 07:50:40','specialities/banners/relatedimages/c123a29f-f3b2-48d3-a6b6-65ae974e4725.webp'),(25,'Diagnostics & Laboratory Medicine','diagnostics-laboratory-medicine','specialities/banners/d383c009-5e44-4dc8-b4ff-06e4c1410d62.webp','specialities/icons/01KGJ8VQJ2WPB7YF4X2BVPE170.webp',1,'<p>Diagnostics &amp; Laboratory Medicine at <strong>Nano Hospitals</strong> provide accurate and timely testing that supports disease detection, treatment planning, and health monitoring. These services form the foundation of modern medical care, helping clinicians make evidence-based decisions.</p>','<p>Many illnesses show internal changes before symptoms become obvious. Laboratory testing helps detect infections, metabolic disorders, organ dysfunction, nutritional deficiencies, and chronic diseases at early stages. At Nano Hospitals, diagnostic services focus on precision, reliability, and quick turnaround times.</p><p>All tests are conducted using standardised protocols, automated analyzers, and strict quality control measures. Reports are interpreted by qualified pathologists and shared securely with treating physicians for integrated care</p>','<p>Diagnostic laboratories analyze blood, urine, tissue, and other body samples to assess overall health and identify disease. Regular testing is essential for preventive care, chronic disease monitoring, and emergency evaluation.</p><p>Nano Hospitals emphasises accuracy, hygiene, and fast reporting to support prompt medical decisions.</p>','<h3>Routine Laboratory Tests</h3><ul><li><p>Complete Blood Count (CBC)</p></li><li><p>Blood sugar and diabetes testing</p></li><li><p>Liver and kidney function tests</p></li><li><p>Lipid profile for cholesterol levels</p></li><li><p>Urine analysis</p></li></ul><h3>Specialized Diagnostic Tests</h3><ul><li><p>Thyroid and hormone testing</p></li><li><p>Vitamin and nutritional deficiency tests</p></li><li><p>Infection screening (viral, bacterial, parasitic)</p></li><li><p>Allergy testing</p></li><li><p>Autoimmune disorder panels</p></li></ul><h3>Advanced Diagnostic Services</h3><ul><li><p>Histopathology and biopsy analysis</p></li><li><p>Cytology testing (Pap smear, fluid analysis)</p></li><li><p>Microbiology cultures and sensitivity testing</p></li><li><p>Molecular diagnostics and PCR testing</p></li><li><p>Tumor marker testing</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Fully automated biochemistry and hematology analyzers</p></li><li><p>Microbiology and pathology laboratories</p></li><li><p>Molecular diagnostic testing equipment</p></li><li><p>Sample collection and processing units</p></li><li><p>Barcode-based sample tracking systems</p></li><li><p>Digital reporting and record management</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Infections and inflammatory diseases</p></li><li><p>Diabetes and metabolic disorders</p></li><li><p>Liver and kidney diseases</p></li><li><p>Hormonal imbalances</p></li><li><p>Nutritional deficiencies</p></li><li><p>Blood disorders such as anemia</p></li><li><p>Cancer indicators through tumor markers</p></li><li><p>Autoimmune diseases</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Strict sterilisation and infection control</p></li><li><p>Regular calibration of laboratory equipment</p></li><li><p>Internal and external quality assurance programs</p></li><li><p>Accurate sample identification and tracking</p></li><li><p>Confidential handling of patient reports</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Clinical Biochemistry</p></li><li><p>Hematology</p></li><li><p>Microbiology</p></li><li><p>Histopathology</p></li><li><p>Cytology</p></li><li><p>Molecular Diagnostics</p></li></ul>','Advanced Diagnostics & Laboratory Medicine in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Get comprehensive diagnostic lab services in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Timely and precise testing for better treatment planning.','2026-02-02 12:48:41','2026-04-21 07:48:15','specialities/banners/relatedimages/c7c14599-24ae-4195-a683-a5a2b466188b.webp'),(26,'Nephrology','nephrology','specialities/banners/cd0a2c5c-a79e-46c0-ab61-25e5a0d70c53.webp','specialities/icons/01KGJ8T36Z71JBCBNPE3K6Z631.webp',1,'<p>Kidneys are vital organs that filter waste, balance fluids, regulate blood pressure, and maintain overall metabolic stability. At Nano Hospitals, our <strong>Kidney Care specialty</strong> is dedicated to preventing, diagnosing, and treating kidney-related diseases with precision and compassion</p>','<p>We combine advanced nephrology expertise, dialysis facilities, and transplant support to ensure patients receive holistic care.</p>','<p>Kidneys are vital organs that filter waste, balance fluids, regulate blood pressure, and maintain overall metabolic stability. At Nano Hospitals, our <strong>Kidney Care specialty</strong> is dedicated to preventing, diagnosing, and treating kidney-related diseases with precision and compassion</p>','<ul><li><p><strong>Medications</strong>: blood pressure control, infection management, immunosuppressants</p></li><li><p><strong>Dialysis</strong>: hemodialysis and peritoneal dialysis</p></li><li><p><strong>Kidney Transplant</strong>: surgical replacement with donor kidney</p></li><li><p><strong>Lifestyle modification</strong>: diet, exercise, stress management</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Experienced nephrologists and transplant surgeons</p></li><li><p>Advanced dialysis units with infection control</p></li><li><p>Multidisciplinary team (dietitians, counselors, physiotherapists)</p></li><li><p>Patient education and support programs</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD)</p></li><li><p>Acute Kidney Injury (AKI)</p></li><li><p>Kidney stones</p></li><li><p>Glomerulonephritis</p></li><li><p>Polycystic Kidney Disease</p></li><li><p>Hypertension-related kidney damage</p></li><li><p>Diabetic nephropathy</p></li></ul>','<ul><li><p>Swelling in legs, ankles, and face</p></li><li><p>Fatigue and weakness</p></li><li><p>Reduced urine output or foamy urine</p></li><li><p>Blood in urine</p></li><li><p>Persistent high blood pressure</p></li><li><p>Untreated → kidney failure, dialysis dependence, cardiovascular complications</p></li></ul>','<h3>1. Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) Management</h3><p>Comprehensive care for patients with long-term kidney damage, focusing on slowing disease progression, managing complications, and improving quality of life.</p><h3>2. Dialysis Care (Hemodialysis &amp; Peritoneal Dialysis)</h3><p>Specialised management of patients requiring dialysis, including treatment planning, monitoring, and complication prevention.</p><h3>3. Kidney Transplant Care</h3><p>Pre-transplant evaluation, donor matching coordination, and post-transplant follow-up care to ensure successful outcomes and long-term graft survival.</p>','Advanced Kidney & Renal Care in Bangalore | Nano Hospitals','Get comprehensive kidney care in Bangalore at Nano Hospitals. Specialized treatment for kidney disorders, dialysis, and long-term management.','2026-02-02 14:10:18','2026-04-21 07:46:25','specialities/banners/relatedimages/73602b0f-1cfb-4a0e-8853-d62c1e3eb548.webp'),(28,'internal medicine','internal-medicine','specialities/banners/3178782b-2568-4df7-8f29-face3ef28605.webp','specialities/icons/b6450a79-47c6-4143-9dec-d19bd4ae07f7.webp',1,'<p></p>','<p></p>','<p></p>','<p></p>','<p></p>','<p></p>','<p></p>','<p></p>',NULL,NULL,'2026-04-10 11:11:58','2026-04-20 13:14:43','specialities/banners/relatedimages/e523ded1-843e-4f42-9547-982c203fc33a.webp');
