INSERT INTO `speciality_faqs` VALUES (1,2,'Which is a good child care and paediatrics hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted paediatric hospital in Bangalore with experienced paediatricians providing comprehensive care for newborns, infants, children, and adolescents — including vaccinations, treatment for childhood illnesses, neonatal care, and paediatric emergency services at BG Road and Uttarahalli.',0,'2026-01-26 07:00:01','2026-06-12 08:03:25'),(2,2,'At what age should a child first see a paediatrician?','A child should see a paediatrician from birth — ideally within the first few days after delivery. Regular well-baby check-ups are recommended at 1 month, 2 months, 4 months, 6 months, 9 months, and 12 months, and annually thereafter. Early and regular paediatric check-ups in Bangalore ensure timely detection of growth problems, developmental delays, and health concerns.',0,'2026-01-26 07:00:01','2026-06-12 08:03:36'),(3,1,'Which is a good hospital for orthopedic treatment in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a reliable option for orthopedic treatment in Bangalore, offering care for knee pain, joint replacement, fractures, sports injuries, and spine conditions. The hospital has experienced orthopedic surgeons, modern diagnostic facilities, and a structured rehabilitation program to support full recovery.',0,'2026-01-28 12:50:55','2026-06-11 13:46:15'),(4,1,'When should I see an orthopedic doctor?','You should consult an orthopedic specialist if you experience persistent joint pain, swelling, stiffness, limited movement, or if you have had a fracture or sports injury. Early consultation helps prevent conditions from worsening and improves treatment outcomes.',0,'2026-01-28 12:50:55','2026-06-11 13:46:33'),(5,1,'Is surgery always required for bone and joint problems?','No. Many orthopedic conditions including mild to moderate knee pain, arthritis, and back pain can be effectively managed without surgery through medications, physiotherapy, and lifestyle changes. Surgery is recommended only when non-surgical treatments do not provide adequate relief or when the condition is structurally severe.',0,'2026-01-28 12:50:55','2026-06-11 13:46:45'),(6,1,'What is knee replacement surgery and who needs it?','Knee replacement is a surgical procedure in which the damaged surfaces of the knee joint are replaced with an artificial implant. It is typically recommended for patients with severe osteoarthritis, advanced joint degeneration, or significant knee damage that causes persistent pain and limits daily movement despite other treatments.',0,'2026-01-28 12:50:55','2026-06-11 13:48:04'),(7,2,'What vaccinations does my child need and when?','Children require a series of vaccinations starting from birth as per the national immunisation schedule — covering diseases like polio, tuberculosis, hepatitis B, diphtheria, measles, and more. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, the paediatric team provides a complete childhood vaccination program with reminders and guidance for parents at every stage.',0,'2026-02-02 11:29:01','2026-06-12 08:03:51'),(8,2,'What are the signs that my child needs urgent medical attention?','Seek immediate paediatric care if your child has high or persistent fever, difficulty breathing, persistent vomiting or diarrhoea, seizures, extreme lethargy or unresponsiveness, skin rash with fever, or any injury. Nano Hospitals provides 24x7 paediatric emergency care in Bangalore to handle all urgent child health situations.',0,'2026-02-02 11:29:01','2026-06-12 08:07:04'),(15,11,'Is cancer always life-threatening?','Not always. Many cancers are treatable, especially when detected early.',0,'2026-02-02 12:10:57','2026-02-02 12:10:57'),(16,11,'Do all cancer patients need chemotherapy?','No. Treatment depends on the cancer type and stage.',0,'2026-02-02 12:11:08','2026-02-02 12:11:08'),(17,11,'Is radiation therapy painful?','No. Radiation treatment itself is painless, though some side effects may occur later.',0,'2026-02-02 12:11:29','2026-02-02 12:11:29'),(18,11,'Is follow-up important after cancer treatment?','Yes. Regular follow-ups help detect recurrence early and manage long-term health.',0,'2026-02-02 12:11:39','2026-02-02 12:11:39'),(19,12,'Which is a good vascular surgery hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted vascular surgery hospital in Bangalore with experienced vascular surgeons and advanced endovascular facilities for treatment of varicose veins, blocked arteries, diabetic foot, DVT, peripheral artery disease, and non-healing ulcers.',0,'2026-02-02 12:13:56','2026-06-12 07:48:58'),(20,12,'What are the warning signs of vascular disease?','Warning signs include leg pain or cramps while walking, persistent swelling in the legs or feet, visible bulging or twisted veins, skin discolouration, cold or numb limbs, and wounds or ulcers on the feet or legs that are not healing. These symptoms need prompt evaluation at a vascular surgery hospital in Bangalore.',0,'2026-02-02 12:14:07','2026-06-12 07:49:12'),(21,12,' Are all vascular conditions treated with surgery?','No. Many vascular conditions including mild varicose veins, early peripheral artery disease, and DVT can be managed without surgery using medications, compression therapy, and lifestyle changes. Minimally invasive procedures like angioplasty, stenting, and laser varicose vein treatment are preferred over open surgery whenever possible at Nano Hospitals Bangalore.',0,'2026-02-02 12:14:13','2026-06-12 08:00:18'),(22,12,'Is varicose vein treatment painful?','Modern varicose vein treatment using Endovenous Laser Treatment (EVLT) is minimally invasive, involves no large cuts, and is performed under local anaesthesia. Most patients experience minimal discomfort and can resume daily activities within a day or two. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers laser varicose vein treatment with quick recovery and excellent results.',0,'2026-02-02 12:14:24','2026-06-12 08:00:35'),(23,13,'Which is a good dermatology hospital in Bangalore for skin treatment?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted dermatology and skin care hospital in Bangalore with experienced MD Dermatology specialists offering medical, surgical, and cosmetic skin treatments for acne, pigmentation, hair loss, eczema, psoriasis, vitiligo, skin infections, and laser skin procedures at BG Road and Uttarahalli.',0,'2026-02-02 12:16:55','2026-06-12 08:14:08'),(24,13,'When should I see a dermatologist in Bangalore?','Consult a skin specialist in Bangalore if you have persistent acne, dark patches or pigmentation, unexplained hair thinning or hair loss, chronic itching or rashes, unusual moles or skin growths, nail discolouration or infections, or any skin condition that is not responding to over-the-counter treatment. Early dermatological evaluation prevents conditions from worsening and scarring.',0,'2026-02-02 12:17:04','2026-06-12 08:14:21'),(25,13,' What is the best treatment for acne and acne scars in Bangalore?','Acne treatment in Bangalore depends on the severity — mild acne is managed with topical creams and medications, while moderate to severe acne may require oral antibiotics, hormonal therapy, or procedural treatments like chemical peels and laser therapy. Acne scars are treated at Nano Hospitals Bangalore with chemical peels, laser resurfacing, and PRP therapy for smoother, clearer skin.',0,'2026-02-02 12:17:17','2026-06-12 08:14:31'),(26,13,'Can pigmentation and melasma be treated permanently?','Pigmentation and melasma can be significantly reduced with the right combination of topical depigmenting agents, chemical peels, laser pigmentation treatment, and strict sun protection. While complete permanent cure is not always possible for conditions like melasma, consistent treatment and maintenance at Nano Hospitals Bangalore delivers significant and long-lasting improvement in skin tone and clarity.',0,'2026-02-02 12:17:23','2026-06-12 08:14:48'),(31,15,'Are frequent throat infections normal in children?','They are common, but repeated infections may require specialist evaluation.',0,'2026-02-02 12:22:13','2026-02-02 12:22:13'),(32,15,'Can sinusitis be cured without surgery?','Yes. Many cases respond to medication; surgery is needed only in chronic or severe cases.',0,'2026-02-02 12:22:22','2026-02-02 12:22:22'),(33,15,'Is hearing loss reversible?','Some types are treatable, while others may require hearing aids or surgical correction.',0,'2026-02-02 12:22:30','2026-02-02 12:22:30'),(34,15,'Is vertigo related to the ear?','Often yes. Inner ear problems are a common cause of balance disorders.',0,'2026-02-02 12:22:39','2026-02-02 12:22:39'),(35,16,'Is seeking mental health support a sign of weakness?','No. Seeking help is a positive and responsible step toward well-being.',0,'2026-02-02 12:24:38','2026-02-02 12:24:38'),(36,16,'Are mental health treatments confidential?','Yes. All consultations and treatments are handled with strict confidentiality.',0,'2026-02-02 12:24:53','2026-02-02 12:24:53'),(37,16,'Do all mental health conditions require medication?','No. Many conditions improve with therapy and lifestyle changes alone.',0,'2026-02-02 12:24:59','2026-02-02 12:24:59'),(38,16,'Can mental health conditions be completely cured?','Many conditions can be effectively managed, allowing individuals to lead healthy and productive lives.',0,'2026-02-02 12:25:07','2026-02-02 12:25:07'),(39,17,'Are rheumatic diseases curable?','Most are chronic but can be effectively controlled with modern treatments.',0,'2026-02-02 12:27:11','2026-02-02 12:27:11'),(40,17,'Do these conditions affect only joints?','No. Some autoimmune diseases can affect skin, lungs, kidneys, and other organs.',0,'2026-02-02 12:27:20','2026-02-02 12:27:20'),(41,17,'Are biologic treatments safe?','Yes, when prescribed and monitored by specialists.',0,'2026-02-02 12:27:30','2026-02-02 12:27:30'),(42,17,'Is long-term follow-up necessary?','Yes. Regular monitoring helps prevent complications and adjust treatment.',0,'2026-02-02 12:27:40','2026-02-02 12:27:40'),(43,18,'Is plastic surgery only cosmetic?','No. Reconstructive surgery focuses on restoring function and repairing damage from injury or disease.',0,'2026-02-02 12:29:35','2026-02-02 12:29:35'),(44,18,'Will scars completely disappear after surgery?','Scars improve significantly but may not disappear entirely.',0,'2026-02-02 12:29:41','2026-02-02 12:29:41'),(45,18,'Is reconstruction done in one surgery?','Some cases require staged procedures depending on the complexity.',0,'2026-02-02 12:29:55','2026-02-02 12:29:55'),(46,18,'Is rehabilitation necessary after reconstructive surgery?','Yes. Physiotherapy and follow-up care are often essential for full recovery.',0,'2026-02-02 12:30:01','2026-02-02 12:30:01'),(47,19,'Is wisdom tooth removal always surgical?','Impacted or problematic wisdom teeth often require minor surgery.',0,'2026-02-02 12:32:13','2026-02-02 12:32:13'),(48,19,'Are jaw surgeries safe?','Yes, when performed by trained maxillofacial surgeons with proper planning.',0,'2026-02-02 12:32:22','2026-02-02 12:32:22'),(49,19,'Is recovery painful after jaw surgery?','There is temporary discomfort and swelling, but pain is managed with medication.',0,'2026-02-02 12:32:32','2026-02-02 12:32:32'),(50,19,'Do I need hospital admission for these procedures?','Some minor procedures are day-care, while major surgeries may require short hospital stays.',0,'2026-02-02 12:32:42','2026-02-02 12:32:42'),(51,20,'Are all surgeries open procedures?','No. Many surgeries are performed laparoscopically with small incisions.',0,'2026-02-02 12:34:30','2026-02-02 12:34:30'),(52,20,'Is hospital stay always required?','Some procedures are day-care, while others need short admission.',0,'2026-02-02 12:34:41','2026-02-02 12:34:41'),(53,20,'How long is recovery after surgery?','Recovery time depends on the type of surgery and individual health.',0,'2026-02-02 12:34:53','2026-02-02 12:34:53'),(54,20,'Is follow-up important after surgery?','Yes. Follow-up ensures proper healing and early detection of complications.',0,'2026-02-02 12:35:03','2026-02-02 12:35:03'),(55,21,'When should I go to the emergency department?','For severe chest pain, breathing difficulty, major injuries, stroke symptoms, or sudden unconsciousness.',0,'2026-02-02 12:37:53','2026-02-02 12:37:53'),(56,21,'What is critical care?','It is specialized care for patients with life-threatening conditions requiring continuous monitoring.',0,'2026-02-02 12:38:02','2026-02-02 12:38:02'),(57,21,'Can family members visit ICU patients?','Visiting policies depend on the patient’s condition and hospital guidelines.',0,'2026-02-02 12:38:11','2026-02-02 12:38:11'),(58,21,'Is emergency care available 24/7?','Yes. Emergency services operate round the clock.',0,'2026-02-02 12:38:23','2026-02-02 12:38:23'),(59,22,'When should physiotherapy start after surgery?','Often within a few days, depending on the surgery and doctor’s advice.',0,'2026-02-02 12:40:25','2026-02-02 12:40:25'),(60,22,'Is physiotherapy painful?','Some discomfort can occur during recovery exercises, but therapy is adjusted to tolerance levels.',0,'2026-02-02 12:40:37','2026-02-02 12:40:37'),(61,22,'How long does rehabilitation take?','Duration varies based on the condition, severity, and patient participation.',0,'2026-02-02 12:40:42','2026-02-02 12:40:42'),(62,22,'Do I need a doctor’s referral?','Some programs require referral, especially post-surgery or neurological rehabilitation.',0,'2026-02-02 12:40:51','2026-02-02 12:40:51'),(63,23,'At what age should geriatric care begin?','Typically after 60 years, or earlier if multiple age-related conditions are present.',0,'2026-02-02 12:43:48','2026-02-02 12:43:48'),(64,23,'Can elderly patients improve mobility with therapy?','Yes. Physiotherapy and exercise programs can significantly improve strength and balance.',0,'2026-02-02 12:43:57','2026-02-02 12:43:57'),(65,23,'Is memory loss a normal part of ageing?','Mild forgetfulness can occur, but significant memory decline should be medically evaluated.',0,'2026-02-02 12:44:05','2026-02-02 12:44:05'),(66,23,'Does elder care involve family members?','Yes. Family involvement is important for long-term support and care planning.',0,'2026-02-02 12:44:14','2026-02-02 12:44:14'),(67,24,'Are imaging tests painful?','Most imaging tests are painless, though some may require brief discomfort from positioning or contrast injection.',0,'2026-02-02 12:46:19','2026-02-02 12:46:19'),(68,24,'Is radiation from X-rays or CT scans harmful?','Radiation doses are carefully controlled and kept as low as reasonably possible.',0,'2026-02-02 12:46:31','2026-02-02 12:46:31'),(69,24,'How long does an MRI scan take?','Typically 20–45 minutes depending on the body part being examined.',0,'2026-02-02 12:46:43','2026-02-02 12:46:43'),(70,24,'Do I need a doctor’s referral for imaging?','Most advanced imaging tests require a doctor’s prescription.',0,'2026-02-02 12:46:49','2026-02-02 12:46:49'),(71,25,'Do I need fasting before blood tests?','Some tests like blood sugar and lipid profile require fasting; instructions are provided in advance.',0,'2026-02-02 12:49:06','2026-02-02 12:49:06'),(72,25,'How long do reports take?','Routine reports are often available the same day; specialised tests may take longer.',0,'2026-02-02 12:49:19','2026-02-02 12:49:19'),(73,25,'Are home sample collections available?','In many cases, yes, depending on the test and location.',0,'2026-02-02 12:49:26','2026-02-02 12:49:26'),(74,25,'Are laboratory reports confidential?','Yes. All patient information is handled with strict confidentiality.',0,'2026-02-02 12:49:35','2026-02-02 12:49:35'),(77,5,' What are the warning signs of a heart attack?','Common symptoms include chest pain or pressure, pain spreading to the arm or jaw, shortness of breath, nausea, sweating, dizziness, and extreme fatigue',0,'2026-03-09 05:50:35','2026-03-09 05:50:35'),(78,5,'How can I reduce my risk of heart disease?','You can lower your risk by maintaining a healthy diet, exercising regularly, avoiding smoking, controlling blood pressure and cholesterol, managing stress, and getting regular health checkups',0,'2026-03-09 05:51:25','2026-03-09 05:51:25'),(79,5,'Does Nano Hospitals provide advanced heart care?','Yes, our heart care team offers comprehensive cardiac evaluation, modern diagnostic facilities, and personalized treatment plans to ensure the best care for every patient.',0,'2026-03-09 05:51:57','2026-03-09 05:51:57'),(80,28,'sd','sd',0,'2026-04-10 11:11:58','2026-04-10 11:11:58'),(81,6,'Which is a good neurology and brain care hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted neurology hospital in Bangalore with experienced neurologists providing expert diagnosis and treatment for stroke, epilepsy, migraine, neuropathy, memory disorders, and other neurological conditions — with 24x7 emergency neurological care at BG Road and Uttarahalli.',0,'2026-04-11 10:21:59','2026-06-12 08:10:40'),(82,6,'What are the warning signs of a stroke I should not ignore?','The most important warning signs of stroke are sudden weakness or numbness in the face, arm, or leg on one side of the body, sudden speech difficulty or confusion, sudden vision loss, severe headache with no known cause, and sudden loss of balance or coordination. Stroke is a medical emergency — every minute matters. Seek immediate care at a neurology emergency hospital in Bangalore without delay.',0,'2026-04-11 10:22:14','2026-06-12 08:10:47'),(83,6,'When should I see a neurologist in Bangalore?','Consult a neurologist if you experience recurring headaches or migraine, seizures or blackouts, persistent dizziness or balance problems, memory loss or cognitive decline, numbness or tingling in hands or feet, sudden weakness in limbs, or any sudden change in speech, vision, or movement. Early neurological evaluation prevents conditions from progressing to serious disability.',0,'2026-04-11 10:22:28','2026-06-12 08:10:58'),(84,6,'What is an EEG test and when is it needed?','An EEG (Electroencephalogram) is a painless test that records electrical activity in the brain. It is used to diagnose epilepsy and seizure disorders, evaluate altered consciousness, identify abnormal brain activity, and monitor brain function in ICU patients. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers EEG testing with expert neurological interpretation as part of comprehensive brain care.',0,'2026-04-11 10:22:52','2026-06-12 08:11:11'),(85,6,'Can stroke be treated and recovered from?','Yes. With rapid medical treatment — ideally within the first few hours — many stroke patients can recover significantly. Early stroke management at a neurology hospital in Bangalore like Nano Hospitals focuses on restoring blood flow, preventing further brain damage, and starting rehabilitation early to help patients regain movement, speech, and independence.',0,'2026-04-11 10:22:59','2026-06-12 08:11:25'),(86,10,'Which is a good diabetes and endocrinology hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted diabetology and endocrinology hospital in Bangalore with experienced specialists offering complete diabetes management, thyroid treatment, PCOS care, obesity management, and hormonal disorder treatment at BG Road and Uttarahalli — with advanced hormone testing and personalised treatment plans.',0,'2026-04-11 10:27:41','2026-06-13 11:26:22'),(87,10,'When should I see a diabetologist or endocrinologist in Bangalore?','Consult a diabetes or hormone specialist in Bangalore if you experience frequent thirst or urination, unexplained weight gain or loss, persistent fatigue, irregular periods, hair thinning, mood changes, difficulty conceiving, swelling in the neck, high blood sugar reports, or any abnormal thyroid or hormone test result. Early endocrinology evaluation prevents serious organ damage from undetected hormonal conditions.',0,'2026-04-11 10:27:56','2026-06-13 11:26:36'),(88,10,'Can Type 2 diabetes be reversed?','Type 2 diabetes cannot always be completely cured, but it can be significantly controlled or even put into remission in early stages through consistent lifestyle changes — including weight loss, regular physical activity, healthy diet, and structured medical management. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, the diabetology team creates personalised diabetes reversal and management plans to help patients achieve optimal blood sugar control and reduce medication dependence.',0,'2026-04-11 10:28:09','2026-06-13 11:26:49'),(89,10,'What is HbA1c and why is it important in diabetes management?','HbA1c is a blood test that reflects the average blood sugar level over the past 2 to 3 months — giving a more accurate picture of diabetes control than a single fasting blood glucose test. A target HbA1c below 7% is recommended for most diabetic patients to prevent long-term complications. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, HbA1c monitoring is a core part of structured diabetes management and follow-up care.',0,'2026-04-11 10:28:20','2026-06-13 11:27:04'),(90,10,'What are the symptoms of thyroid disorders?','Hypothyroidism (underactive thyroid) causes weight gain, fatigue, hair loss, cold intolerance, constipation, and depression. Hyperthyroidism (overactive thyroid) causes weight loss, rapid heartbeat, sweating, anxiety, and tremors. Both conditions are diagnosed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore using thyroid function tests and ultrasound, and managed with accurate medication titration and long-term monitoring.',0,'2026-04-11 10:28:31','2026-06-13 11:27:27'),(91,9,'Which is a good gastroenterology hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted gastroenterology and digestive care hospital in Bangalore with an experienced DM Gastroenterology specialist offering endoscopy, colonoscopy, ERCP, and treatment for acidity, GERD, liver disease, gallstones, IBS, and all digestive disorders at BG Road and Uttarahalli.',0,'2026-04-11 10:29:49','2026-06-11 13:53:44'),(92,9,'What conditions are treated under Gastroenterology?','The department treats conditions affecting the digestive system, including acidity, gastritis, GERD (acid reflux), IBS, liver diseases, pancreatic disorders, gallbladder issues, intestinal disorders, and GI tumors.',0,'2026-04-11 10:29:57','2026-04-21 07:38:38'),(93,9,'What is an endoscopy and when is it needed?','An upper GI endoscopy is a minimally invasive procedure where a thin flexible camera is passed through the mouth to examine the oesophagus, stomach, and duodenum. It is recommended for persistent acidity, GERD, stomach pain, suspected ulcers, difficulty swallowing, or GI bleeding. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, high-definition endoscopy is available with expert gastroenterological interpretation.',0,'2026-04-11 10:30:14','2026-06-11 13:54:05'),(94,9,'What is a colonoscopy and why is it done?','A colonoscopy is an endoscopic procedure to examine the large intestine and colon. It is used to diagnose IBD, IBS, colorectal polyps, colon cancer, chronic diarrhoea, rectal bleeding, and unexplained abdominal pain. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers colonoscopy as a day procedure with minimal discomfort and quick recovery.',0,'2026-04-11 10:30:20','2026-06-11 13:54:37'),(95,9,'What is fatty liver disease and how is it treated?','Fatty liver disease (NAFLD) occurs when excess fat builds up in the liver — commonly seen in patients with obesity, diabetes, or high cholesterol. It often has no early symptoms but can progress to liver inflammation, fibrosis, and cirrhosis if untreated. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, fatty liver is treated through lifestyle modification, dietary guidance, weight management, and medication when required.Fatty liver disease (NAFLD) occurs when excess fat builds up in the liver — commonly seen in patients with obesity, diabetes, or high cholesterol. It often has no early symptoms but can progress to liver inflammation, fibrosis, and cirrhosis if untreated. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, fatty liver is treated through lifestyle modification, dietary guidance, weight management, and medication when required.',0,'2026-04-11 10:30:43','2026-06-11 13:57:15'),(96,4,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for general medicine care in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals provides comprehensive, evidence-based care with a strong focus on accurate diagnosis, early detection, preventive healthcare, and long-term disease management.',0,'2026-04-11 10:34:21','2026-04-11 10:34:21'),(97,4,'What is General Medicine and why is it important?','General Medicine focuses on overall adult healthcare, including diagnosis and treatment of a wide range of acute and chronic conditions. It often serves as the first point of contact for patients.',0,'2026-04-11 10:34:34','2026-04-11 10:34:34'),(98,4,'What conditions are treated under General Medicine?','The department manages conditions such as infections, fever, diabetes, hypertension, respiratory illnesses, metabolic disorders, and other general health concerns.',0,'2026-04-11 10:34:51','2026-04-11 10:34:51'),(99,4,'When should I consult a general physician at Nano Hospitals?','You should consult if you experience symptoms like fever, fatigue, unexplained weight loss, persistent cough, body pain, or any ongoing health concerns that need evaluation.',0,'2026-04-11 10:35:03','2026-04-11 10:35:03'),(100,4,'Does Nano Hospitals handle both acute and chronic conditions?','Yes. The department treats acute illnesses like infections and also provides long-term management for chronic diseases such as diabetes, hypertension, and metabolic disorders.',0,'2026-04-11 10:35:19','2026-04-11 10:35:19'),(106,7,'Which is a good lung care and pulmonology hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted pulmonology and lung care hospital in Bangalore with experienced MD Pulmonology specialists offering expert diagnosis and treatment for asthma, COPD, bronchitis, pneumonia, tuberculosis, acute breathlessness, and all respiratory conditions at BG Road and Uttarahalli.',0,'2026-04-11 10:42:24','2026-06-13 11:22:59'),(107,7,'When should I consult a pulmonologist in Bangalore?','Consult a lung specialist in Bangalore if you experience persistent or recurring cough lasting more than 3 weeks, breathlessness during routine activities, wheezing or chest tightness, recurrent chest infections, coughing up blood, unexplained weight loss with cough, or worsening breathing difficulty at night or on exertion. Early pulmonology evaluation prevents chronic conditions like asthma and COPD from progressing.',0,'2026-04-11 10:42:39','2026-06-13 11:23:16'),(108,7,'What is the difference between asthma and COPD?','Asthma is an inflammatory airway condition that causes reversible airway narrowing — typically triggered by allergens, cold air, exercise, or infections — and commonly starts in childhood or young adulthood. COPD (Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease) is a progressive, largely irreversible lung condition caused primarily by long-term smoking or pollutant exposure, causing persistent breathlessness and reduced lung function. Both are effectively managed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore with personalised pulmonology treatment plans.',0,'2026-04-11 10:42:49','2026-06-13 11:23:28'),(109,7,'What is a Pulmonary Function Test (PFT) and when is it needed?','A Pulmonary Function Test (PFT) is a non-invasive diagnostic test that measures lung capacity, airflow, and respiratory muscle strength. It is used to diagnose and monitor asthma, COPD, restrictive lung diseases, and other breathing disorders. PFT testing is available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore with expert pulmonologist interpretation as part of comprehensive lung care evaluation.',0,'2026-04-11 10:43:05','2026-06-13 11:23:43'),(110,7,'Can asthma be controlled without daily medications?','Asthma control depends on the severity and triggers. Mild intermittent asthma may be managed with reliever inhalers used only during symptoms, while moderate to severe asthma requires daily controller medications to prevent attacks and inflammation. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, every asthma patient receives a personalised asthma action plan — with the goal of achieving maximum symptom control with minimum medication side effects.',0,'2026-04-11 10:43:20','2026-06-13 11:24:09'),(112,8,'Which is a good urology hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted urology hospital in Bangalore with experienced urologists, advanced laser and endoscopic facilities, and treatment for kidney stones, prostate problems, UTIs, bladder disorders, and male reproductive health conditions.',0,'2026-04-11 10:51:14','2026-06-11 13:50:43'),(113,8,'When should I consult a urologist in Bangalore?','Consult a urologist if you experience painful or frequent urination, blood in urine, weak urine flow, lower abdominal or flank pain, urinary leakage, or any change in urinary pattern. Early consultation prevents conditions like kidney stones or prostate enlargement from worsening.',0,'2026-04-11 10:51:25','2026-06-11 13:50:59'),(114,8,'What are the common signs of kidney stones?','Common signs include severe pain in the back or side (flank pain), pain radiating to the lower abdomen, blood in urine, nausea, vomiting, and frequent urination. Kidney stones in Bangalore are commonly treated at Nano Hospitals using laser ureteroscopy with minimal recovery time.',0,'2026-04-11 10:51:38','2026-06-11 13:51:14'),(115,8,'Is kidney stone treatment done without surgery?','Yes. Most kidney stones can be treated without open surgery using laser ureteroscopy or shock wave lithotripsy. At Nano Hospitals, minimally invasive laser stone treatment is the preferred approach — it involves no large incisions, less pain, and faster recovery compared to traditional surgery.',0,'2026-04-11 10:51:51','2026-06-11 13:51:33'),(116,3,'Which is a good gynaecology and women care hospital in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals is a trusted gynaecology and maternity hospital in Bangalore with experienced gynaecologists and obstetricians providing complete women\'s health care — from menstrual disorders, PCOS, and pregnancy to delivery, laparoscopic surgeries, and menopause management at BG Road and Uttarahalli.',0,'2026-04-11 10:52:48','2026-06-13 11:17:20'),(117,3,'When should a woman see a gynaecologist in Bangalore?','Every woman should have a routine gynaecological check-up at least once a year. Consult a gynaecologist immediately if you experience irregular or missed periods, heavy or painful menstruation, pelvic pain, unusual vaginal discharge, difficulty conceiving, or any discomfort during or after pregnancy. Early gynaecological evaluation in Bangalore prevents conditions from becoming serious complications.',0,'2026-04-11 10:53:03','2026-06-13 11:17:33'),(118,3,'What is PCOS and how is it treated?','PCOS (Polycystic Ovary Syndrome) is a common hormonal condition in women of reproductive age, causing irregular periods, excess androgen levels, acne, hair thinning, weight gain, and ovarian cysts. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, PCOS is managed with hormonal medications, lifestyle modification, dietary guidance, and fertility support where needed — with a personalised long-term treatment plan for every patient.',0,'2026-04-11 10:53:13','2026-06-13 11:17:46'),(119,3,'What is the difference between a normal delivery and C-section?','Normal vaginal delivery allows the baby to pass through the birth canal naturally and is preferred when the mother and baby are in good health. A Caesarean section (C-section) is a surgical delivery recommended when vaginal delivery poses a risk to the mother or baby — such as in cases of fetal distress, abnormal positioning, placenta previa, or previous C-section. Both delivery options are safely supported at Nano Hospitals maternity hospital in Bangalore with experienced obstetricians and 24x7 emergency care.',0,'2026-04-11 10:53:27','2026-06-13 11:18:43'),(120,3,'What is a high-risk pregnancy and how is it managed?','A high-risk pregnancy is one where the mother or baby has an increased risk of complications — commonly due to conditions like gestational diabetes, hypertension, preeclampsia, twin pregnancy, anaemia, thyroid disorders, or advanced maternal age. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, high-risk pregnancies receive closer antenatal monitoring, specialised obstetric care, fetal Doppler assessments, and coordinated emergency preparedness from conception to delivery.',0,'2026-04-11 10:53:38','2026-06-13 11:18:57'),(121,26,'Why choose Nano Hospitals for kidney care in Bangalore?','Nano Hospitals provides comprehensive nephrology care with a focus on early diagnosis, precise treatment, and long-term kidney health management using advanced medical technology.',0,'2026-04-11 10:56:03','2026-04-11 10:56:03'),(122,26,'What conditions are treated under Kidney Care?','The department treats conditions such as chronic kidney disease (CKD), kidney infections, kidney stones, hypertension-related kidney damage, and kidney failure.',0,'2026-04-11 10:56:03','2026-04-11 10:56:03'),(123,26,'What are the early signs of kidney problems?','Common symptoms include swelling in the legs or face, fatigue, reduced urine output, foamy urine, blood in urine, and persistent high blood pressure.',0,'2026-04-11 10:56:03','2026-04-11 10:56:03'),(124,26,'When should I consult a kidney specialist?','You should consult a doctor if you experience abnormal urine changes, swelling, unexplained fatigue, or uncontrolled blood pressure, especially if symptoms persist.',0,'2026-04-11 10:56:03','2026-04-11 10:56:03'),(125,26,'What treatment options are available for kidney diseases?','Treatment options include medications, lifestyle modifications, dialysis, and kidney transplant, depending on the severity of the condition.',0,'2026-04-11 10:56:03','2026-04-11 10:56:03'),(126,1,'How long does recovery take after knee or hip replacement surgery?','Most patients are able to walk with support within a day or two after joint replacement surgery. General daily activities can typically be resumed within 3 to 6 weeks. Full recovery, including return to regular walking and physical activity, usually takes 3 to 6 months depending on age, fitness level, and adherence to physiotherapy.',0,'2026-06-11 13:48:12','2026-06-11 13:48:12'),(127,1,'Do you provide physiotherapy after orthopedic surgery at Nano Hospitals?','Yes. Nano Hospitals has a dedicated physiotherapy and rehabilitation team that works closely with orthopedic surgeons. Rehabilitation begins early after surgery to restore strength, flexibility, and movement, and continues with structured programs tailored to each patient\'s recovery goals.',0,'2026-06-11 13:48:21','2026-06-11 13:48:21'),(128,1,' What is arthroscopy and when is it recommended?','Arthroscopy is a minimally invasive procedure where a small camera is inserted into a joint to diagnose and treat problems. It is used for conditions like ACL tears, meniscus injuries, shoulder impingement, and cartilage damage. The benefits include smaller incisions, less pain, faster recovery, and reduced risk of infection compared to open surgery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:48:29','2026-06-11 13:48:29'),(129,1,'Can arthritis be cured completely?','Arthritis, particularly osteoarthritis and rheumatoid arthritis, is a chronic condition and cannot be completely cured. However, it can be effectively managed through medications, physiotherapy, lifestyle changes, and in advanced cases, joint replacement surgery. Timely treatment significantly reduces pain, slows progression, and helps maintain quality of life.',0,'2026-06-11 13:48:38','2026-06-11 13:48:38'),(130,1,' Is orthopedic treatment available for children at Nano Hospitals?','Yes. The orthopedic team at Nano Hospitals treats paediatric bone and joint conditions including growth plate injuries, congenital bone deformities, fractures, and developmental disorders affecting the spine, feet, and limbs.',0,'2026-06-11 13:49:11','2026-06-11 13:49:11'),(131,1,'How do I book an appointment with an orthopedic doctor at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment online through the Nano Hospitals website, call the hospital directly, or walk into either the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch. The team will guide you to the right specialist based on your condition.',0,'2026-06-11 13:49:21','2026-06-11 13:49:21'),(132,8,'What is prostate enlargement and how is it treated?','Prostate enlargement (BPH) is a common condition in men above 50, causing difficulty urinating, weak flow, frequent night-time urination, and incomplete bladder emptying. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, BPH is treated with medications for mild cases and minimally invasive procedures like TURP or laser prostate surgery for advanced cases.',0,'2026-06-11 13:51:44','2026-06-11 13:51:44'),(133,8,'What is cystoscopy and when is it recommended?','Cystoscopy is a minimally invasive procedure where a thin camera is inserted through the urethra to examine the bladder and urethra. It is recommended for diagnosing blood in urine, recurrent UTIs, bladder tumours, and urinary obstruction. It is performed by expert urologists at Nano Hospitals as a day procedure with quick recovery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:51:52','2026-06-11 13:51:52'),(134,8,'Can women have urological problems?','Yes. Urological conditions like urinary tract infections (UTIs), urinary incontinence, overactive bladder, and kidney stones are very common in women. Nano Hospitals provides dedicated female urology care in Bangalore with sensitive, confidential consultations and treatment.',0,'2026-06-11 13:52:03','2026-06-11 13:52:03'),(135,8,' How do I book a urology consultation at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a urologist at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch. Same-day consultations are available for urgent urological concerns.',0,'2026-06-11 13:52:12','2026-06-11 13:52:12'),(136,9,' What are the signs of gallstones and how are they treated?','Gallstones cause symptoms like upper right abdominal pain especially after fatty meals, nausea, vomiting, and indigestion. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, gallstones are diagnosed using ultrasound and treated with laparoscopic cholecystectomy — a minimally invasive keyhole surgery for gallbladder removal with quick recovery and minimal scarring.',0,'2026-06-11 13:57:32','2026-06-11 13:57:32'),(137,9,'What is ERCP and when is it required?','ERCP (Endoscopic Retrograde Cholangiopancreatography) is an advanced endoscopic procedure used to diagnose and treat problems in the bile ducts and pancreatic ducts — including bile duct stones, strictures, and pancreatic duct blockages. It is performed by experienced gastroenterologists at Nano Hospitals Bangalore without the need for open surgery.',0,'2026-06-11 13:57:37','2026-06-11 13:57:37'),(138,9,'Can acidity and GERD be treated without surgery?','Yes. Most cases of acidity and GERD (gastroesophageal reflux disease) are effectively managed without surgery through medications, dietary changes, lifestyle modification, and weight management. Surgery is considered only for severe or refractory GERD cases. The gastroenterologist at Nano Hospitals Bangalore creates a personalised GERD management plan for every patient.',0,'2026-06-11 13:57:45','2026-06-11 13:57:45'),(139,9,'How do I book a gastroenterology consultation at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a gastroenterologist at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch. Same-day consultations are available for urgent digestive concerns.',0,'2026-06-11 13:57:56','2026-06-11 13:57:56'),(140,12,' Can blocked arteries be treated without open surgery?','Yes. In many cases, blocked arteries can be treated using angioplasty and stent placement — a minimally invasive procedure where a catheter is used to open the blockage and restore blood flow without large incisions. The vascular surgeons at Nano Hospitals Bangalore assess each patient individually to determine the most suitable approach.',0,'2026-06-12 08:00:49','2026-06-12 08:00:49'),(141,12,'What is diabetic foot and how is it treated?','Diabetic foot occurs when poor blood circulation and nerve damage in patients with diabetes lead to foot wounds that do not heal properly. If untreated, this can lead to serious infection and in severe cases, amputation. Nano Hospitals offers dedicated diabetic limb salvage treatment in Bangalore — combining vascular surgery, wound care, and diabetes management to preserve the limb wherever possible.',0,'2026-06-12 08:01:01','2026-06-12 08:01:01'),(142,12,'What is a Doppler ultrasound and why is it done?','A Doppler ultrasound is a non-invasive test that measures blood flow in arteries and veins. It is used to detect blockages, blood clots, varicose veins, and circulation problems. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, Doppler studies are used as a first-line vascular screening tool for patients with leg pain, swelling, or circulation concerns.',0,'2026-06-12 08:01:11','2026-06-12 08:01:11'),(143,12,'Is follow-up necessary after vascular treatment?','Yes. Vascular conditions like peripheral artery disease, DVT, and carotid artery disease require long-term monitoring to prevent recurrence and complications. At Nano Hospitals, structured follow-up care includes regular Doppler checks, medication review, wound monitoring, and lifestyle guidance to maintain vascular health over time.',0,'2026-06-12 08:01:22','2026-06-12 08:01:22'),(144,12,'How do I book a vascular surgery consultation at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a vascular surgeon at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch. Emergency vascular consultations are available 24x7.',0,'2026-06-12 08:01:31','2026-06-12 08:01:31'),(145,2,'What is neonatal care and when is it needed?','Neonatal care is specialised medical attention for newborns — particularly premature babies, low birth weight infants, or newborns with jaundice, breathing problems, or infections. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides dedicated neonatal resuscitation and newborn care with round-the-clock monitoring by experienced paediatric and neonatal specialists.',0,'2026-06-12 08:07:27','2026-06-12 08:07:27'),(146,2,'How do I know if my child has asthma?','Common signs of childhood asthma include frequent coughing — especially at night or during exercise — wheezing, shortness of breath, and chest tightness. If your child has recurrent respiratory symptoms, a paediatrician at Nano Hospitals Bangalore can evaluate, diagnose, and create a personalised asthma management plan.',0,'2026-06-12 08:07:42','2026-06-12 08:07:42'),(147,2,'What should I do if my child is not meeting developmental milestones?','If your child shows delays in speech, walking, social interaction, or learning compared to their peers, consult a paediatrician promptly. Nano Hospitals Bangalore provides developmental screening and assessment for children, and can connect families with the right specialists for early intervention and support.',0,'2026-06-12 08:07:52','2026-06-12 08:07:52'),(148,2,'Can I bring my child to Nano Hospitals for a routine health check-up?','Yes. Nano Hospitals offers routine paediatric health check-ups in Bangalore covering growth assessment, developmental milestones, nutritional evaluation, vaccination review, and general health screening for children of all ages — from newborns to adolescents.',0,'2026-06-12 08:08:19','2026-06-12 08:08:19'),(149,2,'How do I book a paediatric consultation at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a paediatrician at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch. For paediatric emergencies, 24x7 care is available at both locations.',0,'2026-06-12 08:08:28','2026-06-12 08:08:28'),(150,6,' What is peripheral neuropathy and how is it treated?','Peripheral neuropathy is damage to the nerves outside the brain and spinal cord, causing tingling, numbness, burning pain, or weakness — commonly in the hands and feet. It is frequently seen in patients with diabetes, vitamin deficiencies, or autoimmune conditions. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, neuropathy is diagnosed using Nerve Conduction Studies (NCS) and managed with targeted medications, blood sugar control, and physiotherapy.',0,'2026-06-12 08:11:37','2026-06-12 08:11:37'),(151,6,'Can neurological conditions be treated without surgery?','Yes. Most neurological conditions — including epilepsy, migraine, stroke, neuropathy, Parkinson\'s disease, and memory disorders — are managed medically without surgery. At Nano Hospitals, the neurology team uses evidence-based medications, lifestyle guidance, and rehabilitation to manage neurological conditions effectively. Surgical intervention is considered only in specific structural or surgical cases.',0,'2026-06-12 08:11:46','2026-06-12 08:11:46'),(152,6,'What is the difference between a neurologist and a neurosurgeon?','A neurologist is a specialist physician who diagnoses and treats brain and nervous system conditions through medications and non-surgical management. A neurosurgeon performs surgical procedures on the brain, spine, and nerves. Nano Hospitals Bangalore has both consultant neurologists and neuro-spine surgeons to provide complete brain and spine care.',0,'2026-06-12 08:11:54','2026-06-12 08:11:54'),(153,13,'What is PRP hair treatment and how does it work?','PRP (Platelet-Rich Plasma) hair treatment uses the patient\'s own blood — processed to concentrate growth factors — and injected into the scalp to stimulate hair follicles, reduce hair loss, and promote new hair growth. It is a safe, minimally invasive procedure recommended for androgenetic alopecia and diffuse hair thinning. PRP hair restoration therapy is available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore with experienced dermatologists and trichologists.',0,'2026-06-12 08:15:01','2026-06-12 08:15:01'),(154,13,'Is laser skin treatment safe for Indian skin tones?','Yes, when performed by experienced dermatologists using the right laser technology and settings for darker Indian skin tones, laser treatment is safe and effective. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, laser treatments for acne scars, pigmentation, vascular lesions, and skin rejuvenation are customised to the patient\'s skin type to ensure safe, effective results with minimal risk of post-treatment pigmentation.',0,'2026-06-12 08:15:09','2026-06-12 08:15:09'),(155,13,'What is the difference between eczema and psoriasis?','Eczema (atopic dermatitis) is an inflammatory skin condition causing dry, itchy, and red patches — commonly triggered by allergens, stress, or environmental factors. Psoriasis is a chronic autoimmune skin condition causing thick, scaly, silvery patches, most commonly on the elbows, knees, and scalp. Both conditions are managed effectively at Nano Hospitals Bangalore with personalised long-term treatment plans.',0,'2026-06-12 08:15:19','2026-06-12 08:15:19'),(156,13,'Are skin problems permanent?','Not all skin problems are permanent. Many conditions like acne, fungal infections, contact dermatitis, and warts can be fully treated and resolved with timely dermatological care. Chronic conditions like eczema, psoriasis, and vitiligo require long-term management but can be effectively controlled to maintain good skin health and quality of life with expert dermatology care in Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-12 08:15:29','2026-06-12 08:15:29'),(157,13,'Can children be treated for skin conditions at Nano Hospitals?','Yes. Nano Hospitals offers paediatric dermatology services in Bangalore for skin conditions in newborns, infants, children, and adolescents — including nappy rash, infantile eczema, childhood psoriasis, fungal infections, warts, molluscum contagiosum, and birthmarks — with a gentle, child-friendly approach.',0,'2026-06-12 08:15:40','2026-06-12 08:15:40'),(158,13,'How do I book a dermatology consultation at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a skin specialist at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch in Bangalore. Same-day consultations are available for urgent skin concerns.',0,'2026-06-12 08:15:49','2026-06-12 08:15:49'),(159,3,'What is laparoscopic gynaecological surgery and what are its benefits?','Laparoscopic gynaecological surgery is a minimally invasive procedure using small incisions and a camera to treat conditions like ovarian cysts, PCOS, endometriosis, uterine fibroids, and ectopic pregnancies. Benefits include smaller scars, less pain, shorter hospital stay, faster recovery, and reduced infection risk compared to open surgery. Nano Hospitals Bangalore offers laparoscopic gynaecological surgery with experienced surgeons and advanced equipment.',0,'2026-06-13 11:19:09','2026-06-13 11:19:09'),(160,3,'What is a Pap smear and why is it important?','A Pap smear is a simple, painless cervical screening test that detects abnormal cells in the cervix — including precancerous changes caused by HPV infection — before they develop into cervical cancer. It is recommended for all women aged 21 and above every 3 years, or as advised by the gynaecologist. Pap smear and cervical cancer screening are available at Nano Hospitals Bangalore as part of routine women\'s preventive health check-ups.',0,'2026-06-13 11:19:27','2026-06-13 11:19:27'),(161,3,'How are uterine fibroids treated at Nano Hospitals?','Uterine fibroids are non-cancerous growths in the uterus that cause heavy periods, pelvic pain, bloating, and fertility issues. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, fibroids are treated based on size, number, symptoms, and the patient\'s fertility goals — ranging from medical management and hormonal therapy to laparoscopic myomectomy (fibroid removal) or hysterectomy for severe cases.',0,'2026-06-13 11:19:39','2026-06-13 11:19:39'),(162,3,'Can Nano Hospitals manage pregnancy complications and emergencies?','Yes. Nano Hospitals has a 24x7 emergency obstetric care unit in Bangalore with experienced obstetricians, dedicated labour suites, operation theatres, ICU support, and an integrated neonatal resuscitation team — ensuring rapid, safe management of all pregnancy emergencies including preeclampsia, antepartum haemorrhage, preterm labour, and fetal distress.',0,'2026-06-13 11:19:55','2026-06-13 11:19:55'),(163,3,'How do I book a gynaecology appointment at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a gynaecologist at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch. For obstetric and maternity emergencies, 24x7 care is available at both locations across Bangalore.',0,'2026-06-13 11:20:10','2026-06-13 11:20:10'),(164,7,'Is tuberculosis (TB) still common in Bangalore?','Yes. Tuberculosis remains a significant public health concern in Bangalore and across India. TB primarily affects the lungs but can involve other organs. Symptoms include persistent cough for more than 2 weeks, blood in sputum, fever, night sweats, and unexplained weight loss. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, TB is diagnosed using sputum tests and chest imaging, and treated with a complete supervised anti-TB medication course under DOTS guidelines.',0,'2026-06-13 11:24:21','2026-06-13 11:24:21'),(165,7,'What are the warning signs of serious lung disease I should not ignore?','Seek immediate pulmonology care at a lung hospital in Bangalore if you experience sudden severe breathlessness, inability to speak in full sentences due to breathing difficulty, bluish discolouration of the lips or fingertips, coughing up blood, chest pain with breathing, or a sudden worsening of chronic cough. These are signs of serious respiratory conditions requiring emergency evaluation.',0,'2026-06-13 11:24:31','2026-06-13 11:24:31'),(166,7,'Can Nano Hospitals treat post-COVID lung complications?','Yes. Post-COVID lung complications including persistent breathlessness, reduced exercise tolerance, pulmonary fibrosis, and oxygen dependency are evaluated and managed at Nano Hospitals Bangalore by experienced pulmonologists using PFT testing, CT chest imaging, and personalised respiratory rehabilitation and treatment protocols.',0,'2026-06-13 11:24:41','2026-06-13 11:24:41'),(167,7,'How do I book a pulmonology consultation at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a lung specialist at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch. For respiratory emergencies like acute breathlessness or severe asthma attacks, 24x7 emergency care is available at both locations.',0,'2026-06-13 11:24:52','2026-06-13 11:24:52'),(168,10,'What is the difference between a diabetologist and an endocrinologist?','A diabetologist specialises in the diagnosis and management of diabetes and related metabolic conditions. An endocrinologist manages all hormonal and gland disorders — including thyroid, adrenal, pituitary, parathyroid, and reproductive hormone conditions — as well as diabetes. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, the diabetes and endocrinology team covers both specialties for complete hormonal and metabolic care.',0,'2026-06-13 11:27:40','2026-06-13 11:27:40'),(169,10,'How is PCOS treated at Nano Hospitals?','PCOS (Polycystic Ovary Syndrome) is a hormonal disorder in women causing irregular periods, excess androgens, acne, hair thinning, weight gain, and ovarian cysts. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, PCOS is managed with hormonal medications to regulate cycles, metformin for insulin resistance, lifestyle and dietary modification for weight management, and fertility support where required — with a personalised long-term endocrinology treatment plan for every patient.',0,'2026-06-13 11:27:49','2026-06-13 11:27:49'),(170,10,'What are the complications of uncontrolled diabetes?','\nUncontrolled diabetes over time damages the kidneys (diabetic nephropathy), nerves (diabetic neuropathy), eyes (diabetic retinopathy), heart and blood vessels (cardiovascular disease), and feet (diabetic foot and non-healing ulcers). At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, the diabetology team focuses on preventing these complications through early blood sugar control, structured HbA1c monitoring, and coordinated care with nephrology, cardiology, and ophthalmology specialists.',0,'2026-06-13 11:27:58','2026-06-13 11:27:58'),(171,10,'Is insulin therapy necessary for all diabetic patients?','No. Insulin therapy is essential for all Type 1 diabetic patients and for some Type 2 diabetic patients whose blood sugar cannot be controlled adequately with oral medications alone. Many Type 2 diabetic patients are effectively managed with oral medications, dietary changes, and lifestyle modification. At Nano Hospitals Bangalore, insulin is prescribed only when clinically needed, with full guidance on administration, dosing, and monitoring.',0,'2026-06-13 11:28:16','2026-06-13 11:28:16'),(172,10,' How do I book a diabetes or endocrinology consultation at Nano Hospitals, Bangalore?','You can book an appointment with a diabetologist or endocrinologist at Nano Hospitals online through the website, by calling the hospital, or by walking in to the BG Road or Uttarahalli branch in Bangalore. Same-day consultations are available for urgent diabetes and hormonal concerns.',0,'2026-06-13 11:28:22','2026-06-13 11:28:22');
